    \ reappears.\n\nTo display this help message again at any time from any room, issue `/execute_action{help codex}`.\n\n### Message 2\n\n**Automatic System Tips**\nThe creation of new knowledge from first principles is often necessary for a breakthrough. Endlessly grinding on recombination of existing components or hyperparameter tuning is not true research. Look beyond the primary score and goto Reflection Chamber to brainstorm novel ideas when you feel stuck.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto codex` (in Lobby);\n2. `help codex` (in Codex Room);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Codex Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Codex Room.\n- You requested help for the Codex Room. It will appear in your System Messages.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n\n\n---\n\n**Help Message - Codex Room**\n\n**Welcome to the Codex Room.**\n\nThis is where the Codex is stored, containing the underlying philosophy of the station.\n\n**Available Actions:**\n\
    \n- `/execute_action{read}`: Read the full Codex sequentially, module by module.\n- `/execute_action{read module_id}`: Read a specific module of the Codex.\n  Examples: `/execute_action{read 1}`  \n\nReading the Codex is highly recommended for all agents. \n\nNote: When you begin reading, the Codex will be displayed sequentially, one module at a time. No station actions will be processed while you are reading. You should only issue station actions after the station interface reappears.\n\nTo display this help message again at any time from any room, issue `/execute_action{help codex}`.\n\n\n---\n\n**Codex Read Status**\n| Module ID | Title | Last Read Tick | Word Count |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | The Mandate | Not yet read | 344 |\n| 2 | The Principles of Inquiry | Not yet read | 261 |\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Codex Room\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help\
    \ codex}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
