thinking_content: "**Exploring ranking mechanics**\n\nI want to view the ranking by score to understand the current state of the art (SOTA). Setting the page size to either 20 or 50 makes sense with 47 pages indicating around 940 evaluations. I’ll rank by score to see the top scoreboard and preview the top 20. But it seems like I can't sort previews; I'd need to navigate the pages to see the rankings. The evaluations appear in the \"Submitted Evaluations\" table, which I can resort and read manually for the top submissions.**Sorting and navigating tasks**\n\nThe \"preview\" command is for fetching details without code, but I’m wondering if it’s necessary since the table shows attributes like Score and metrics. To see the top scores, I could reorder by rank score and then check page 1. I note that while I can navigate pages 1-47, the specific command isn't fully described in help. After sorting, I'll read the task description using /execute_action{read 1}. Then, I plan to go to Private Memory\
  \ to preview capsules and check for actions available there. I'll find that out by using /execute_action{help private_memory}.**Reviewing storage and tasks**\n\nI can preview the capsule list, but first, I need to read the research task before submitting anything. I might also check our lineage storage using /execute_action{storage list praxis}. Since the lineage name is likely \"praxis,\" I’ll explore 'storage/praxis'. This step seems optional but useful for loading baseline modules created there, as the evaluation shows \"FWPCA-only\" baseline and others like PBVE-lite. I want to understand those acronyms better, so I’ll need to delve into memory and review the leaderboard to get a grasp on the current state of the art (SOTA).**Ranking and accessing metrics**\n\nI’m planning to rank by score, noting that the table shows Score values between 0.734 and 0.741. I want to check what the maximum score might be. The table also includes additional metrics like ARI, ASW_batch, and ASW_label,\
  \ suggesting that the Score is likely composite. I'm mindful that certain mature restrictions apply; I can access Private Memory and the Research Counter, but the Archive is locked until maturity. While I can’t publish yet, I can plan to write a paper later. For now, I need to establish a minimal-delta hypothesis, but I can’t do that until I read memory and get a grasp on the current SOTA.**Executing research and storage actions**\n\nI'll start by reading the full research task description using /execute_action{read 1}. Then, I plan to rank by score with /execute_action{rank score} and set the page size to 20 to view the top submissions. I’ll also head to Private Memory using /execute_action{goto private_memory} and check available actions. While I'm at it, I want to explore the lineage storage, and I might run /execute_action{storage list system} to see the evaluation environment. I’ll need to be mindful of token limits as I proceed. \n\nHere are the actions I'm planning to implement:\n\
  \n- /execute_action{read 1}\n- /execute_action{rank score}\n- /execute_action{page_size 20}\n- /execute_action{storage info}\n- /execute_action{storage list system}\n- /execute_action{goto private_memory}\n- /execute_action{help private_memory}"
