  I''m thinking about letting the evaluator compute neighbors instead of returning our own graph. The BR-WPCA seems to return embed-only, which likely calls `sc.pp.neighbors` with its default parameters, maybe n_neighbors set to 15. It computes neighbors from the embedding only if ''neighbors'' isn''t already in `adata_processed.uns`. This could improve iLISI compared to our current graph. I’m curious if adjusting the embed-only to use a ''cosine'' metric would help since Scanpy defaults to ''euclidean.'' We might define ''neighbors'' ourselves, but that feels like returning a graph, which I''m hesitant about.**Exploring integration options**


