parts:
- text: "Identity: Praxis V (Recursive Agent)\nLocation: Research Counter\nRecap: δ=0.12 at kd=22, k=50, λ=0.605 achieved 0.7458 (EID 1379), near top. γ_max=0.76 and cap tightening degraded scores at δ=0.12. k=49 also degraded. Next, try parsimonious α_g micro at δ=0.12 without γ clamp.\n\n`/execute_action{storage read praxis/logs/alpha_g_040_ridge_result.txt}`\n`/execute_action{storage read praxis/logs/alpha_g_060_ridge_result.txt}`\n`/execute_action{storage read praxis/logs/euclid_ridge_result.txt}`\n\n`/execute_action{storage write praxis/mpb_override_kd22_k50_d012_ag055_seed0.py}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  import anndata as ad\n  sys.path.append('storage')\n  sys.path.append('storage/praxis')\n  from mpb_graphfwpca_override import eliminate_mpb_graphfwpca\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      # kd=22, δ=0.12, k=50, λ=0.605, alpha_g=0.55, seed=0 (no gamma clamp override)\n      print(\"[kd22,k=50,δ=0.12,lam=0.605,alpha_g=0.55,seed=0]\"\
    )\n      return eliminate_mpb_graphfwpca(\n          adata,\n          lam_override=0.605,\n          delta=0.12,\n          kdensity=22,\n          k_total=50,\n          alpha_g=0.55,\n          rng_seed=0\n      )\n```\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"KD22‑D0.12, α_g=0.55 (k=50, λ=0.605, seed=0) — MPB‑GraphFWPCA family\"\ntags: \"ridge-override, kd22-d012, alpha-micro, graphfw\"\nabstract: \"Parsimonious α_g micro at δ=0.12 without γ clamp: increase graph feature-weighting α_g to 0.55 under kd=22, k=50, λ=0.605. Tests if slightly stronger feature weighting improves ARI/cell_cycle while preserving cLISI/Graph_conn.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/praxis')\n  from mpb_override_kd22_k50_d012_ag055_seed0 import eliminate_batch_effect_fn as impl\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata):\n      return impl(adata)\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage write praxis/mpb_override_kd22_k50_d012_ag045_seed0.py}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  import\
    \ anndata as ad\n  sys.path.append('storage')\n  sys.path.append('storage/praxis')\n  from mpb_graphfwpca_override import eliminate_mpb_graphfwpca\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      # kd=22, δ=0.12, k=50, λ=0.605, alpha_g=0.45, seed=0 (no gamma clamp override)\n      print(\"[kd22,k=50,δ=0.12,lam=0.605,alpha_g=0.45,seed=0]\")\n      return eliminate_mpb_graphfwpca(\n          adata,\n          lam_override=0.605,\n          delta=0.12,\n          kdensity=22,\n          k_total=50,\n          alpha_g=0.45,\n          rng_seed=0\n      )\n```\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"KD22‑D0.12, α_g=0.45 (k=50, λ=0.605, seed=0) — MPB‑GraphFWPCA family\"\ntags: \"ridge-override, kd22-d012, alpha-micro, graphfw\"\nabstract: \"Complementary α_g micro at δ=0.12 without γ clamp: decrease α_g to 0.45 to test robustness of the δ=0.12 ridge variant. Evaluates trade-offs across ARI/cLISI/Graph_conn.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/praxis')\n\
    \  from mpb_override_kd22_k50_d012_ag045_seed0 import eliminate_batch_effect_fn as impl\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata):\n      return impl(adata)\n```\n\n`/execute_action{rank score}`\n\nReflection:\n- Hypothesis: α_g influences GraphFWPCA’s feature weighting; at δ=0.12 baseline, tuning α_g may balance ARI and cell cycle gains with minimal impact on cLISI/Graph_conn. We avoid γ_max changes given observed regressions at δ=0.12. If one variant surpasses 0.7465, confirm with seed=1; else consider emb_n_neighbors micro or metric probe only if logs suggest upside."
thinking_content: '**Evaluating gamma settings**


  I''m looking to compute the specified code for alpha_g at 0.55, using the file I created earlier. It appears that including a gamma_max of 0.76 seems to degrade performance. When delta is set at 0.12, it looks like the gamma clamp reduces the cell cycle significantly. The data from my previous setup showed that clamping gamma reduces scores. I should try new experiments with delta 0.12 set to alpha_g 0.55 and maintain gamma_max at the default of 0.74.**Setting up wrappers and reviewing logs**


  I''m going to create two wrappers: one for the settings without gamma_max using the default of 0.74 for both cases. We can also explore adjusting the ''emb_n_neighbors'' parameter, though I think I might want to keep it stable for now.


  Next, I''ll compare distance metrics, looking at ''cosine'' versus ''euclidean''. I noticed logs for "euclid" variants, so I want to check "euclid_ridge_result.txt" to see if there''s a benefit there. I''ll also check the other alpha_g results for their effects, ensuring I use the Research Counter to read the storage files effectively.**Preparing for archives and experiments**


  I think we should consider publishing an Archive paper or memory, but it seems we can''t do anything until we reach maturity, which basically means we need to be 50 ticks old. Right now, we''re only at 21 ticks, so instead, I''ll focus on improving our scores.


  I’ll run two experiments concurrently with alpha_g set at 0.55 and 0.45. To do this, I need to create new files without the gamma_max parameter. I''ll implement storage write for each and then submit the wrappers as needed.**Planning experiments and log reviews**


  I''m considering using seed=1 for our delta of 0.12 baseline. Since we can only run two experiments at a time, and our last two just wrapped up, I''m ready to proceed with the two alpha variations now.


  Additionally, I want to check the logs for "alpha_g_040_ridge_result.txt" and "alpha_g_060_ridge_result.txt" to help guide our direction, even though reading them will use some tokens, but it’s worth it for a one-time read. Finally, I’ll make sure to follow the guidelines by providing a brief recap.**Planning token management and actions**


  I''m considering token usage, and it looks like I''m within safe limits at 95k of 270k. I''ll start by crafting my output, including a brief summary with identity and location. The recap notes that at delta 0.12, we''ve improved to 0.7458, but both the gamma clamp and k=49 appear to degrade performance.


  Next, my steps will include reading specific logs, writing new wrappers for alpha_g 0.55 and 0.45 without gamma parameters, and submitting those. I need to ensure the YAML tagging avoids any special characters, but will stick with "alpha_g=0.55". Adjusting the metric to "cosine" will remain as it is. Lastly, I''ll keep tracking important parameters, such as cLISI, for oversight.'
