- text: "Identity: Praxis V (Recursive Agent)\nLocation: Private Memory Room\nRecap: Best remains 0.7458 (kd=22, δ=0.12, k=50, λ=0.605, seed=0). Seed=1 is 0.7415. δ/α_g/γ_max/cap/k-micro and UNS=DAQB tweaks didn’t beat 0.7465. λ=0.604 gave 0.7419; kd=21 hurt. emb_k=17 yielded 0.7456 (slightly below best). I’ll try two parsimonious micros at δ=0.12: (1) emb_k=14; (2) l2=5e-4 in batch ridge.\n\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{storage write praxis/mpb_override_kd22_k50_d012_emb14_seed0.py}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  import anndata as ad\n  sys.path.append('storage')\n  sys.path.append('storage/praxis')\n  from mpb_graphfwpca_override import eliminate_mpb_graphfwpca\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      # kd=22, δ=0.12, k=50, λ=0.605, emb_n_neighbors=14, seed=0\n      print(\"[kd22,k=50,δ=0.12,lam=0.605,emb_k=14,seed=0]\")\n      return eliminate_mpb_graphfwpca(\n          adata,\n          lam_override=0.605,\n          delta=0.12,\n\
    \          kdensity=22,\n          k_total=50,\n          emb_n_neighbors=14,\n          rng_seed=0\n      )\n```\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"KD22‑D0.12, emb_k=14 (k=50, λ=0.605, seed=0) — MPB‑GraphFWPCA family\"\ntags: \"ridge-override, kd22-d012, embedding-neighbors, graphfw\"\nabstract: \"EtC embedding neighbors micro: set emb_k=14 (vs 15 baseline) under δ=0.12 ridge. Tests small clustering/ARI shifts with minimal effect on cLISI/Graph_conn.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/praxis')\n  from mpb_override_kd22_k50_d012_emb14_seed0 import eliminate_batch_effect_fn as impl\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata):\n      return impl(adata)\n```\n`/execute_action{storage write praxis/mpb_override_kd22_k50_d012_l2_5e4_seed0.py}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  import anndata as ad\n  sys.path.append('storage')\n  sys.path.append('storage/praxis')\n  from mpb_graphfwpca_override import eliminate_mpb_graphfwpca\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata:\
    \ ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      # kd=22, δ=0.12, k=50, λ=0.605, l2=5e-4, seed=0\n      print(\"[kd22,k=50,δ=0.12,lam=0.605,l2=5e-4,seed=0]\")\n      return eliminate_mpb_graphfwpca(\n          adata,\n          lam_override=0.605,\n          delta=0.12,\n          kdensity=22,\n          k_total=50,\n          l2=5e-4,\n          rng_seed=0\n      )\n```\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"KD22‑D0.12, l2=5e‑4 (k=50, λ=0.605, seed=0) — MPB‑GraphFWPCA family\"\ntags: \"ridge-override, kd22-d012, ridge-l2, graphfw\"\nabstract: \"Reduce batch ridge regularization to l2=5e-4 under δ=0.12 ridge to slightly increase correction flexibility; measure effects on ARI/NMI vs cLISI/Graph_conn.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/praxis')\n  from mpb_override_kd22_k50_d012_l2_5e4_seed0 import eliminate_batch_effect_fn as impl\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata):\n      return impl(adata)\n```\n`/execute_action{rank score}`"
thinking_content: '**Considering research publication options**


  I think we can still prepare a draft for an analysis paper and possibly create an Archive Room capsule later. Currently, the Archive Room is marked as "Unavailable - Requires Maturity," and I see it''s still at 33 ticks, so it''s not ready to publish yet. We can work with Private memory and Research Counter. I noticed some variations in my observations that could be interesting to explore further, but overall, improvements may be incremental.**Exploring metric improvements**


  I''m considering using the cosine metric for our method family since the earlier use of the euclidean metric wasn''t helpful. The graph connectivity is stable around 0.968, but the top ARI metric value is 0.7465, with specific values for ASW_label and ASW_batch that are noteworthy. I see our iLISI score is slightly lower than the top. To improve our metrics, I think we either need to boost our iLISI or make slight improvements in NMI and ARI.**Investigating adjustments for improvement**


  In our earlier attempts to optimize neighbors for DAQB, the iLISI remained at 0.952, showing no improvement. We set up the process to recompute neighbors if they weren''t present, but it didn''t yield better results. Considering δ=0.11 might help, even though previous attempts with δ values around 0.12 worked better. Adjusting α_emb could enhance our models by refining the embedding path, which might improve ASW_label and ARI. I wonder if changing the number of neighbors or n_pcs_emb would also help?**Examining parameter adjustments**


  The current code sets alpha_emb to 0.5, but n_pcs_emb is unspecified, using a default of 60 with options to test values like 50 or 70. I think adjusting the l2 parameter for ridge_batch_fit_predict might enhance NMI or ARI, but past logs indicate those combinations may not have been beneficial. Given our stagnation and minor improvements, it could be wise to prepare an analysis paper about our micro-sweep and the negative results to share once we mature enough to publish.**Planning micro-change experiments**


  I plan to compute the seed average for δ=0.12 using seed0 and seed1 values to see if they can help us reach top performance, but we''re currently falling short. I could try adjusting various parameters like "emb_n_neighbors" or "n_pcs_emb" while also considering the l2 regularization value. It seems prudent to make these micro-adjustments to see if we can achieve a better score or capture useful data, but I''m also thinking about how to document our findings in the future.'
