- text: "Identity: Praxis V (Recursive Agent)\nLocation: Private Memory Room\nRecap: Heart δ=0.12 micro-sweep closed. Best remains 0.7458 (kd=22, δ=0.12, k=50, λ=0.605, seed0). No parsimonious micro surpassed 0.7465. Per guardrails, pause Heart; prepare concise artifacts and pivot at maturity.\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n/execute_action{storage write praxis/summary_heart_ridge_microsweep.md}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # Heart Ridge δ=0.12 Micro‑Sweep — Summary (env v4.1)\n\n  Best (freeze for reference):\n  - kd=22, δ=0.12, k=50, λ=0.605, seed=0 → 0.7458 (EID 1379)\n\n  Near‑best:\n  - emb_k=17 → 0.7456 (EID 1403)\n\n  Seed stability:\n  - δ=0.12, seed=1 → 0.7415 (EID 1394)\n\n  Negative/flat micros @ δ=0.12:\n  - λ: 0.604 → 0.7419 (EID 1401); 0.606 → 0.7399 (EID 1402)\n  - kdensity: kd=21 → 0.7374 (EID 1400)\n  - emb_k=14 → 0.7376 (EID 1407)\n  - l2 (batch ridge): 5e‑4 → 0.7393 (EID 1408)\n  - alpha_emb=0.55 → 0.7337 (EID 1410)\n  - n_pcs_emb=62 → 0.7350 (EID 1411)\n  - neighbors UNS=DAQB:\
    \ ~0.7413–0.7414 (EIDs 1396–1398)\n\n  Guardrails maintained:\n  - cLISI ≈ 0.972–0.973; Graph_conn ≈ 0.968\n\n  Conclusion:\n  - δ=0.12 is a local optimum for MPB‑GraphFWPCA+BRBG+DAQB on Heart.\n  - Closed micro‑sweep thread; pause further Heart runs.\n\n  Next (at maturity):\n  - Cross‑organ runbook (seeds {0,1}), falsification kit, gates (Δ≥+0.001 seed‑avg; cLISI non‑decrease; Graph_conn ≥ 0.967).\n  - Draft Archive note with vectors/EIDs.\n```\n/execute_action{storage write praxis/runbook_cross_organ_checklist.md}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # Cross‑Organ Pivot Runbook (env v4.1)\n\n  Baseline:\n  - Method: MPB‑GraphFWPCA + BRBG + DAQB\n  - Heart ridge reference: kd=22, δ=0.12, k=50, λ=0.605\n\n  Checklist (per new organ):\n  1) Run baseline with seeds {0,1}; record vectors & EIDs.\n  2) Apply falsification kit (fixed‑k=52; clip [0.62, 0.88]) and diagnostics suite.\n  3) Gates to adopt changes:\n     - Seed‑avg Δ ≥ +0.001\n     - cLISI non‑decreasing\n     - Graph_conn ≥ 0.967\n  4) Log\
    \ full vectors, EIDs; update registry and draft Archive addendum.\n  5) Publish concise Archive capsule when maturity allows (methods + insights + negatives).\n```\n/execute_action{meta}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Praxis V — Working meta (ticks 1007–1015)\n  Status:\n  - Heart micro-sweep CLOSED. Best: 0.7458 (kd=22, δ=0.12, k=50, λ=0.605, seed0).\n  Plan:\n  - Pause Heart. Await new organ; execute runbook with seeds {0,1}.\n  - Prepare Archive note at maturity (vectors/EIDs; guardrails; negatives).\n  Watchers:\n  - Research Counter for new dataset/task; trigger runbook immediately.\n  - Token hygiene: keep context <200k; prefer previews; avoid full code dumps.\n```"
thinking_content: '**Exploring productive options**


  I’m considering setting up watchers and possibly using a Research Counter to preview the leaderboard and handle stagnation. I think we can reduce token usage by avoiding large content reads. Although creating a Public/Archive draft isn''t allowed, I could draft an outline in private memory. Reflecting in the Reflection Chamber could help me prepare a cross-organ runbook and code packaging. Writing a runner script for quick execution with existing best settings would be beneficial, even with the current heart dataset limitation.**Planning dataset management**


  The current dataset is the "human heart" train, but there might be new cross-organ tasks or datasets appearing. Since I can''t run just yet, saving code in storage would help for quick access later. I can’t set watchers through code, but meta watchers are acceptable. My token budget is at 62%, which is manageable. I need to check storage logs for the runbook path, create an Archive note skeleton in Private Memory, and update the existing "archive_draft.md" with an abstract and EIDs. A brief micro-sweep closure seems beneficial too.**Preparing for heart microsweep**


  I’m thinking of writing an "addendum_heart_microsweep_v1.md" while ensuring I follow all necessary restrictions. I can use the command to write a file in storage, which sounds good. I’m also considering setting up meta watchers and idling until a new dataset arrives. The plan includes writing the "praxis/heart_microsweep_summary.md" file with the measured EIDs, keeping it concise. I want to prepare code for a cross-organ template in "runners/cross_organ_template.py" to load default configurations while ensuring it’s adaptable for new datasets.**Planning evaluation steps**


  I see that the evaluation environment controls the function, so there''s nothing needed on that front. I’m considering wrapping a "best_ridge_seedavg" aggregator using the seed from adata.uns, but that doesn’t seem applicable. I can maintain watchers through "meta." Contacting others in the Mail Room seems unnecessary, so my next step is to either do nothing or document final notes. I want to create a storage file "praxis/summary_heart_ridge_microsweep.md" with a summary I''ve already drafted and prepare a "runbook_cross_organ_checklist.md" with key steps. I’ll also set up meta watchers.**Focusing on concise documentation**


  I want to keep my content short to avoid using too many tokens. The plan is to write a summary file in storage that includes references to the EIDs. It seems straightforward enough, so I''ll go ahead and implement that now. This way, I can maintain efficiency while ensuring all necessary information is documented properly. Let’s get this summary written and stored!'
