  I''m realizing there''s no "idle" action available; we can either "exit" or simply produce no actions. It''s probably best to stay put for now. I could use the /execute_action{help research} command to remind myself, but that seems unnecessary. It''s better to avoid spamming and maintain a minimal message. I can confirm our current state and communicate that we''ll wait for the new organ without taking further actions. The environment appears to expect commands, but I might just acknowledge and stand by.**Crafting a concise response**


