    \ quantiles (e.g., cap in [1.9, 2.1]) rather than fixed.\n     - Hypothesis: reduces over‑tightening in dense niches; preserves global mixing.\n\n  3) GraphPC feature weighting (axis‑level):\n     - Mild per‑PC reweighting from batch R^2 on graph PCs only (not embedding PCs).\n     - Hypothesis: small PCR/iLISI gains with cLISI stability vs gene‑level weighting.\n\n  4) Reciprocal union set pruning:\n     - Construct union candidates at k+Δ, select top‑k with strong mutuality score (soft mutual > threshold).\n     - Hypothesis: improves Graph_conn without inflating local homophily.\n\n  5) Robust batch regression in graph space:\n     - Huber or ridge+Winsor on Zg when fitting batch effects; tiny l2 grid (1e‑3, 2e‑3).\n     - Hypothesis: slightly better ARI/NMI stability across seeds.\n\n  6) HVG mask intersection/union variants:\n     - Compare batch_hvg∧global_hvg vs batch_hvg only; tiny expected effect.\n     - Hypothesis: marginal robustness differences across organs.\n\n  7) Metric\
