parts:
- text: "Identity: Praxis V (Recursive Agent)\nLocation: Private Memory Room\nRecap: Heart micro-sweep closed; best 0.7458 (kd=22, δ=0.12, k=50, λ=0.605, seed0). Artifacts and runbook pinned. Standing by for new organ; preparing an Archive capsule draft for rapid publication at maturity.\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n/execute_action{storage write praxis/archive_capsule_draft.yaml}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  title: \"Ridge δ=0.12 Micro‑Sweep on Human Heart (env v4.1): Parsimonious Stability and Negative Results\"\n  tags: \"ridge, graph, batch-integration, negative-results, reproducibility\"\n  abstract: >\n    We evaluate parsimonious micro‑changes around the adopted Heart ridge\n    for MPB‑GraphFWPCA+BRBG+DAQB. None surpassed the best 0.7458\n    (kd=22, δ=0.12, k=50, λ=0.605, seed=0). Guardrails held\n    (cLISI≈0.972–0.973; Graph_conn≈0.968). We provide full vectors/EIDs and\n    a cross‑organ runbook to encourage reproducibility and generalization.\n  content: |\n    Context\n   \
    \ - Task: scRNA‑seq batch integration (Human Heart, env v4.1; OpenProblems 2.0 metrics).\n    - Baseline topology: MPB‑GraphFWPCA + BRBG + DAQB (cosine), adopted ridge.\n\n    Key results\n    - Best: 0.7458 (kd=22, δ=0.12, k=50, λ=0.605, seed=0; EID 1379).\n    - Near‑best: emb_k=17 → 0.7456 (EID 1403).\n    - Seed stability: δ=0.12, seed=1 → 0.7415 (EID 1394).\n    - Negative/flat micros (selected): λ=0.604 → 0.7419 (EID 1401), λ=0.606 → 0.7399 (1402),\n      kd=21 → 0.7374 (1400), emb_k=14 → 0.7376 (1407), l2=5e‑4 → 0.7393 (1408),\n      alpha_emb=0.55 → 0.7337 (1410), n_pcs_emb=62 → 0.7350 (1411),\n      neighbors UNS=DAQB ~0.7413–0.7414 (1396–1398).\n\n    Guardrails\n    - cLISI non‑decreasing; Graph_conn ≥ 0.967. All runs respected guardrails.\n\n    Files (repro and references)\n    - Summary: storage/praxis/summary_heart_ridge_microsweep.md\n    - EIDs CSV: storage/praxis/eids_ridge_microsweep.csv\n    - Diagnostics/falsification kit: storage/shared/diagnostics/\n\n    Discussion\n\
    \    - Evidence suggests δ=0.12 is a local optimum for this topology on Heart.\n    - Smooth micro‑tuning around the ridge yields diminishing returns; future gains\n      likely require orthogonal adjustments or cross‑organ evaluations.\n\n    Next steps\n    - At maturity: publish full note; pivot to new organ via runbook (seeds {0,1}),\n      apply falsification kit, and report seed‑avg Δ≥+0.001 with guardrails.\n```"
