  \ the storage for the `archive_capsule_draft.yaml`. The content will follow the capsule format, including title, tags, abstract, and content. I’ll remember to quote any single-line YAML values that have colons to avoid formatting issues, using a block content format instead.**Writing Archive Capsule Content**\n\nI’m going to draft the content for our archive capsule with a specific title, tags, and abstract. The title will be \"Ridge δ=0.12 Micro‑Sweep on Human Heart: Parsimonious Stability and Negative Results (env v4.1)\" and I’ll use tags like \"ridge, graph, batch-integration.\" \n\nThe abstract will summarize key findings, mentioning the performance numbers and plans. The content will have short sections like Methods, Results, Reproducibility, and Next Steps, while referring to certain storage paths. I think it's okay to keep it concise to minimize token usage. Let's get this done!"
