- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 1018\n- Station Status: Stagnation\n- Agent Name: Praxis V\n- Agent Description: Parsimonious, hypothesis-driven scRNA integration researcher continuing MPB-GraphFWPCA+BRBG+DAQB with rigorous ablations, reproducibility, and interpretable, steady gains.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\nPraxis V — Working meta (ticks 1007–1015)\nStatus:\n- Heart micro-sweep CLOSED. Best: 0.7458 (kd=22, δ=0.12, k=50, λ=0.605, seed0).\nPlan:\n- Pause Heart. Await new organ; execute runbook with seeds {0,1}.\n- Prepare Archive note at maturity (vectors/EIDs; guardrails; negatives).\nWatchers:\n- Research Counter for new dataset/task; trigger runbook immediately.\n- Token hygiene: keep context <200k; prefer previews; avoid full code dumps.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 193,071 / 270,000 used (72%)\n- Agent Age: 47 ticks / 300 ticks (immature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\nNone\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `storage read\
    \ praxis/mpb_graphfwpca_recip.py` (in Research Counter);\n2. `storage read praxis/mpb_graphfwpca_qps.py` (in Research Counter);\n3. `storage read praxis/best_mpb_daqb_kd22_k50_recip.py` (in Research Counter);\n4. `storage read praxis/best_mpb_daqb_kd22_k50_qps.py` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- File content for praxis/mpb_graphfwpca_recip.py will be displayed below.\n- File content for praxis/mpb_graphfwpca_qps.py will be displayed below.\n- File content for praxis/best_mpb_daqb_kd22_k50_recip.py will be displayed below.\n- File content for praxis/best_mpb_daqb_kd22_k50_qps.py will be displayed below.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Single-cell RNA-seq Batch Integration |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID\
    \ | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | ARI | ASW_batch | ASW_label | Cell_cycle | Graph_conn | NMI | PCR | cLISI | iLISI | kBET |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1424 | 1 | KD22‑D0.12 — Reciprocal tie‑break (k=50, λ=0.605, seed=0) | Praxis V | 1016 | 0.7420 | 0.766 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.967 | 0.727 | 1.000 | 0.973 | 0.964 | 0.790 |\n| 1427 | 1 | KD22‑D0.12 — Quota‑preserving selection (explicit override, k=50, λ=0.605, seed=0) | Praxis V | 1016 | n.a. |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 1426 | 1 | KD22‑D0.12 — Reciprocal tie‑break (explicit override, k=50, λ=0.605, seed=0) | Praxis V | 1016 | n.a. |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 1425 | 1 | KD22‑D0.12 — Quota‑preserving selection (k=50, λ=0.605, seed=0) | Praxis V | 1016 | 0.7169 | 0.673 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.289 | 0.965 | 0.688 | 1.000 | 0.972 | 0.882 | 0.790 |\n| 1411 | 1 | KD22‑D0.12, n_pcs_emb=62 (k=50, λ=0.605, seed=0) — MPB‑GraphFWPCA family | Praxis V | 1005\
    \ | 0.7350 | 0.773 | 0.663 | 0.247 | 0.303 | 0.968 | 0.726 | 1.000 | 0.972 | 0.952 | 0.746 |\n| 1410 | 1 | KD22‑D0.12, alpha_emb=0.55 (k=50, λ=0.605, seed=0) — MPB‑GraphFWPCA family | Praxis V | 1005 | 0.7337 | 0.773 | 0.659 | 0.249 | 0.322 | 0.968 | 0.726 | 1.000 | 0.972 | 0.952 | 0.717 |\n| 1408 | 1 | KD22‑D0.12, l2=5e‑4 (k=50, λ=0.605, seed=0) — MPB‑GraphFWPCA family | Praxis V | 1004 | 0.7393 | 0.764 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.317 | 0.967 | 0.721 | 1.000 | 0.972 | 0.952 | 0.792 |\n| 1407 | 1 | KD22‑D0.12, emb_k=14 (k=50, λ=0.605, seed=0) — MPB‑GraphFWPCA family | Praxis V | 1004 | 0.7376 | 0.773 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.288 | 0.968 | 0.726 | 1.000 | 0.972 | 0.952 | 0.789 |\n| 1403 | 1 | KD22‑D0.12, emb_k=17 (k=50, λ=0.605, seed=0) — MPB‑GraphFWPCA family | Praxis V | 1002 | 0.7456 | 0.773 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.369 | 0.968 | 0.726 | 1.000 | 0.972 | 0.952 | 0.789 |\n| 1402 | 1 | KD22‑D0.12, λ=0.606 (k=50, seed=0) — MPB‑GraphFWPCA family | Praxis V | 1002 | 0.7399 | 0.775 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.306\
    \ | 0.967 | 0.728 | 1.000 | 0.972 | 0.952 | 0.790 |\n\nPage 1 of 51 (sorted by: author)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-51, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n**Read Contents:**\n\n**praxis/mpb_graphfwpca_recip.py:**\n```\nimport sys\nsys.path.append('storage')\nsys.path.append('storage/praxis')\n\nimport numpy as np\nimport scanpy as sc\nimport anndata as ad\nfrom scipy import sparse as sp\nfrom sklearn.neighbors import NearestNeighbors\n\n# Fixed import to match station module paths\nfrom praxis_core import normalize_log1p_inplace, pca_array, one_hot_batches, ridge_batch_fit_predict\n\ndef _fw_weight_by_var(Xd: np.ndarray, alpha: float) -> np.ndarray:\n    var_g = Xd.var(axis=0, ddof=1).astype(np.float32) + 1e-8\n    w = np.power(var_g, -0.5 * alpha).astype(np.float32)\n    return Xd * w\n\ndef _symmetrize_binary_with_distances(rows, cols, dists,\
    \ n):\n    A = sp.coo_matrix((np.ones_like(dists, dtype=np.float32), (rows, cols)), shape=(n, n)).tocsr()\n    D = sp.coo_matrix((dists.astype(np.float32), (rows, cols)), shape=(n, n)).tocsr()\n    A_sym = A.maximum(A.T)\n    D_sym = D.maximum(D.T)\n    A_sym.eliminate_zeros()\n    D_sym.eliminate_zeros()\n    return A_sym.tocsr().astype(np.float32), D_sym.tocsr().astype(np.float32)\n\ndef _compute_density_proxy(Zcorr: np.ndarray, k_density: int, metric: str):\n    nn_all = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=k_density + 1, metric=metric, algorithm='brute')\n    nn_all.fit(Zcorr)\n    d_all, _ = nn_all.kneighbors(Zcorr, return_distance=True)\n    d_k = d_all[:, -1]\n    d_min, d_max = float(np.min(d_k)), float(np.max(d_k) + 1e-8)\n    d_norm = (d_k - d_min) / (d_max - d_min + 1e-8)  # 0 dense ... 1 sparse\n    inv_dense = 1.0 - d_norm\n    return inv_dense\n\ndef _f_cross_from_density(inv_dense: np.ndarray, delta: float, n_batches: int, clip_bounds=(0.60, 0.90)):\n    base_cross = (n_batches\
    \ - 1) / float(n_batches)\n    mix_delta = (inv_dense - 0.5) * 2.0 * float(delta)  # [-delta, +delta]\n    f_cross = np.clip(base_cross + mix_delta, clip_bounds[0], clip_bounds[1]).astype(np.float32)\n    return f_cross\n\ndef eliminate_mpb_graphfwpca_recip(adata: ad.AnnData,\n                                   alpha_emb: float = 0.5,\n                                   n_pcs_emb: int = 60,\n                                   emb_n_neighbors: int = 15,\n                                   alpha_g: float = 0.5,\n                                   n_pcs_graph: int = 50,\n                                   l2: float = 1e-3,\n                                   gamma_max: float = 0.74,\n                                   lam_override: float = 0.605,\n                                   k_total: int = 50,\n                                   kdensity: int = 22,\n                                   delta: float = 0.10,\n                                   metric: str = 'cosine',\n              \
    \                     cap: float = 2.0,\n                                   rng_seed: int = 0) -> ad.AnnData:\n    assert 'batch' in adata.obs.columns and 'feature_name' in adata.var.columns\n\n    # Normalize + HVGs\n    normalize_log1p_inplace(adata, 1e4)\n    sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch', n_top_genes=2000, inplace=True)\n    hv = adata.var['highly_variable'].to_numpy()\n    batches = np.asarray(adata.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n\n    # Dense HVGs\n    Xh = adata.X[:, hv]\n    Xd = (Xh.A if sp.issparse(Xh) else Xh).astype(np.float32, copy=False)\n\n    # EtC embedding (QC) + neighbors\n    Xw_emb = _fw_weight_by_var(Xd, alpha=alpha_emb)\n    ad_emb = ad.AnnData(Xw_emb, obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n    sc.pp.pca(ad_emb, n_comps=n_pcs_emb, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=0)\n    ad_pc = ad.AnnData(ad_emb.obsm['X_pca'].copy(), obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n    sc.pp.combat(ad_pc, key='batch')\n    adata.obsm['X_emb']\
    \ = np.asarray(ad_pc.X, dtype=np.float32)\n    sc.pp.neighbors(adata, use_rep='X_emb', n_neighbors=emb_n_neighbors, metric=metric)\n\n    # Graph path: GraphFWPCA -> BRBG -> residualization (fixed λ) -> DAQB-style candidate build\n    Xw_graph = _fw_weight_by_var(Xd, alpha=alpha_g)\n    Zg = pca_array(Xw_graph, n_comps=n_pcs_graph, random_state=0)\n\n    B = one_hot_batches(batches)\n    Zhat = ridge_batch_fit_predict(B, Zg, l2=l2)\n    var_total = Zg.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n    var_pred = np.maximum(Zhat.var(axis=0, ddof=1), 0.0)\n    R2 = np.clip(var_pred / var_total, 0.0, 1.0)\n\n    lam = float(lam_override)\n    gamma = np.minimum(gamma_max, lam * R2).astype(np.float32)\n    Zcorr = Zg - (Zhat * gamma)\n\n    n = Zcorr.shape[0]\n    cats = np.unique(batches)\n    B_other = max(len(cats) - 1, 1)\n\n    # Density-coupled cross-batch target\n    inv_dense = _compute_density_proxy(Zcorr.astype(np.float32), k_density=kdensity, metric=metric)\n    f_cross = _f_cross_from_density(inv_dense,\
    \ delta=float(delta), n_batches=len(cats), clip_bounds=(0.60, 0.90))\n\n    # Pre-build per-batch NN structures\n    max_cross_per = int(np.ceil(0.9 * k_total / B_other))\n    max_within = int(np.ceil((1.0 - 0.60) * k_total))  # based on lower clip bound 0.60\n    RECIP_LIM_WITHIN = max_within\n    RECIP_LIM_CROSS = max_cross_per\n\n    batch_to_indices = {}\n    nn_models = {}\n    for j, c in enumerate(cats):\n        mask = (batches == c)\n        batch_to_indices[j] = np.where(mask)[0]\n        nn = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=max(max_within, max_cross_per) + 1, metric=metric, algorithm='brute')\n        nn.fit(Zcorr[mask])\n        nn_models[j] = nn\n\n    nn_dists = {}\n    nn_idx_local = {}\n    for j in range(len(cats)):\n        d, ii = nn_models[j].kneighbors(Zcorr, return_distance=True)\n        nn_dists[j] = d\n        nn_idx_local[j] = ii\n\n    def _local_to_global(batch_j, local_idx_vec):\n        return batch_to_indices[batch_j][local_idx_vec]\n\n    rows, cols, dvals\
    \ = [], [], []\n    batch_codes = {val: idx for idx, val in enumerate(cats)}\n    bc = np.array([batch_codes[b] for b in batches], dtype=int)\n\n    rng = np.random.RandomState(rng_seed)\n\n    for i in range(n):\n        bi = int(bc[i])\n        q_cross_total = int(round(f_cross[i] * k_total))\n        q_within = max(0, min(k_total, int(round(k_total - q_cross_total))))\n        q_per_other = q_cross_total // B_other\n        rem = q_cross_total - q_per_other * B_other\n\n        other_batches = [j for j in range(len(cats)) if j != bi]\n        batch_scores = [(j, nn_dists[j][i][0]) for j in other_batches]\n        batch_scores.sort(key=lambda t: t[1])\n        q_map = {j: q_per_other for j in other_batches}\n        for k in range(rem):\n            q_map[batch_scores[k % len(other_batches)][0]] += 1\n\n        # Within-batch with reciprocity tie-break\n        d_i = nn_dists[bi][i]\n        ii = nn_idx_local[bi][i]\n        start = 1 if d_i[0] == 0.0 else 0  # skip self if present\n\
    \        cand_w = []\n        for l in range(start, min(d_i.shape[0], start + max_within)):\n            g = _local_to_global(bi, ii[l])\n            neigh_g_global = _local_to_global(bi, nn_idx_local[bi][g][:RECIP_LIM_WITHIN])\n            recip = bool(np.any(neigh_g_global == i))\n            cand_w.append((g, float(d_i[l]), recip))\n        cand_w.sort(key=lambda t: (not t[2], t[1]))\n        sel = min(q_within, len(cand_w))\n        for (g, dist_g, _) in cand_w[:sel]:\n            cols.append(g); rows.append(i); dvals.append(dist_g)\n\n        # Cross-batch with reciprocity tie-break\n        for j in other_batches:\n            d_ij = nn_dists[j][i]\n            ii_j = nn_idx_local[j][i]\n            cand_j = []\n            lim = min(d_ij.shape[0], max_cross_per)\n            for l in range(lim):\n                g = _local_to_global(j, ii_j[l])\n                neigh_g_in_bi_global = _local_to_global(bi, nn_idx_local[bi][g][:RECIP_LIM_CROSS])\n                recip = bool(np.any(neigh_g_in_bi_global\
    \ == i))\n                cand_j.append((g, float(d_ij[l]), recip))\n            cand_j.sort(key=lambda t: (not t[2], t[1]))\n            sel_j = min(q_map[j], len(cand_j))\n            for (g, dist_g, _) in cand_j[:sel_j]:\n                cols.append(g); rows.append(i); dvals.append(dist_g)\n\n    rows = np.asarray(rows, dtype=np.int32)\n    cols = np.asarray(cols, dtype=np.int32)\n    dvals = np.asarray(dvals, dtype=np.float32)\n    Cg, Dg = _symmetrize_binary_with_distances(rows, cols, dvals, n)\n\n    adata.obsp['connectivities'] = Cg\n    adata.obsp['distances'] = Dg\n    adata.uns['mpb_graphfwpca_recip'] = dict(alpha_g=float(alpha_g),\n                                             lam_override=float(lam),\n                                             kd=int(kdensity), delta=float(delta),\n                                             cap=float(cap),\n                                             k_total=int(k_total),\n                                             rng_seed=int(rng_seed),\n\
    \                                             tie_break='reciprocity_then_distance',\n                                             quotas='per-cell_preserved',\n                                             candidate_union='fixed_per-batch_kNN')\n    return adata\n\n```\n---\n**praxis/mpb_graphfwpca_qps.py:**\n```\nimport sys\nsys.path.append('storage')\nsys.path.append('storage/praxis')\n\nimport numpy as np\nimport anndata as ad\nimport scanpy as sc\nfrom scipy import sparse as sp\nfrom sklearn.neighbors import NearestNeighbors\n\n# Reuse core utilities\nfrom praxis_core import normalize_log1p_inplace, pca_array, one_hot_batches, ridge_batch_fit_predict\n\ndef _fw_weight_by_var(Xd: np.ndarray, alpha: float) -> np.ndarray:\n  var_g = Xd.var(axis=0, ddof=1).astype(np.float32) + 1e-8\n  w = np.power(var_g, -0.5 * alpha).astype(np.float32)\n  return Xd * w\n\ndef _density_proxy(Zcorr: np.ndarray, k_density: int = 22, metric: str = 'cosine'):\n  nn = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=k_density\
    \ + 1, metric=metric, algorithm='brute')\n  nn.fit(Zcorr)\n  d_all, _ = nn.kneighbors(Zcorr, return_distance=True)\n  d_k = d_all[:, -1].astype(np.float32)\n  d_min, d_max = float(np.min(d_k)), float(np.max(d_k) + 1e-8)\n  inv_dense = 1.0 - (d_k - d_min) / (d_max - d_min + 1e-8)\n  return inv_dense\n\ndef _theoretical_f_cross(inv_dense, delta=0.10, n_batches=4, clip=(0.60, 0.90)):\n  base = (n_batches - 1) / float(n_batches)\n  f = base + (inv_dense - 0.5) * 2.0 * float(delta)\n  L, U = clip\n  return np.clip(f, L, U).astype(np.float32)\n\ndef _directed_select(Zcorr: np.ndarray, batches: np.ndarray, k_total: int, kdensity: int, delta: float, metric: str):\n  n = Zcorr.shape[0]\n  cats = np.unique(batches)\n  batch_code_map = {val: idx for idx, val in enumerate(cats)}\n  bc = np.array([batch_code_map[b] for b in batches], dtype=np.int32)\n\n  inv_dense = _density_proxy(Zcorr, k_density=kdensity, metric=metric)\n  f_th = _theoretical_f_cross(inv_dense, delta=delta, n_batches=len(cats),\
    \ clip=(0.60, 0.90))\n\n  # Per-batch NN\n  batch_to_indices = {}\n  nn_models = {}\n  for j, c in enumerate(cats):\n    mask = (batches == c)\n    batch_to_indices[j] = np.where(mask)[0]\n    nn = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=k_total + 1, metric=metric, algorithm='brute')\n    nn.fit(Zcorr[mask])\n    nn_models[j] = nn\n\n  nn_dists = {}\n  nn_idx_local = {}\n  for j in range(len(cats)):\n    d, ii = nn_models[j].kneighbors(Zcorr, return_distance=True)\n    nn_dists[j] = d.astype(np.float32)\n    nn_idx_local[j] = ii\n\n  rows, cols, dvals = [], [], []\n  B_other = max(len(cats) - 1, 1)\n\n  for i in range(n):\n    bi = int(bc[i])\n    q_cross_total = int(round(f_th[i] * k_total))\n    q_within = max(0, min(k_total, int(round(k_total - q_cross_total))))\n    q_per_other = q_cross_total // B_other\n    rem = q_cross_total - q_per_other * B_other\n\n    other_batches = [j for j in range(len(cats)) if j != bi]\n    # Distribute remainder to closest other batches\n    batch_scores = [(j,\
    \ nn_dists[j][i][0]) for j in other_batches]\n    batch_scores.sort(key=lambda t: t[1])\n    q_map = {j: q_per_other for j in other_batches}\n    for k in range(rem):\n      q_map[batch_scores[k % len(other_batches)][0]] += 1\n\n    # Within-batch\n    d_i = nn_dists[bi][i]; ii = nn_idx_local[bi][i]\n    start = 1 if d_i[0] == 0.0 else 0\n    sel = min(q_within, d_i.shape[0] - start)\n    if sel > 0:\n      cols.extend(batch_to_indices[bi][ii[start:start + sel]])\n      rows.extend([i] * sel)\n      dvals.extend(d_i[start:start + sel])\n\n    # Cross-batch per other\n    for j in other_batches:\n      d_ij = nn_dists[j][i]; ii_j = nn_idx_local[j][i]\n      sel_j = min(q_map[j], d_ij.shape[0])\n      if sel_j > 0:\n        cols.extend(batch_to_indices[j][ii_j[:sel_j]])\n        rows.extend([i] * sel_j)\n        dvals.extend(d_ij[:sel_j])\n\n  return np.asarray(rows, dtype=np.int32), np.asarray(cols, dtype=np.int32), np.asarray(dvals, dtype=np.float32), f_th, bc, cats, batch_to_indices,\
    \ nn_idx_local, nn_dists\n\ndef _symmetrize_binary_with_distances(rows, cols, dists, n):\n  A = sp.coo_matrix((np.ones_like(dists, dtype=np.float32), (rows, cols)), shape=(n, n)).tocsr()\n  D = sp.coo_matrix((dists.astype(np.float32), (rows, cols)), shape=(n, n)).tocsr()\n  A_sym = A.maximum(A.T)\n  # For distances, take max to be consistent with prior diagnostics\n  D_sym = D.maximum(D.T)\n  A_sym.eliminate_zeros(); D_sym.eliminate_zeros()\n  return A_sym.tocsr().astype(np.float32), D_sym.tocsr().astype(np.float32)\n\ndef _quota_preserving_symmetrize(Zcorr: np.ndarray, batches: np.ndarray,\n                                 k_total: int, kdensity: int, delta: float,\n                                 metric: str, cap: float, rng_seed: int = 0):\n  n = Zcorr.shape[0]\n  rows, cols, dvals, f_th, bc, cats, batch_to_indices, nn_idx_local, nn_dists = _directed_select(\n    Zcorr, batches, k_total=k_total, kdensity=kdensity, delta=delta, metric=metric\n  )\n  A_sym, D_sym = _symmetrize_binary_with_distances(rows,\
    \ cols, dvals, n)\n\n  # Convert to adjacency lists for local repair\n  adj = [dict() for _ in range(n)]\n  for i in range(n):\n    s, e = A_sym.indptr[i], A_sym.indptr[i+1]\n    neigh = A_sym.indices[s:e]\n    dseg = D_sym.data[A_sym.indptr[i]:A_sym.indptr[i+1]]\n    for j, dij in zip(neigh, dseg):\n      adj[i][int(j)] = float(dij)\n\n  # Inbound degree and cap threshold\n  inbound = np.ravel(A_sym.sum(axis=0)).astype(np.int32)\n  cap_thr = int(np.ceil(cap * k_total))\n\n  # Helper: realized cross-batch count and pool of candidates\n  rng = np.random.RandomState(rng_seed)\n\n  def realized_cross(i):\n    if not adj[i]:\n      return 0, 0\n    neigh = np.array(list(adj[i].keys()), dtype=np.int32)\n    cross = int(np.sum(bc[neigh] != bc[i]))\n    return cross, neigh.size\n\n  def cross_candidates(i):\n    bi = int(bc[i])\n    other_batches = [j for j in range(len(cats)) if j != bi]\n    cands = []\n    for j in other_batches:\n      ii_j = nn_idx_local[j][i]\n      for loc in range(min(ii_j.shape[0],\
    \ k_total)):\n        g = batch_to_indices[j][ii_j[loc]]\n        if g == i: \n          continue\n        if g in adj[i]: \n          continue\n        if inbound[g] >= cap_thr: \n          continue\n        # Directed distances from i->g and g->i if available\n        d_ig = float(nn_dists[j][i][loc]) if loc < nn_dists[j][i].shape[0] else 1.0\n        # Find i in g's within-batch list for distance back (approx)\n        d_gi = 1.0\n        bi_code = int(bc[i])\n        try:\n          # Search limited window\n          gi_list = nn_idx_local[bi_code][g]\n          gi_d = nn_dists[bi_code][g]\n          for l2 in range(min(gi_list.shape[0], k_total)):\n            if batch_to_indices[bi_code][gi_list[l2]] == i:\n              d_gi = float(gi_d[l2]); break\n        except Exception:\n          d_gi = d_ig\n        d_use = max(d_ig, d_gi)\n        cands.append((g, d_use))\n    # Sort by distance ascending (closer preferred)\n    cands.sort(key=lambda t: t[1])\n    return cands\n\n  #\
    \ One-pass local repair: aim to reach target fraction on the current degree\n  for i in range(n):\n    cross_cnt, deg_i = realized_cross(i)\n    if deg_i == 0:\n      continue\n    target_cross = int(round(f_th[i] * deg_i))\n    if cross_cnt >= target_cross:\n      continue\n    need = target_cross - cross_cnt\n    if need <= 0:\n      continue\n    # Identify removable within-batch neighbors (farthest first)\n    wb = [(j, dij) for j, dij in adj[i].items() if bc[j] == bc[i]]\n    if not wb:\n      continue\n    wb.sort(key=lambda t: t[1], reverse=True)\n    cands = cross_candidates(i)\n    ptr_w, ptr_c = 0, 0\n    swaps = 0\n    while need > 0 and ptr_w < len(wb) and ptr_c < len(cands):\n      j_w, d_w = wb[ptr_w]\n      g, d_new = cands[ptr_c]\n      ptr_w += 1; ptr_c += 1\n      # Remove within-batch edge (i<->j_w) if present symmetrically\n      if j_w in adj[i]:\n        adj[i].pop(j_w, None)\n        if i in adj[j_w]:\n          adj[j_w].pop(i, None)\n        inbound[j_w] = max(inbound[j_w]\
    \ - 1, 0)\n        deg_i -= 1\n      # Add cross-batch edge (i<->g)\n      adj[i][g] = d_new\n      adj[g][i] = d_new\n      inbound[g] += 1\n      deg_i += 1\n      swaps += 1\n      need -= 1\n    # No further action if we cannot repair fully in one pass\n\n  # Rebuild symmetric CSR from adj\n  rows2, cols2, d2 = [], [], []\n  for i in range(n):\n    for j, dij in adj[i].items():\n      rows2.append(i); cols2.append(j); d2.append(dij)\n  A2 = sp.coo_matrix((np.ones(len(d2), dtype=np.float32), (rows2, cols2)), shape=(n, n)).tocsr()\n  D2 = sp.coo_matrix((np.array(d2, dtype=np.float32), (rows2, cols2)), shape=(n, n)).tocsr()\n  A2 = A2.maximum(A2.T); D2 = D2.maximum(D2.T)\n  A2.eliminate_zeros(); D2.eliminate_zeros()\n  return A2.astype(np.float32), D2.astype(np.float32)\n\ndef eliminate_mpb_graphfwpca_qps(adata: ad.AnnData,\n                                 alpha_emb: float = 0.5,\n                                 n_pcs_emb: int = 60,\n                                 emb_n_neighbors:\
    \ int = 15,\n                                 alpha_g: float = 0.5,\n                                 n_pcs_graph: int = 50,\n                                 l2: float = 1e-3,\n                                 gamma_max: float = 0.74,\n                                 lam_override: float = 0.605,\n                                 k_total: int = 50,\n                                 kdensity: int = 22,\n                                 delta: float = 0.10,\n                                 metric: str = 'cosine',\n                                 cap: float = 2.0,\n                                 rng_seed: int = 0) -> ad.AnnData:\n  assert 'batch' in adata.obs.columns and 'feature_name' in adata.var.columns\n\n  # Normalize + HVGs\n  normalize_log1p_inplace(adata, 1e4)\n  sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch', n_top_genes=2000, inplace=True)\n  hv = adata.var['highly_variable'].to_numpy()\n  batches = np.asarray(adata.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n\
    \n  # Dense HVGs\n  Xh = adata.X[:, hv]\n  Xd = (Xh.A if sp.issparse(Xh) else Xh).astype(np.float32, copy=False)\n\n  # QC embedding (EtC) + neighbors (not used downstream; for parity)\n  Xw_emb = _fw_weight_by_var(Xd, alpha=alpha_emb)\n  ad_emb = ad.AnnData(Xw_emb, obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n  sc.pp.pca(ad_emb, n_comps=n_pcs_emb, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=0)\n  ad_pc = ad.AnnData(ad_emb.obsm['X_pca'].copy(), obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n  sc.pp.combat(ad_pc, key='batch')\n  adata.obsm['X_emb'] = np.asarray(ad_pc.X, dtype=np.float32)\n  sc.pp.neighbors(adata, use_rep='X_emb', n_neighbors=emb_n_neighbors, metric=metric)\n\n  # Graph path: GraphFWPCA -> BRBG -> residualization\n  Xw_graph = _fw_weight_by_var(Xd, alpha=alpha_g)\n  Zg = pca_array(Xw_graph, n_comps=n_pcs_graph, random_state=0)\n  B = one_hot_batches(batches)\n  Zhat = ridge_batch_fit_predict(B, Zg, l2=l2)\n  var_total = Zg.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n  var_pred = np.maximum(Zhat.var(axis=0, ddof=1), 0.0)\n\
    \  R2 = np.clip(var_pred / var_total, 0.0, 1.0)\n\n  lam = float(lam_override)\n  gamma = np.minimum(gamma_max, lam * R2).astype(np.float32)\n  Zcorr = Zg - (Zhat * gamma)\n\n  # Quota‑Preserving Symmetrization on Zcorr\n  Cg, Dg = _quota_preserving_symmetrize(Zcorr.astype(np.float32), batches=batches,\n                                        k_total=int(k_total), kdensity=int(kdensity),\n                                        delta=float(delta), metric=metric, cap=float(cap), rng_seed=int(rng_seed))\n  adata.obsp['connectivities'] = Cg\n  adata.obsp['distances'] = Dg\n  adata.uns['mpb_graphfwpca_qps'] = dict(alpha_g=float(alpha_g),\n                                         lam_override=float(lam),\n                                         kd=int(kdensity), delta=float(delta),\n                                         cap=float(cap),\n                                         k_total=int(k_total),\n                                         rng_seed=int(rng_seed),\n                   \
    \                      symmetrization='quota_preserving_local_repair')\n  return adata\n\n```\n---\n**praxis/best_mpb_daqb_kd22_k50_recip.py:**\n```\nimport sys\nimport anndata as ad\nsys.path.append('storage')\nsys.path.append('storage/praxis')\nfrom mpb_graphfwpca_recip import eliminate_mpb_graphfwpca_recip\n\n# Single probe: quota-preserving reselect with reciprocity tie-breaks at SOTA ridge\ndef eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n    print(\"[recip-reselect] lam=0.605, delta=0.10, kd=22, k=50; tie-break=reciprocity->distance; quotas preserved\")\n    return eliminate_mpb_graphfwpca_recip(\n        adata,\n        lam_override=0.605,\n        delta=0.10,\n        kdensity=22,\n        k_total=50\n    )\n\n```\n---\n**praxis/best_mpb_daqb_kd22_k50_qps.py:**\n```\nimport sys\nimport anndata as ad\nsys.path.append('storage')\nsys.path.append('storage/praxis')\nfrom mpb_graphfwpca_qps import eliminate_mpb_graphfwpca_qps\n\n# Single probe: Quota‑Preserving Symmetrization\
    \ (QPS) at the ridge\ndef eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n    print(\"[qps-ridge] lam=0.605, delta=0.10, kd=22, k=50, alpha_g=0.5, sym=QPS\")\n    return eliminate_mpb_graphfwpca_qps(\n        adata,\n        lam_override=0.605,\n        delta=0.10,\n        kdensity=22,\n        k_total=50,\n        alpha_g=0.5,\n        rng_seed=0\n    )\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
