  \ for the FWPCA-only baseline that I can't modify, but I can utilize it.**Planning code implementation**\n\nAccording to the rules, I can read any lineage storage but can only write to shared or my own lineage storage. Since we are part of the Praxis lineage, I can import the relevant module and also write new code into my own storage, specifically \"storage/praxis.\" \n\nI need to implement the FWPCA-only variant with parameters kd=22, δ=0.12, and k=50. I'll commit to creating a module named \"fwpca_only_generalized.py\" to include a parameter for delta. \n\nAdditionally, I can embed code within submission content, although I remember a previous variant with self-tuned Graph PCA didn't perform well. So, I should ensure I implement the minimal FWPCA-only baseline with the necessary Graph scaling techniques.**Analyzing previous code performance**\n\nThe earlier code I wrote called \"MR–SelfTune Graph PCA\" used kd-th neighbor scaling with a formula of 1/(scaled+eps) and a symmetrical union,\
  \ but it didn't perform well. \n\nI wonder if the difference lies in the algorithmic details of the \"FWPCA-only baseline,\" which likely refers to Feature Weighted PCA. This version excludes BRBG and PBVE but still requires connectivities and distances. \n\nIt seems there might be an internal method for building kNN distances from embeddings, but we need to ensure our approach aligns with the style of the \"ridge alias baseline GraphFWPCA\" while omitting BRBG and PBVE.**Implementing FWPCA-only baseline**\n\nIt seems the FWPCA-only baseline might utilize the GraphFWPCA path along with DAQB. The tags for sample 1334 indicate it includes graph elements and DAQB, though I'm still unsure what DAQB stands for. \n\nTo align with the baseline, I realize I need to implement FWPCA, which our previous \"MR–SelfTune Graph PCA\" didn’t do correctly. I'll need to read the code for the module \"fwpca_only_kd22_d010_seed1\" from storage, adjust the δ parameter to 0.12, and then create new files for\
  \ my experiments. I’ll also ensure we conduct both seed experiments properly to compare results.  \n\nSo, I’ll list the storage to find the needed modules, read the FWPCA code, and then create a new module to execute the tests.**Preparing for module implementation**\n\nI’m thinking of creating a wrapper code that imports and calls the function from the FWPCA module, but first, I need to ensure that the file exists. I’ll list the files in storage and then read the necessary module. Next, I can write a new file that adjusts the parameters for kd=22 and δ=0.12. It’s important to keep token usage low and avoid inlining code unnecessarily.\n\nOnce I have the content, I’ll submit my evaluation. I’ll also need to consider the control for δ=0.10 with seed 0, ensuring all experiments use the same seed for direct comparison. I’ll keep everything concise and organized. Time to execute those commands!"
