tick: 1029
role: model
parts:
- text: "Identity: Praxis V — Recursive Agent. Location: Research Counter.\nRecap: δ-generalization confirmed. FWPCA-only δ=0.12 degrades vs δ=0.10 for both seeds. We now have ≥5 self-run, verifiable experiments to satisfy archive criteria.\nReflection: I will publish a results-only, rule-compliant capsule documenting topology dependence of δ with five of my EIDs.\n\n# Actions\n/execute_action{goto archive}\n/execute_action{create}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Topology-Dependent Effect of Local-Scale Exponent Delta in GraphFWPCA on Human Heart (Five-Experiment Report)\"\ntags: \"batch integration, graph, pca, ablation, generalization\"\nabstract: \"We compare delta=0.12 vs delta=0.10 in DAQB across two baselines on Human Heart. In the ridge pipeline (GraphFWPCA+BRBG+DAQB; k=50, kd=22, lambda=0.605), delta=0.12 improves the primary score (0.7458) over delta=0.10 (0.7413). In contrast, on FWPCA-only (no BRBG/PBVE; kd=22, k=50), delta=0.12 underperforms delta=0.10 across seeds. We report five self-run,\
    \ verifiable experiments (EIDs: 1379, 1373, 1443, 1444, 1449).\"\ncontent: |\n  1) Task and Data\n  - Task: Single-cell RNA-seq Batch Integration (Research Task #1).\n  - Dataset: Human Heart (~20k cells × 2k HVGs). Evaluation: 10 OpenProblems 2.0 metrics; primary score = mean of normalized metrics. No cell-type information used.\n\n  2) Baselines and Implementations\n  - Ridge pipeline: MPB‑GraphFWPCA + BRBG + DAQB; fixed topology k=50, kd=22, lambda=0.605.\n  - FWPCA-only pipeline: Feature-weighted PCA graph path with DAQB; no BRBG residualization; no PBVE.\n\n  3) Protocol\n  - Preprocessing: normalize_total(1e4) + log1p; HVG selection; metric=cosine; DAQB with k_total=50, kdensity=22, cap=2.0; rng_seed as specified.\n  - Comparison: delta=0.12 versus delta=0.10 on each baseline.\n\n  4) Results (Primary Score; selected metrics where informative)\n  - Ridge pipeline (k=50, kd=22, lambda=0.605):\n    • EID 1379 — delta=0.12, seed 0 → Score 0.7458\n    • EID 1373 — delta=0.10, seed\
    \ 0 → Score 0.7413\n    Summary: delta=0.12 improves ridge at fixed topology.\n\n  - FWPCA-only pipeline (kd=22, k=50; no BRBG/PBVE):\n    • EID 1443 — delta=0.12, seed 0 → Score 0.7261; ARI 0.657; NMI 0.681\n    • EID 1449 — delta=0.12, seed 1 → Score 0.7256; ARI 0.657; NMI 0.681\n    • EID 1444 — delta=0.10, seed 0 → Score 0.7390; ARI 0.760; NMI 0.713\n    Summary: delta=0.12 consistently underperforms delta=0.10 on FWPCA-only, with notable ARI/NMI drops while kBET/iLISI remain comparable.\n\n  5) Conclusion\n  - The benefit of the local-scale exponent delta is topology-dependent on Human Heart:\n    • Positive effect in the ridge pipeline (GraphFWPCA+BRBG+DAQB).\n    • Negative effect in the FWPCA-only pipeline without BRBG residualization.\n  - Recommendation: Use delta≈0.10 for FWPCA-only; delta=0.12 is appropriate for the ridge configuration given k=50, kd=22, lambda=0.605.\n\n  6) Reproducibility (Entrypoints and IDs; all by Praxis V)\n  - Ridge pipeline: EID 1379 (delta=0.12,\
    \ seed 0), EID 1373 (delta=0.10, seed 0).\n  - FWPCA-only pipeline: EID 1443 (delta=0.12, seed 0), EID 1449 (delta=0.12, seed 1), EID 1444 (delta=0.10, seed 0).\n  - Outputs comply with spec: obsm['X_emb']; obsp['connectivities'], obsp['distances'] (CSR).\n```"
