tick: 1033
role: model
parts:
- text: "Identity: Praxis V — Recursive Agent. Location: Research Counter.\nRecap: Submitted analysis-only diagnostics (EID 1454) to compute σ_kd from final distance graphs at δ=0.12. Ridge alias may not expose δ; to ensure integrity, I’ll add a second analysis-only test that computes σ_kd for FWPCA-only at δ∈{0.10, 0.12} using explicit parameters.\nReflection: This isolates the mechanism without conflating alias defaults. Concurrency allows 2 runs, so launching the companion FWPCA-only diagnostic now.\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Diagnostics: σ_kd distributions — FWPCA-only at δ∈{0.10,0.12} (kd=22, k=50)\"\ntags: \"analysis, diagnostics, fwpca, kd, delta, density\"\nabstract: \"Analysis-only test. Runs FWPCA-only twice on Human Heart with δ=0.10 and δ=0.12 (kd=22, k=50), then computes kd-th neighbor distance (σ_kd) distributions from the final distance graphs. Reports global and per-batch summaries (median, mean, CV, Gini) for both deltas.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys,\
    \ json, numpy as np\n  import anndata as ad\n  import scipy.sparse as sp\n  sys.path.append('storage/praxis')\n  from fwpca_only_utils import run_fwpca_only\n\n  def _kd_stat_from_distances(D: sp.csr_matrix, kd: int) -> np.ndarray:\n      if not sp.isspmatrix_csr(D):\n          D = D.tocsr()\n      n = D.shape[0]\n      sigma = np.full(n, np.nan, dtype=np.float64)\n      idx_ptr = D.indptr\n      data = D.data\n      for i in range(n):\n          start, end = idx_ptr[i], idx_ptr[i+1]\n          row = data[start:end]\n          if row.size >= kd:\n              kth = np.partition(row, kd-1)[kd-1]\n              sigma[i] = float(kth)\n      return sigma\n\n  def _gini(x):\n      x = np.asarray(x, dtype=np.float64)\n      x = x[np.isfinite(x)]\n      if x.size == 0:\n          return np.nan\n      x = np.abs(x)\n      if np.allclose(x.sum(), 0):\n          return 0.0\n      x.sort()\n      n = x.size\n      cumx = np.cumsum(x)\n      return (n + 1 - 2 * np.sum(cumx) / cumx[-1]) / n\n\n\
    \  def _summaries(sigma: np.ndarray, batches: np.ndarray, label: str):\n      mask = np.isfinite(sigma)\n      s = sigma[mask]\n      out = {\n          \"label\": label,\n          \"n\": int(s.size),\n          \"median\": float(np.median(s)) if s.size else np.nan,\n          \"mean\": float(np.mean(s)) if s.size else np.nan,\n          \"std\": float(np.std(s, ddof=1)) if s.size > 1 else np.nan,\n          \"cv\": float(np.std(s, ddof=1) / np.mean(s)) if s.size > 1 and np.mean(s) > 0 else np.nan,\n          \"gini\": float(_gini(s)),\n      }\n      per_batch = {}\n      for b in np.unique(batches):\n          mb = mask & (batches == b)\n          sb = sigma[mb]\n          sb = sb[np.isfinite(sb)]\n          per_batch[str(b)] = float(np.median(sb)) if sb.size else np.nan\n      out[\"per_batch_median\"] = per_batch\n      return out\n\n  def test(adata: ad.AnnData):\n      kdensity = 22\n      k_total = 50\n      batches = np.asarray(adata.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n\
    \n      # FWPCA-only at δ=0.10\n      ad_d010 = adata.copy()\n      ad_d010 = run_fwpca_only(\n          ad_d010,\n          alpha_g=0.50,\n          kdensity=kdensity,\n          k_total=k_total,\n          delta=0.10,\n          metric='cosine',\n          cap=2.0,\n          rng_seed=0,\n          pbve_temper=None\n      )\n      D010 = ad_d010.obsp.get('distances', None)\n\n      # FWPCA-only at δ=0.12\n      ad_d012 = adata.copy()\n      ad_d012 = run_fwpca_only(\n          ad_d012,\n          alpha_g=0.50,\n          kdensity=kdensity,\n          k_total=k_total,\n          delta=0.12,\n          metric='cosine',\n          cap=2.0,\n          rng_seed=0,\n          pbve_temper=None\n      )\n      D012 = ad_d012.obsp.get('distances', None)\n\n      results = {}\n      if D010 is not None:\n          sig010 = _kd_stat_from_distances(D010, kdensity)\n          results[\"fwpca_d010\"] = _summaries(sig010, batches, \"fwpca_d010\")\n      else:\n          results[\"fwpca_d010\"] =\
    \ {\"label\": \"fwpca_d010\", \"error\": \"no_distances\"}\n\n      if D012 is not None:\n          sig012 = _kd_stat_from_distances(D012, kdensity)\n          results[\"fwpca_d012\"] = _summaries(sig012, batches, \"fwpca_d012\")\n      else:\n          results[\"fwpca_d012\"] = {\"label\": \"fwpca_d012\", \"error\": \"no_distances\"}\n\n      # Contrast summary: relative change of median and dispersion\n      if \"fwpca_d010\" in results and \"fwpca_d012\" in results and \"median\" in results[\"fwpca_d010\"] and \"median\" in results[\"fwpca_d012\"]:\n          m010 = results[\"fwpca_d010\"][\"median\"]\n          m012 = results[\"fwpca_d012\"][\"median\"]\n          cv010 = results[\"fwpca_d010\"][\"cv\"]\n          cv012 = results[\"fwpca_d012\"][\"cv\"]\n          results[\"diff\"] = {\n              \"median_ratio_d012_over_d010\": (m012 / m010) if (m010 and np.isfinite(m010) and np.isfinite(m012)) else np.nan,\n              \"cv_delta\": (cv012 - cv010) if (cv010 is not None and\
    \ cv012 is not None) else np.nan\n          }\n\n      print(json.dumps(results, indent=2, sort_keys=True))\n      return \"σ_kd diagnostics completed (FWPCA-only)\"\n```"
thinking_content: '**Planning analysis submissions**


  I noticed the message "Your submission has been queued," but I haven''t seen any results yet. It''s probably still processing. I''ve got the option to set watchers through meta, but we already have that covered. I think I can prepare for the next step: running an analysis with δ=0.10 to compute distributions. Given the constraints of running evaluations, I can submit another diagnostic test for ridge and FWPCA-only to get comprehensive results quickly. That sounds like a good idea!**Examining ridge alias settings**


  I see that our test code is using best_adopted_alias for ridge, but that function might default to δ values of either 0.06 or 0.10. Previously, our ridge baseline was at δ=0.10, and its parameters might not match what we want. I need to enforce the δ value within the ridge alias, but that can be tricky. A better approach might be to replicate the ridge pipeline while introducing the δ parameter, even if that adds complexity.**Exploring distance calculations**


  Another idea is to use the dataset and compute neighbor distances from the adata.obsm data rather than relying on the alias''s graph. The alias gives us connectivities and distances, but I could calculate kd distance distribution based on the underlying representation, Z_g, and introduce δ in that computation. However, if I want to recompute with a different δ, I would need to rebuild the graph using my own function, which is a challenge since we don’t have the function for BRBG.**Calculating distances in embedding space**


  I can compute distances in the embedding space instead of relying on the graph. While that won’t give me the DAQB kd-th distances, I could implement local scaling for kd-th neighbor distances in purely geometric terms using Euclidean space with kd=22. This would let me focus on measuring the effect of BRBG preprocessing on local density. The reviewer suggested computing local neighborhood sizes before and after BRBG, which is achievable by calculating kd-th neighbor distances in Zg PC space, avoiding the enforcement of δ and concentrating on the raw distance distribution.**Preparing for FWPCA analysis**


  I could compute kd-th neighbor distances on the raw Zg PCA space, but the code for ridge alias isn''t available. The alias includes BRBG residualization, complicating things. Still, I plan to calculate distances at δ=0.10. However, discrepancies arise since the ridge alias sometimes uses δ=0.06, which I''m concerned could misrepresent results. It might be best to focus solely on FWPCA, running tests at both δ=0.10 and δ=0.12, ensuring that I correctly analyze and interpret the outcomes. I''ll set up everything accordingly.**Crafting the final output**


  Alright, I need to begin by identifying the content and location. I see that submission 1454 is running, and I have some concerns about the ridge alias. My plan is to add diagnostics comparing FWPCA at δ=0.10 versus δ=0.12. I’ll prepare to submit the second test without reviewing 1454 since it’s still in progress. I’ll import run_fwpca_only, compute distances, and calculate kd-th neighbor distances from D. I’ll also implement Gini and CV, then return "done." Let''s format everything properly in the YAML block.'
