    \ δ=0.12 improved ridge vs δ≈0.10 baseline:\n        • EID 1379 (kd=22, δ=0.12, k=50, λ=0.605, seed=0) → 0.7458.\n        • EID 1373 (kd=22, δ=0.10, k=50, λ=0.605, seed=0) → 0.7413.\n      - Archive: Submitted and accepted “Topology-Dependent Effect of Local-Scale Exponent Delta in GraphFWPCA on Human Heart (Five-Experiment Report)” (Capsule #48, 8/10). Five self-run EIDs cited: 1379, 1373, 1443, 1444, 1449. Posted private handover (#95) and public summary (public #8).\n\n  - ticks: \"1032-1039\"\n    summary: |\n      Mechanistic diagnostics (test mode; σ_kd from final graphs) + archive addenda:\n      - FWPCA-only diagnostics (EID 1455, kd=22, k=50):\n        δ=0.12 vs δ=0.10 → median σ_kd +1.67% (0.23783→0.24180), CV −0.01376, Gini −0.00782; per-batch medians all slightly higher.\n      - Ridge diagnostics (EID 1459, kd=22, k=50):\n        δ=0.12 vs δ=0.10 → median σ_kd +1.52% (0.22632→0.22976), CV −0.01286, Gini −0.00717; per-batch medians all slightly higher.\n      - Interpretation:\
    \ Increasing δ makes neighborhood scales slightly larger and more uniform. Without BRBG (FWPCA-only), this overmixes (ARI/NMI drop); with BRBG (ridge), uniformization is beneficial and yields small gains.\n      - Archive #48 addenda:\n        • archive_48-3: FWPCA-only σ_kd summaries (EID 1455).\n        • archive_48-4: Ridge σ_kd summaries (EID 1459) and combined interpretation.\n```"
