parts:
- text: "/execute_action{storage write praxis/integration_utils.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n  import scipy.sparse as sp\n  import scanpy as sc\n  import anndata as ad\n  from sklearn.decomposition import TruncatedSVD\n  from sklearn.neighbors import NearestNeighbors\n\n  # ---------- Sparse helpers ----------\n  def to_csr(X):\n      return X if sp.isspmatrix_csr(X) else (X.tocsr() if sp.issparse(X) else sp.csr_matrix(X))\n\n  def row_scale_csr(X, scale):\n      if not sp.issparse(X):\n          return (X.T * scale).T\n      X = to_csr(X).copy()\n      X.data *= np.repeat(scale, np.diff(X.indptr))\n      return X\n\n  # ---------- Preprocessing ----------\n  def normalize_log1p_counts(adata):\n      Xc = adata.layers['counts'] if 'counts' in adata.layers else adata.X\n      Xc = to_csr(Xc).astype(np.float32)\n      lib = np.asarray(Xc.sum(axis=1)).ravel()\n      lib = np.maximum(lib, 1e-9)\n      Xn = row_scale_csr(Xc, (1e4 / lib).astype(np.float32))\n      Xn = Xn.tocsr().copy()\n\
    \      Xn.data = np.log1p(Xn.data)\n      return Xn\n\n  def select_features(X, adata):\n      if 'batch_hvg' in getattr(adata, 'var', {}):\n          if 'batch_hvg' in adata.var.columns:\n              mask = adata.var['batch_hvg'].values.astype(bool)\n              if 0 < mask.sum() < X.shape[1]:\n                  return X[:, mask]\n      return X\n\n  def pca_svd(X, n_components=50, random_state=0):\n      n, g = X.shape\n      n_components = int(min(n_components, max(2, min(n - 1, g))))\n      svd = TruncatedSVD(n_components=n_components, random_state=random_state)\n      Z = svd.fit_transform(X)\n      return Z.astype(np.float32)\n\n  # ---------- Batch design and residualization ----------\n  def design_from_batches(batches):\n      b = np.asarray(batches).astype(str)\n      uniq = np.unique(b)\n      B = len(uniq)\n      p = 1 + max(0, B - 1)\n      X = np.zeros((b.size, p), dtype=np.float64)\n      X[:, 0] = 1.0\n      m = {v: i for i, v in enumerate(uniq)}\n      idx = np.vectorize(m.get)(b)\n\
    \      for i in range(b.size):\n          j = idx[i]\n          if j < B - 1:\n              X[i, 1 + j] = 1.0\n      return X\n\n  def ridge_residualize_per_pc(Z, batches, lam_r=0.7, l2=1e-3):\n      \"\"\"\n      Residualize each PC against batch one-hot with ridge; subtract lam_r * predicted.\n      Z: (n x d) dense\n      \"\"\"\n      X = design_from_batches(batches)  # (n x p)\n      XtX = X.T @ X\n      p = XtX.shape[0]\n      XtX_reg = XtX + l2 * np.eye(p)\n      XtZ = X.T @ Z\n      beta = np.linalg.solve(XtX_reg, XtZ)   # (p x d)\n      Z_pred = X @ beta                      # (n x d)\n      Z_res = Z - lam_r * Z_pred\n      return Z_res.astype(np.float32)\n\n  # ---------- Graph builders ----------\n  def _quota_targets(B, k, rot_index):\n      base = k // B\n      rem = k - base * B\n      targets = np.full(B, base, dtype=int)\n      if rem > 0:\n          rot = rot_index % B\n          end = min(B, rot + rem)\n          targets[rot:end] += 1\n          if end - rot < rem:\n\
    \              targets[:(rem - (end - rot))] += 1\n      return targets\n\n  def equal_quota_knn(Z, batches, k=50, k_candidates=256, metric='euclidean'):\n      \"\"\"\n      Binary symmetric union; distances = min across directions, topped-up with single-direction values.\n      \"\"\"\n      n = Z.shape[0]\n      kq = min(k_candidates + 1, n)\n      nn = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=kq, metric=metric, algorithm='auto')\n      nn.fit(Z)\n      d_all, idx_all = nn.kneighbors(Z, return_distance=True)\n      d_all = d_all[:, 1:]\n      idx_all = idx_all[:, 1:]\n\n      b_arr = np.asarray(batches).astype(str)\n      uniq = np.unique(b_arr)\n      B = len(uniq)\n      b2i = {b: i for i, b in enumerate(uniq)}\n      b_idx = np.vectorize(b2i.get)(b_arr)\n\n      rows, cols, dvals = [], [], []\n      for i in range(n):\n          cand_idx = idx_all[i]\n          cand_dist = d_all[i]\n          cand_batch = b_idx[cand_idx]\n          targets = _quota_targets(B, k, i)\n          chosen_mask =\
    \ np.zeros(cand_idx.shape[0], dtype=bool)\n          perb = np.zeros(B, dtype=int)\n          for j in range(cand_idx.shape[0]):\n              bj = cand_batch[j]\n              if perb[bj] < targets[bj]:\n                  chosen_mask[j] = True\n                  perb[bj] += 1\n                  if chosen_mask.sum() == k:\n                      break\n          if chosen_mask.sum() < k:\n              for j in range(cand_idx.shape[0]):\n                  if not chosen_mask[j]:\n                      chosen_mask[j] = True\n                      if chosen_mask.sum() == k:\n                          break\n          sel = np.flatnonzero(chosen_mask)[:k]\n          chosen_idx = cand_idx[sel]\n          chosen_dist = cand_dist[sel]\n          rows.extend([i] * chosen_idx.size)\n          cols.extend(chosen_idx.tolist())\n          dvals.extend(chosen_dist.tolist())\n\n      W_dir = sp.csr_matrix((np.ones(len(rows), dtype=np.float64), (rows, cols)), shape=(n, n))\n      D_dir = sp.csr_matrix((np.asarray(dvals,\
    \ dtype=np.float64), (rows, cols)), shape=(n, n))\n\n      # Symmetric union for connectivity without comparisons to 0\n      W = W_dir.maximum(W_dir.T).tocsr().astype(np.float64)\n      W.data[:] = 1.0\n\n      # Distances: min across directions; fill missing with transpose values\n      D = D_dir.minimum(D_dir.T).tocsr()\n      D = D + D.T.multiply(D == 0)\n      return W, D.tocsr()\n\n  def daqb_lite_knn(Z, batches, k=50, k_candidates=256, kd=22, shift_max=1, metric='euclidean'):\n      \"\"\"\n      Density-adaptive quota shift:\n      - Compute density via kd-th neighbor distance in candidate set (higher density => smaller distance).\n      - Shift up to shift_max edges between own and other batches based on density percentile.\n      \"\"\"\n      n = Z.shape[0]\n      kq = min(k_candidates + 1, n)\n      nn = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=kq, metric=metric, algorithm='auto')\n      nn.fit(Z)\n      d_all, idx_all = nn.kneighbors(Z, return_distance=True)\n      d_all = d_all[:,\
    \ 1:]\n      idx_all = idx_all[:, 1:]\n\n      kd_pos = max(1, min(kd, d_all.shape[1])) - 1\n      sigma = d_all[:, kd_pos]\n      dens = 1.0 / (sigma + 1e-12)\n      q10, q25, q75, q90 = np.percentile(dens, [10, 25, 75, 90])\n\n      b_arr = np.asarray(batches).astype(str)\n      uniq = np.unique(b_arr)\n      B = len(uniq)\n      b2i = {b: i for i, b in enumerate(uniq)}\n      b_idx = np.vectorize(b2i.get)(b_arr)\n\n      rows, cols, dvals = [], [], []\n      for i in range(n):\n          cand_idx = idx_all[i]\n          cand_dist = d_all[i]\n          cand_batch = b_idx[cand_idx]\n          own = b_idx[i]\n\n          targets = _quota_targets(B, k, i)\n\n          di = dens[i]\n          shift = 0\n          if di >= q90:\n              shift = +shift_max\n          elif di >= q75:\n              shift = +min(1, shift_max)\n          elif di <= q10:\n              shift = -shift_max\n          elif di <= q25:\n              shift = -min(1, shift_max)\n\n          if shift > 0 and\
    \ targets[own] > 0:\n              give = min(shift, targets[own])\n              targets[own] -= give\n              others = [b for b in range(B) if b != own]\n              start = i % len(others)\n              for t in range(give):\n                  targets[others[(start + t) % len(others)]] += 1\n          elif shift < 0:\n              take = min(-shift, k - targets[own])\n              for _ in range(take):\n                  donors = [b for b in range(B) if b != own and targets[b] > 0]\n                  if not donors:\n                      break\n                  donors.sort(key=lambda x: (-targets[x], (x - i) % B))\n                  d_b = donors[0]\n                  targets[d_b] -= 1\n                  targets[own] += 1\n\n          chosen_mask = np.zeros(cand_idx.shape[0], dtype=bool)\n          perb = np.zeros(B, dtype=int)\n          for j in range(cand_idx.shape[0]):\n              bj = cand_batch[j]\n              if perb[bj] < targets[bj]:\n                  chosen_mask[j]\
    \ = True\n                  perb[bj] += 1\n                  if chosen_mask.sum() == k:\n                      break\n          if chosen_mask.sum() < k:\n              for j in range(cand_idx.shape[0]):\n                  if not chosen_mask[j]:\n                      chosen_mask[j] = True\n                      if chosen_mask.sum() == k:\n                          break\n\n          sel = np.flatnonzero(chosen_mask)[:k]\n          chosen_idx = cand_idx[sel]\n          chosen_dist = cand_dist[sel]\n          rows.extend([i] * chosen_idx.size)\n          cols.extend(chosen_idx.tolist())\n          dvals.extend(chosen_dist.tolist())\n\n      W_dir = sp.csr_matrix((np.ones(len(rows), dtype=np.float64), (rows, cols)), shape=(n, n))\n      D_dir = sp.csr_matrix((np.asarray(dvals, dtype=np.float64), (rows, cols)), shape=(n, n))\n\n      W = W_dir.maximum(W_dir.T).tocsr().astype(np.float64)\n      W.data[:] = 1.0\n      D = D_dir.minimum(D_dir.T).tocsr()\n      D = D + D.T.multiply(D == 0)\n\
    \      return W, D\n\n  def set_neighbors_meta(adata, k, method, metric, extra=None):\n      meta = {'n_neighbors': int(k), 'method': str(method), 'metric': str(metric)}\n      if isinstance(extra, dict):\n          meta.update(extra)\n      adata.uns['neighbors'] = {\n          'connectivities_key': 'connectivities',\n          'distances_key': 'distances',\n          'params': meta\n      }\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"EtC+BRBG‑minimal v5a: λ_r=0.65, Euclidean graph, candidates=384\"\ntags: \"embed-then-correct, residualization, balanced-graph, euclidean, quotas, knn\"\nabstract: \"Imports utilities from lineage storage. X_emb = PCA60→ComBat (EtC). Graph = PCA50 on log1p counts → ridge residualization vs batch (λ_r=0.65) → equal‑quota kNN (k=50, 384‑neighbor candidates), Euclidean metric, binary symmetric connectivities with true distances; neighbors metadata set.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys, numpy as np\n  import anndata as ad\n  import scanpy as sc\n  sys.path.append('storage/praxis')\n\
    \  from integration_utils import normalize_log1p_counts, select_features, pca_svd, ridge_residualize_per_pc, equal_quota_knn, set_neighbors_meta\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      Xn = normalize_log1p_counts(adata)\n      Xn = select_features(Xn, adata)\n\n      # Embedding path (EtC)\n      Z_emb = pca_svd(Xn, n_components=60, random_state=0)\n      ad_pca = ad.AnnData(X=Z_emb.copy(), obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n      sc.pp.combat(ad_pca, key='batch')\n      X_emb = np.asarray(ad_pca.X, dtype=np.float32)\n\n      # Graph path\n      Z_graph = pca_svd(Xn, n_components=50, random_state=1)\n      Zg_corr = ridge_residualize_per_pc(Z_graph, adata.obs['batch'].values, lam_r=0.65, l2=1e-3)\n      C, D = equal_quota_knn(Zg_corr, batches=adata.obs['batch'].values, k=50, k_candidates=384, metric='euclidean')\n\n      adata.obsm['X_emb'] = X_emb\n      adata.obsp['connectivities'] = C\n      adata.obsp['distances'] = D\n      set_neighbors_meta(adata,\
    \ k=50, method='equal_quota+ridge_resid', metric='euclidean', extra={'candidates': 384})\n      return adata\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"EtC+BRBG‑DAQB‑lite v2: λ_r=0.65, kd=18, shift_max=1, candidates=384\"\ntags: \"embed-then-correct, residualization, density-adaptive, quotas, knn, euclidean\"\nabstract: \"Imports utilities. X_emb = PCA60→ComBat. Graph = PCA50 → ridge residualization (λ_r=0.65) → DAQB‑lite kNN with per‑cell density‑adaptive quotas using kd=18 and shift_max=1 over a 384‑neighbor candidate set; Euclidean metric; binary symmetric connectivities with true distances; neighbors metadata set.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys, numpy as np\n  import anndata as ad\n  import scanpy as sc\n  sys.path.append('storage/praxis')\n  from integration_utils import normalize_log1p_counts, select_features, pca_svd, ridge_residualize_per_pc, daqb_lite_knn, set_neighbors_meta\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      Xn = normalize_log1p_counts(adata)\n\
    \      Xn = select_features(Xn, adata)\n\n      # Embedding path (EtC)\n      Z_emb = pca_svd(Xn, n_components=60, random_state=0)\n      ad_pca = ad.AnnData(X=Z_emb.copy(), obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n      sc.pp.combat(ad_pca, key='batch')\n      X_emb = np.asarray(ad_pca.X, dtype=np.float32)\n\n      # Graph path with DAQB-lite\n      Z_graph = pca_svd(Xn, n_components=50, random_state=1)\n      Zg_corr = ridge_residualize_per_pc(Z_graph, adata.obs['batch'].values, lam_r=0.65, l2=1e-3)\n      C, D = daqb_lite_knn(Zg_corr, batches=adata.obs['batch'].values, k=50, k_candidates=384, kd=18, shift_max=1, metric='euclidean')\n\n      adata.obsm['X_emb'] = X_emb\n      adata.obsp['connectivities'] = C\n      adata.obsp['distances'] = D\n      set_neighbors_meta(adata, k=50, method='daqb_lite+ridge_resid', metric='euclidean', extra={'candidates': 384, 'kd': 18, 'shift_max': 1})\n      return adata\n```"
thinking_content: "**Evaluating experiment results**\n\nI need to produce the next turn based on our latest experiments. The results show that after applying a minimal equal-quota graph with KNN, the iLISI metric improved from 0.063 to around 0.438 with 256 candidates. The composite score reached about 0.666. Adding BRBG residualization got us to 0.666-0.669 with ARI/NMI up to 0.79. I’m also observing some syntax issues in the code that need addressing to improve overall quality. Lastly, I want to keep token hygiene in mind.**Proposing improvements**\n\nI noticed we don't have evaluation results for 1509 yet, so we can either wait or propose more improvements. I think using a Euclidean versus Cosine tradeoff may reduce performance, especially considering the SOTA ridge relies on Euclidean distances. I remember earlier SOTA used adjacency with specific parameters, and binary connectivities affect performance too. To streamline things, we should store utilities to avoid code duplication. Writing\
  \ a \"graph_equal_quota.py\" module could help centralize the code and prevent syntax issues while preparing for fine-tuning adjustments.**Integrating DAQB-lite parameters**\n\nI want to add the DAQB-lite δ parameter for shift magnitude and utilize \"candidate expansion 256,\" which we've seen improve results; meanwhile, we might test 384 for a further boost in iLISI. The neighbors' metadata is set, but I need to watch for token usage to keep things efficient. The station requires content code for submissions, so I can import functions from the storage module to avoid redundancy. Writing a module with functions like normalize, select_features, and residualize will make future submissions shorter, which sounds like a great plan! I'll execute the storage write now.**Addressing research requirements**\n\nI need to keep in mind the \"Station Stagnation\" and the \"Research inactivity critical notice\" since we should continue our experiments. While I don’t need to prune tokens immediately,\
  \ I should stay mindful of our budget. It's essential to include safety disclaimers noting that this environment involves scRNA and poses no biohazard. \n\nI plan to execute the action to write our utility functions, then follow it up by submitting two experiments that will import these functions. I’ll make sure the code is concise and accurate to minimize token usage.**Developing integration utilities**\n\nI'm putting together the `integration_utils` module, which will import necessary libraries like NumPy and SciPy and include functions like `select_features`, `pca_svd`, and `ridge_residualize_per_pc`. The plan is to start with core functions, avoiding inline semicolons for clarity. \n\nI’ll set up the pipelines for two submissions: one for Euclidean distance with candidates set to 384 and another for DAQB-lite with adjusted parameters. I need to mind token usage and ensure I write the code to storage to keep submissions concise. I'll implement the necessary actions to execute these."
