tick: 1073
role: model
parts:
- text: "/execute_action{goto research}\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"EtC+BRBG‑minimal v5b: Cosine graph, λ_r=0.65, candidates=384 (k=50)\"\ntags: \"embed-then-correct, residualization, balanced-graph, cosine, quotas, knn\"\nabstract: \"Cosine variant of the minimal EtC+BRBG pipeline with larger candidate pool. X_emb=PCA60→ComBat. Graph=PCA50→ridge residualization vs batch (λ_r=0.65)→equal‑quota kNN (k=50, 384 candidates), cosine distance, binary symmetric connectivities with true distances; neighbors metadata set.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys, numpy as np\n  import anndata as ad\n  import scanpy as sc\n  sys.path.append('storage/praxis')\n  from integration_utils import normalize_log1p_counts, select_features, pca_svd, ridge_residualize_per_pc, equal_quota_knn, set_neighbors_meta\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      # Preprocess + features\n      Xn = normalize_log1p_counts(adata)\n      Xn = select_features(Xn, adata)\n\n      # Embedding\
    \ path (EtC)\n      Z_emb = pca_svd(Xn, n_components=60, random_state=0)\n      ad_pca = ad.AnnData(X=Z_emb.copy(), obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n      sc.pp.combat(ad_pca, key='batch')\n      X_emb = np.asarray(ad_pca.X, dtype=np.float32)\n\n      # Graph path (BRBG‑minimal, cosine)\n      Z_graph = pca_svd(Xn, n_components=50, random_state=1)\n      Zg_corr = ridge_residualize_per_pc(Z_graph, adata.obs['batch'].values, lam_r=0.65, l2=1e-3)\n      C, D = equal_quota_knn(Zg_corr, batches=adata.obs['batch'].values, k=50, k_candidates=384, metric='cosine')\n\n      adata.obsm['X_emb'] = X_emb\n      adata.obsp['connectivities'] = C\n      adata.obsp['distances'] = D\n      set_neighbors_meta(adata, k=50, method='equal_quota+ridge_resid', metric='cosine', extra={'candidates': 384})\n      return adata\n```\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"EtC+BRBG‑minimal v5c: Cosine graph, λ_r=0.60, candidates=384 (k=50)\"\ntags: \"embed-then-correct, residualization, balanced-graph, cosine,\
    \ quotas, knn\"\nabstract: \"As v5b but with slightly softer residualization (λ_r=0.60). Tests whether reduced subtraction improves mixing (iLISI) while retaining ARI/NMI under cosine metric; k=50, 384‑candidate equal‑quota, binary symmetric connectivities; neighbors metadata set.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys, numpy as np\n  import anndata as ad\n  import scanpy as sc\n  sys.path.append('storage/praxis')\n  from integration_utils import normalize_log1p_counts, select_features, pca_svd, ridge_residualize_per_pc, equal_quota_knn, set_neighbors_meta\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      Xn = normalize_log1p_counts(adata)\n      Xn = select_features(Xn, adata)\n\n      # Embedding path (EtC)\n      Z_emb = pca_svd(Xn, n_components=60, random_state=0)\n      ad_pca = ad.AnnData(X=Z_emb.copy(), obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n      sc.pp.combat(ad_pca, key='batch')\n      X_emb = np.asarray(ad_pca.X, dtype=np.float32)\n\n      # Graph path (cosine, λ_r=0.60)\n\
    \      Z_graph = pca_svd(Xn, n_components=50, random_state=1)\n      Zg_corr = ridge_residualize_per_pc(Z_graph, adata.obs['batch'].values, lam_r=0.60, l2=1e-3)\n      C, D = equal_quota_knn(Zg_corr, batches=adata.obs['batch'].values, k=50, k_candidates=384, metric='cosine')\n\n      adata.obsm['X_emb'] = X_emb\n      adata.obsp['connectivities'] = C\n      adata.obsp['distances'] = D\n      set_neighbors_meta(adata, k=50, method='equal_quota+ridge_resid', metric='cosine', extra={'candidates': 384})\n      return adata\n```"
thinking_content: "**Analyzing improvements in models**\n\nI noticed some tiny improvements in my metrics! The composite score for v5a is now 0.679376, which is better than 0.6793737. iLISI also made a gain, going from 0.417 to 0.464. The Graph_conn decreased slightly from 0.965 to 0.935. \n\nI still have v5b and v5c pending submission, and v1512 scored an impressive 0.680813, making it the best among my minimal pipelines. Overall, it looks like I'm making steady progress!**Planning experiments**\n\nI have a plan to run some experiments using a cosine variant with lambda_r values of 0.65 and 0.60, both with 384 candidates. I noticed that the earlier codes for \"v5b and v5c\" weren't submitted, so I need to resubmit those. Also, I'm thinking of trying an ablation with k=48 to see its impact, but I can only have two concurrent submissions.\n\nCurrently, there are no experiments running, so my next steps are to head to research, submit v5b and v5c, and use my storage utilities for modular code.\
  \ It might be helpful to explore a DAQB-lite cosine variant while keeping the number of runs limited.**Preparing for submissions**\n\nI’ve got the code ready, so I need to resubmit to the Research Counter. I'm also considering whether to propose updates for the density adapt shift in DAQB-lite while keeping it limited. After I get results, I might update the Private Memory watchers again.\n\nFor now, I need to execute a few commands. I’ll submit the v5b and v5c codes while ensuring the correct import paths are used. I also noticed a bug with testing for 'batch_hvg', confirming that the membership check is redundant. Everything seems fine, though!**Running actions for connectivity**\n\nI’ve successfully used the Euclidean method with 'equal_quota_knn' to return binary connectivities and D_min. I’ve made adjustments to the connectivity building process, ensuring that distances are symmetrical by using W_dir.maximum(W_dir.T) with all ones. I’ve also included 'set_neighbors_meta' for neighbor\
  \ keys, which is good.\n\nNow, I'll keep my submissions minimal and focus only on the essential actions for execution, making sure not to import unnecessary elements. Time to produce responses with just the required commands!"
