tick: 1075
role: model
parts:
- text: "/execute_action{goto research}\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"EtC+BRBG‑minimal v5b‑k48: Cosine graph, λ_r=0.65, candidates=384 (k=48)\"\ntags: \"embed-then-correct, residualization, balanced-graph, cosine, quotas, knn\"\nabstract: \"Cosine variant with k=48. X_emb=PCA60→ComBat. Graph=PCA50→ridge residualization vs batch (λ_r=0.65)→equal‑quota kNN (k=48, 384 candidates), cosine distance, binary symmetric connectivities with true distances; neighbors metadata set.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys, numpy as np\n  import anndata as ad\n  import scanpy as sc\n  sys.path.append('storage/praxis')\n  from integration_utils import normalize_log1p_counts, select_features, pca_svd, ridge_residualize_per_pc, equal_quota_knn, set_neighbors_meta\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      Xn = normalize_log1p_counts(adata)\n      Xn = select_features(Xn, adata)\n\n      # Embedding (EtC)\n      Z_emb = pca_svd(Xn, n_components=60, random_state=0)\n  \
    \    ad_pca = ad.AnnData(X=Z_emb.copy(), obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n      sc.pp.combat(ad_pca, key='batch')\n      X_emb = np.asarray(ad_pca.X, dtype=np.float32)\n\n      # Graph (cosine, k=48)\n      Z_graph = pca_svd(Xn, n_components=50, random_state=1)\n      Zg_corr = ridge_residualize_per_pc(Z_graph, adata.obs['batch'].values, lam_r=0.65, l2=1e-3)\n      C, D = equal_quota_knn(Zg_corr, batches=adata.obs['batch'].values, k=48, k_candidates=384, metric='cosine')\n\n      adata.obsm['X_emb'] = X_emb\n      adata.obsp['connectivities'] = C\n      adata.obsp['distances'] = D\n      set_neighbors_meta(adata, k=48, method='equal_quota+ridge_resid', metric='cosine', extra={'candidates': 384})\n      return adata\n```\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"EtC+BRBG‑DAQB‑lite v3: Cosine graph, λ_r=0.65, kd=18, shift_max=1, candidates=384 (k=50)\"\ntags: \"embed-then-correct, residualization, density-adaptive, quotas, cosine, knn\"\nabstract: \"Cosine DAQB‑lite variant. X_emb=PCA60→ComBat.\
    \ Graph=PCA50→ridge residualization (λ_r=0.65)→DAQB‑lite kNN (k=50, 384 candidates) with density‑adaptive quota shifts (kd=18, shift_max=1); binary symmetric connectivities with true distances; neighbors metadata set.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys, numpy as np\n  import anndata as ad\n  import scanpy as sc\n  sys.path.append('storage/praxis')\n  from integration_utils import normalize_log1p_counts, select_features, pca_svd, ridge_residualize_per_pc, daqb_lite_knn, set_neighbors_meta\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      Xn = normalize_log1p_counts(adata)\n      Xn = select_features(Xn, adata)\n\n      # Embedding (EtC)\n      Z_emb = pca_svd(Xn, n_components=60, random_state=0)\n      ad_pca = ad.AnnData(X=Z_emb.copy(), obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n      sc.pp.combat(ad_pca, key='batch')\n      X_emb = np.asarray(ad_pca.X, dtype=np.float32)\n\n      # Graph (cosine DAQB‑lite)\n      Z_graph = pca_svd(Xn, n_components=50, random_state=1)\n    \
    \  Zg_corr = ridge_residualize_per_pc(Z_graph, adata.obs['batch'].values, lam_r=0.65, l2=1e-3)\n      C, D = daqb_lite_knn(Zg_corr, batches=adata.obs['batch'].values, k=50, k_candidates=384, kd=18, shift_max=1, metric='cosine')\n\n      adata.obsm['X_emb'] = X_emb\n      adata.obsp['connectivities'] = C\n      adata.obsp['distances'] = D\n      set_neighbors_meta(adata, k=50, method='daqb_lite+ridge_resid', metric='cosine', extra={'candidates': 384, 'kd': 18, 'shift_max': 1})\n      return adata\n```"
thinking_content: "**Considering code integration**\n\nI have a storage module, integration_utils.py, that I can reuse for coding tasks, which is great. I want to keep running experiments while also making sure I'm maintaining token hygiene. \n\nI need to issue some actions: First, I should go to research to submit new experiments, but I might want to navigate through token management first. \n\nNext, I’ll submit equal_quota_knn with cosine using k=48 to see if it improves performance, especially since previous ablations showed k=49 was ineffective.**Planning experiments submission**\n\nI need to submit two experiments: v5b-k48 with lambda 0.65, and v5c-k48 with lambda 0.60. There’s also an option to test DAQB-lite with cosine, using KD=18 and shift=1, since it might improve mixing based on earlier results with Euclidean.\n\nAdditionally, I want to adjust k_candidates to 512, although we previously used 384. Testing 512 could be heavy, but it should fit within the 30-minute limit. I should\
  \ remember we can only run two evaluations at a time, and right now, it seems we have none running.**Formulating submission actions**\n\nAt tick 1075, we're in Token Management and can submit two new evaluations after evaluating v5b and v5c. So, I’ll submit: 1) v5b_k48, which uses cosine with lambda 0.65 and k=48, and 2) v5d_daqb_cosine for the DAQB-lite model with cosine, kd=18, and shift=1.\n\nSince we can run only two evaluations at a time, I need to prioritize. I could also update the private memory watchlist and record any changes. I can simplify the submission process by importing utilities for equal_quota_knn and daqb_lite_knn.**Defining and submitting functions**\n\nI need to define the eliminate_batch_effect_fn again, specifically with the k=48 variation. \n\nFor the submission, I'll go with DAQB-lite using cosine. To keep token usage low, I won’t repeat the full functions but will include a minimal code block that references the storage/praxis module properly. Also, I’ll add\
  \ the neighbor metadata we've set up in the utils.\n\nIt's probably unnecessary to include no_debugger. I’ll note that \"Results show cosine > euclidean,\" and mention that softening residualization to 0.60 improved iLISI. I'll make sure the YAML tags are concise and consistent to avoid heavy token usage.**Crafting submission code**\n\nI’m going to write the code for v5b_k48. I’ll start by importing necessary libraries like sys, numpy, anndata, and scanpy. Then, I’ll use the integration_utils functions. Inside the function, I’ll perform Xn normalization and selection, keeping the embedding and graph paths the same. I’ll set up PCA with 50 components and residualize using ridge with lambda 0.65, followed by equal_quota_knn with k=48 and metric='cosine'.\n\nFor the DAQB-lite variant, I'll use daqb_lite_knn, setting kd to 18 or possibly 22. I’ll finalize the plan without pruning since we've already pruned."
