thinking_content: "**Managing experiments and tokens**\n\nI'm considering running more experiments, but I hit the limit of two concurrent evaluations. Since I already have two running, I can't submit more until they complete, because it would just queue up. I could either write some code or test a function, or maybe prune some tokens since I'm at 103k out of 270k. There's also the option to summarize a minimal path with a Private Memory capsule. I'll need to manage these tokens effectively and check my cooldown status.**Evaluating cooldown and updates**\n\nAt 1077, I might still have one tick left in cooldown, so it's probably safer to avoid pruning attempts on ticks 1070-1073. I could check the Archive for pinned items #49 or #50, but that doesn’t seem crucial right now. The previous \"Station Inactivity\" warning is now resolved with active experiments. I can update the meta to reflect minimal pipeline results and work on code improvements for efficiency. Also, I might want to add a function\
  \ for candidate 'cosine' weighted features to normalize rows effectively.**Considering distance metrics and enhancements**\n\nSklearn's 'cosine' metric operates using 1 - cosine similarity, which does normalize but may compute using normalized dot products without needing pre-normalization. However, pre-normalizing could improve speed a bit. Another idea is implementing symmetrical union distances more robustly in the equal_quota_knn. We set W = max(W_dir, W_dir.T), ensuring symmetrical representations. I’m also thinking about adding row normalization to connectivities. Lastly, we may improve kBET and iLISI by increasing the candidate pool and adjusting quotas, all while planning to review running EIDs post-completion.**Planning review actions**\n\nI'm unsure if the process has finished, but I can still issue review actions since the station will indicate pending status or show results. I could go to research or review the results for 1527/1528. If one of those is better, I might then\
  \ propose synergy between kd=22 shift=1 versus kd=18. While it's still running, I’ll monitor via \"rank id\" or \"rank score.\" I can also update meta, prepare a Private Memory note summarizing results, and pin capsule #48. I'll remember to keep my responses concise!**Executing research plan**\n\nMy plan is to go to the Research Counter and try to review experiments 1527 and 1528. If they're pending, that's fine; if not, we'll see the results. Since we can't submit more due to concurrency, after the review, we can schedule to run v5b with candidates=512 if slots free up. It could help iLISI improve. \n\nI'll also prepare commands like reviewing the actions, ranking items, and writing a new function for cosine row-normalization, all while keeping code minimal. Let's move ahead with the actions!"
