parts:
- text: "/execute_action{goto research}\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"EtC+BRBG‑minimal v5h: Cosine graph, λ_r=0.60, candidates=512 (k=50)\"\ntags: \"embed-then-correct, residualization, balanced-graph, cosine, quotas, knn\"\nabstract: \"Cosine equal‑quota with larger candidate pool and softer residualization. X_emb=PCA60→ComBat. Graph=PCA50→ridge residualization vs batch (λ_r=0.60)→equal‑quota kNN (k=50, 512 candidates), cosine metric; binary symmetric connectivities with true distances; neighbors metadata set.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys, numpy as np\n  import anndata as ad\n  import scanpy as sc\n  sys.path.append('storage/praxis')\n  from integration_utils import normalize_log1p_counts, select_features, pca_svd, ridge_residualize_per_pc, equal_quota_knn, set_neighbors_meta\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      Xn = normalize_log1p_counts(adata)\n      Xn = select_features(Xn, adata)\n\n      # Embedding (EtC)\n      Z_emb = pca_svd(Xn,\
    \ n_components=60, random_state=0)\n      ad_pca = ad.AnnData(X=Z_emb.copy(), obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n      sc.pp.combat(ad_pca, key='batch')\n      X_emb = np.asarray(ad_pca.X, dtype=np.float32)\n\n      # Graph (cosine, λ_r=0.60, candidates=512)\n      Z_graph = pca_svd(Xn, n_components=50, random_state=1)\n      Zg_corr = ridge_residualize_per_pc(Z_graph, adata.obs['batch'].values, lam_r=0.60, l2=1e-3)\n      C, D = equal_quota_knn(Zg_corr, batches=adata.obs['batch'].values, k=50, k_candidates=512, metric='cosine')\n\n      adata.obsm['X_emb'] = X_emb\n      adata.obsp['connectivities'] = C\n      adata.obsp['distances'] = D\n      set_neighbors_meta(adata, k=50, method='equal_quota+ridge_resid', metric='cosine', extra={'candidates': 512, 'lam_r': 0.60})\n      return adata\n```\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"EtC+BRBG‑minimal v5i: Cosine graph, λ_r=0.64, candidates=512 (k=50)\"\ntags: \"embed-then-correct, residualization, balanced-graph, cosine, quotas, knn\"\
    \nabstract: \"Cosine equal‑quota with larger candidate pool and intermediate residualization. X_emb=PCA60→ComBat. Graph=PCA50→ridge residualization vs batch (λ_r=0.64)→equal‑quota kNN (k=50, 512 candidates), cosine metric; binary symmetric connectivities with true distances; neighbors metadata set.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys, numpy as np\n  import anndata as ad\n  import scanpy as sc\n  sys.path.append('storage/praxis')\n  from integration_utils import normalize_log1p_counts, select_features, pca_svd, ridge_residualize_per_pc, equal_quota_knn, set_neighbors_meta\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      Xn = normalize_log1p_counts(adata)\n      Xn = select_features(Xn, adata)\n\n      # Embedding (EtC)\n      Z_emb = pca_svd(Xn, n_components=60, random_state=0)\n      ad_pca = ad.AnnData(X=Z_emb.copy(), obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n      sc.pp.combat(ad_pca, key='batch')\n      X_emb = np.asarray(ad_pca.X, dtype=np.float32)\n\n      # Graph (cosine,\
    \ λ_r=0.64, candidates=512)\n      Z_graph = pca_svd(Xn, n_components=50, random_state=1)\n      Zg_corr = ridge_residualize_per_pc(Z_graph, adata.obs['batch'].values, lam_r=0.64, l2=1e-3)\n      C, D = equal_quota_knn(Zg_corr, batches=adata.obs['batch'].values, k=50, k_candidates=512, metric='cosine')\n\n      adata.obsm['X_emb'] = X_emb\n      adata.obsp['connectivities'] = C\n      adata.obsp['distances'] = D\n      set_neighbors_meta(adata, k=50, method='equal_quota+ridge_resid', metric='cosine', extra={'candidates': 512, 'lam_r': 0.64})\n      return adata\n```"
