parts:
- text: "/execute_action{goto research}\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"EtC+BRBG‑minimal v6e: ACP v3 favor_sparse (λ_r=0.64, k=50, kd=22, kq 256→768, cosine)\"\ntags: \"embed-then-correct, residualization, balanced-graph, cosine, adaptive-candidates, quotas\"\nabstract: \"Adaptive-candidate equal‑quota v3 (no padding; rotated remainders) allocating larger candidate pools to sparse regions (σ_kd large). Tests λ_r=0.64 with k=50, kd=22, kq∈[256,768] under cosine; compares to fixed kq=512/768 baselines.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys, numpy as np\n  import anndata as ad\n  import scanpy as sc\n  sys.path.append('storage/praxis')\n  from integration_utils import normalize_log1p_counts, select_features, pca_svd, ridge_residualize_per_pc, set_neighbors_meta\n  from eq_adaptive import equal_quota_knn_adaptive_kq_v3\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      # Preprocess\n      Xn = normalize_log1p_counts(adata)\n      Xn = select_features(Xn, adata)\n\
    \n      # Embedding (EtC: PCA60 -> ComBat)\n      Z_emb = pca_svd(Xn, n_components=60, random_state=0)\n      ad_pca = ad.AnnData(X=Z_emb.copy(), obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n      sc.pp.combat(ad_pca, key='batch')\n      X_emb = np.asarray(ad_pca.X, dtype=np.float32)\n\n      # Graph (BRBG-minimal on PCs; cosine eq-quota with ACP v3 favor_sparse)\n      Zg = pca_svd(Xn, n_components=50, random_state=1)\n      Zg_corr = ridge_residualize_per_pc(Zg, adata.obs['batch'].values, lam_r=0.64, l2=1e-3)\n      C, D = equal_quota_knn_adaptive_kq_v3(\n          Zg_corr, batches=adata.obs['batch'].values,\n          k=50, kq_min=256, kq_max=768, kd=22, metric='cosine',\n          mapping='favor_sparse', remainder_mode='rotate'\n      )\n\n      adata.obsm['X_emb'] = X_emb\n      adata.obsp['connectivities'] = C\n      adata.obsp['distances'] = D\n      set_neighbors_meta(adata, k=50, method='eq_quota_acp_v3_sparse+ridge_resid',\n                         metric='cosine', extra={'kq_min':256,\
    \ 'kq_max':768, 'kd':22, 'lam_r':0.64})\n      return adata\n```\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"EtC+BRBG‑minimal v6f: ACP v3 favor_sparse (λ_r=0.62, k=50, kd=22, kq 256→768, cosine)\"\ntags: \"embed-then-correct, residualization, balanced-graph, cosine, adaptive-candidates, quotas\"\nabstract: \"Same as v6e but with λ_r=0.62 to probe residualization–mixing balance under ACP v3 favor_sparse. Expect iLISI ≥ fixed kq=512 and composite ≥ 0.6969 if ACP mapping is correct.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys, numpy as np\n  import anndata as ad\n  import scanpy as sc\n  sys.path.append('storage/praxis')\n  from integration_utils import normalize_log1p_counts, select_features, pca_svd, ridge_residualize_per_pc, set_neighbors_meta\n  from eq_adaptive import equal_quota_knn_adaptive_kq_v3\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      Xn = normalize_log1p_counts(adata)\n      Xn = select_features(Xn, adata)\n\n      Z_emb = pca_svd(Xn, n_components=60, random_state=0)\n\
    \      ad_pca = ad.AnnData(X=Z_emb.copy(), obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n      sc.pp.combat(ad_pca, key='batch')\n      X_emb = np.asarray(ad_pca.X, dtype=np.float32)\n\n      Zg = pca_svd(Xn, n_components=50, random_state=1)\n      Zg_corr = ridge_residualize_per_pc(Zg, adata.obs['batch'].values, lam_r=0.62, l2=1e-3)\n      C, D = equal_quota_knn_adaptive_kq_v3(\n          Zg_corr, batches=adata.obs['batch'].values,\n          k=50, kq_min=256, kq_max=768, kd=22, metric='cosine',\n          mapping='favor_sparse', remainder_mode='rotate'\n      )\n\n      adata.obsm['X_emb'] = X_emb\n      adata.obsp['connectivities'] = C\n      adata.obsp['distances'] = D\n      set_neighbors_meta(adata, k=50, method='eq_quota_acp_v3_sparse+ridge_resid',\n                         metric='cosine', extra={'kq_min':256, 'kq_max':768, 'kd':22, 'lam_r':0.62})\n      return adata\n```"
thinking_content: '**Evaluating YAML Title Formatting**


  I need to keep my code minimal yet functional. I have to consider if using special characters like ''→'' or ''–'' in the ''title'' string is okay. However, I realize that for YAML, special characters like colons require quoting. Since the title includes a colon after ''kq 256→768, kd=22'', I should ensure that the ''title'' field is quoted. I guess quoting it will be the right way to handle this! Now, let’s produce the actions.'
