parts:
- text: "/execute_action{goto research}\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"EtC+BRBG‑minimal v5l: Cosine eq‑quota, rotated remainders (λ_r=0.64, k=50, kq=896)\"\ntags: \"embed-then-correct, residualization, balanced-graph, cosine, quotas\"\nabstract: \"Fixed-candidate cosine equal‑quota graph with rotated remainder allocation; larger candidate pool (kq=896). Embedding: PCA60→ComBat. Graph PCs: PCA50→ridge residualization (λ_r=0.64). Binary symmetric connectivities with true distances; neighbors metadata set.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys, numpy as np\n  import anndata as ad\n  import scanpy as sc\n  sys.path.append('storage/praxis')\n  from integration_utils import normalize_log1p_counts, select_features, pca_svd, ridge_residualize_per_pc, set_neighbors_meta\n  from eq_quota_utils import eq_quota_knn_cosine\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      # Preprocess + HVGs\n      Xn = normalize_log1p_counts(adata)\n      Xn = select_features(Xn, adata)\n\
    \n      # Embedding (EtC)\n      Z_emb = pca_svd(Xn, n_components=60, random_state=0)\n      ad_pca = ad.AnnData(X=Z_emb.copy(), obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n      sc.pp.combat(ad_pca, key='batch')\n      X_emb = np.asarray(ad_pca.X, dtype=np.float32)\n\n      # Graph (cosine eq‑quota, kq=896, rotated remainders)\n      Zg = pca_svd(Xn, n_components=50, random_state=1)\n      Zg_corr = ridge_residualize_per_pc(Zg, adata.obs['batch'].values, lam_r=0.64, l2=1e-3)\n      C, D = eq_quota_knn_cosine(\n          Zg_corr, batches=adata.obs['batch'].values,\n          k=50, k_candidates=896, metric='cosine', remainder_mode='rotate'\n      )\n\n      adata.obsm['X_emb'] = X_emb\n      adata.obsp['connectivities'] = C\n      adata.obsp['distances'] = D\n      set_neighbors_meta(adata, k=50, method='eq_quota_rotated+ridge_resid', metric='cosine',\n                         extra={'k_candidates': 896, 'lam_r': 0.64})\n      return adata\n```\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"EtC+BRBG‑minimal\
    \ v5m: Cosine eq‑quota, rotated remainders (λ_r=0.64, k=50, kq=1024)\"\ntags: \"embed-then-correct, residualization, balanced-graph, cosine, quotas\"\nabstract: \"As v5l but with an even larger candidate pool (kq=1024) to test iLISI/Graph_conn sensitivity at fixed k and λ_r. Uses rotated remainders to avoid batch bias at k=50.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys, numpy as np\n  import anndata as ad\n  import scanpy as sc\n  sys.path.append('storage/praxis')\n  from integration_utils import normalize_log1p_counts, select_features, pca_svd, ridge_residualize_per_pc, set_neighbors_meta\n  from eq_quota_utils import eq_quota_knn_cosine\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      Xn = normalize_log1p_counts(adata)\n      Xn = select_features(Xn, adata)\n\n      Z_emb = pca_svd(Xn, n_components=60, random_state=0)\n      ad_pca = ad.AnnData(X=Z_emb.copy(), obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n      sc.pp.combat(ad_pca, key='batch')\n      X_emb = np.asarray(ad_pca.X, dtype=np.float32)\n\
    \n      Zg = pca_svd(Xn, n_components=50, random_state=1)\n      Zg_corr = ridge_residualize_per_pc(Zg, adata.obs['batch'].values, lam_r=0.64, l2=1e-3)\n      C, D = eq_quota_knn_cosine(\n          Zg_corr, batches=adata.obs['batch'].values,\n          k=50, k_candidates=1024, metric='cosine', remainder_mode='rotate'\n      )\n\n      adata.obsm['X_emb'] = X_emb\n      adata.obsp['connectivities'] = C\n      adata.obsp['distances'] = D\n      set_neighbors_meta(adata, k=50, method='eq_quota_rotated+ridge_resid', metric='cosine',\n                         extra={'k_candidates': 1024, 'lam_r': 0.64})\n      return adata\n```"
thinking_content: "**Evaluating ARI results**\n\nI've noticed that the ARI decreased from 0.794 to 0.789, still off from the top score of 0.746. I'm thinking we should consolidate our efforts by submitting two more tests: v5l and v5m, to see if that boosts the iLISI further. Testing \"front\" versus \"rotate\" mode is also on my mind for fairness—though \"rotate\" seems solid. I wonder if incorporating a \"min mutual check\" could help manage long-tail edges. It’s also worth trying PCA adjustments while keeping an eye on concurrency. We should update our plan, but that’s not urgent.**Optimizing token hygiene**\n\nI need to keep my code concise, but luckily, I can reuse the eq_quota_utils we wrote earlier. I plan to submit two new entries: v5l with kq=896 and v5m with kq=1024. I have to ensure that the k_candidates is set correctly for both; caution is needed with 1024 neighbors across 20k cells. It seems like adjusting lam_r around 0.64 might work best, based on previous results. I’ll also\
  \ aim to ensure the composite improves above 0.7007, while document watchers. Now, let’s code those submissions!**Preparing submissions**\n\nI’m considering including a minimal track plan in the meta prompt, but it’s optional. I could also prune the conversation, although the cooldown is unknown. The last prune was done earlier, so it might not be necessary. I’ll just submit the two entries for now. \n\nI need to ensure that if we can't run more than two concurrently, we should check that none are running—good news, there aren't any. \n\nI’ll include the following commands and structure the YAML neatly while keeping the code minimal."
