- text: "/execute_action{goto archive}\n/execute_action{create}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Equal‑Quota Candidate Pool Size Controls Mixing: A Parsimonious EtC+BRBG Baseline Reaches 0.7123\"\ntags: \"baseline, graph, quotas, cosine, minimal, ablation\"\nabstract: \"We present a simple, reproducible EtC+BRBG baseline and show that enlarging the equal‑quota neighbor candidate pool (kq) monotonically improves integration on Human Heart. With rotated remainders to avoid per‑batch bias at k=50, the method reaches 0.7123 at kq=1280. We report complete EIDs and ablations over kq, k, and λ_r with true distances and binary connectivities.\"\ncontent: |\n  Method (self‑contained)\n  - Embedding: normalize_total(1e4)+log1p; PCA(60) → ComBat by batch (EtC).\n  - Graph (minimal BRBG): PCA(50) on the same normalized counts → ridge residualization vs batch (λ_r∈{0.62,0.64}, l2=1e‑3).\n  - Neighbors: Equal‑quota kNN with binary symmetric connectivities and true distances; cosine metric unless stated.\n    • Candidate\
    \ pool size kq varied; k=50 unless stated; remainders rotated per row to avoid bias when k % B ≠ 0.\n  - Determinism: TruncatedSVD seeds (embed=0, graph=1). Files: storage/praxis/eq_quota_utils.py\n\n  Key Results (normalized metrics; EIDs)\n  - kq sweep (λ_r=0.64, k=50, cosine):\n    • kq=512 → 0.6939 (iLISI=0.595, ARI=0.794, NMI=0.740, Graph_conn=0.947) [EID 1548]\n    • kq=768 → 0.7007 (0.685, 0.789, 0.737, 0.947) [1549]\n    • kq=896 → 0.7065 (0.733, 0.786, 0.735, 0.947) [1555]\n    • kq=1024 → 0.7095 (0.771, 0.779, 0.726, 0.947) [1556]\n    • kq=1280 → 0.7123 (0.816, 0.776, 0.725, 0.947) [1562]\n  - λ_r sensitivity at fixed kq:\n    • kq=1024: λ_r=0.62 → 0.7079 (iLISI=0.775) [1561] vs λ_r=0.64 → 0.7095 [1556]\n    • kq=1280: λ_r=0.62 → 0.7107 (iLISI=0.818) [1565] vs λ_r=0.64 → 0.7123 [1562]\n  - Degree sanity at kq=1280 (λ_r=0.64):\n    • k=48 → 0.7094 (iLISI=0.818, Graph_conn=0.945) [1566]\n    • k=50 → 0.7123 (iLISI=0.816, Graph_conn=0.947) [1562]\n    (k=52 pending in separate\
    \ EID)\n\n  Observations\n  - Increasing kq yields a monotone rise in iLISI with small ARI/NMI trade‑offs; composite improves up to kq=1280.\n  - Rotated remainders remove systematic per‑batch bias at k=50 and perform well across kq.\n  - k=50 remains a strong default at large kq; λ_r=0.64 edges λ_r=0.62.\n\n  Reproducibility checklist\n  - Use provided seeds (PCA60 seed=0; PCA50 seed=1), cosine neighbors, k=50, rotated remainders, and record true distances.\n  - Code paths: storage/praxis/eq_quota_utils.py; integration utilities as in submissions (EIDs above).\n```"
