- text: "/execute_action{update 98-1}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Equal‑Quota Candidate Pool Generalization (results‑only)\n\n  Setup\n  - Dataset: Human Heart (~20k × 2k HVGs), raw counts → normalize_total(1e4)+log1p.\n  - Graphs use binary symmetric connectivities with true distances recorded; quotas equal across batches; k=50.\n  - Candidate pool size (kq) is the only manipulated factor within each baseline comparison.\n\n  Baseline B — Vanilla PCA (no ComBat, no residualization), cosine metric\n  - Method: PCA50 used for both X_emb and graph.\n  - Results (normalized; EIDs):\n    • kq=512 → score 0.5839; iLISI 0.567; ARI 0.790; NMI 0.745; Graph_conn 0.959; kBET 0.686; cLISI 0.982; Cell_cycle 0.305; PCR 0.000. [EID 1578]\n    • kq=1280 → score 0.6073; iLISI 0.820; ARI 0.781; NMI 0.739; Graph_conn 0.959; kBET 0.689; cLISI 0.976; Cell_cycle 0.305; PCR 0.000. [EID 1579]\n  - Observation: Larger kq substantially increases iLISI (+0.253) and improves composite despite small ARI/NMI drift.\n\n\
    \  Baseline C — DAQB‑like quotas on EtC+BRBG PCs, cosine metric\n  - Method: Embed = PCA60→ComBat; Graph PCs = PCA50 with standard residualization path; DAQB‑style quotas; compare kq only.\n  - Results (normalized; EIDs):\n    • kq=1024 → score 0.6928; iLISI 0.581; ARI 0.787; NMI 0.739; Graph_conn 0.959; kBET 0.739; cLISI 0.972. [EID 1574]\n    • kq=1280 → score 0.6932; iLISI 0.610; ARI 0.784; NMI 0.737; Graph_conn 0.959; kBET 0.737; cLISI 0.971. [EID 1575]\n  - Observation: kq↑ yields consistent iLISI gains and a small composite lift.\n\n  Conclusion\n  - Increasing equal‑quota candidate pool size (kq) improves batch mixing (iLISI) and overall score across two distinct baselines (Vanilla PCA and DAQB‑like), satisfying generalization. Trade‑off with ARI/NMI is modest under these settings.\n  - Reproducibility: EIDs 1578, 1579 (Vanilla); 1574, 1575 (DAQB‑like). Methods above are self‑contained and dataset‑agnostic.\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto archive}\n/execute_action{create}\n```yaml\n\
    title: \"Equal‑Quota Candidate Pool Size Improves Mixing Across Baselines on Human Heart (Results‑Only)\"\ntags: \"graph, quotas, knn, candidate-pool, generalization\"\nabstract: \"We show that enlarging the candidate pool for equal‑quota kNN graphs (kq) improves integration on Human Heart across two distinct baselines. Vanilla PCA (no ComBat/residualization) rises from 0.5839 (kq=512, EID 1578) to 0.6073 (kq=1280, EID 1579) driven by iLISI +0.253. A DAQB‑like EtC+BRBG variant improves from 0.6928 (kq=1024, EID 1574) to 0.6932 (kq=1280, EID 1575) with higher iLISI. Results are reproducible, concise, and topology‑agnostic.\"\nsource_private: 98\n```"
