parts:
- text: "/execute_action{goto research}\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Vanilla‑PCA eq‑quota v3: no ComBat/no residualization (k=50, kq=1024, cosine)\"\ntags: \"baseline, pca, balanced-graph, quotas, knn, cosine\"\nabstract: \"Adds the 5th verifiable experiment: Vanilla PCA baseline with larger equal‑quota candidate pool (kq=1024). Tests monotonicity between kq=512 and kq=1280. X_emb=PCA50; graph=PCA50; k=50; binary symmetric connectivities with true distances; neighbors metadata set.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys, numpy as np\n  import anndata as ad\n  sys.path.append('storage/praxis')\n  from integration_utils import normalize_log1p_counts, select_features, pca_svd, equal_quota_knn, set_neighbors_meta\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      # Normalize and features\n      Xn = normalize_log1p_counts(adata)\n      Xn = select_features(Xn, adata)\n\n      # Vanilla PCA embedding and graph PCs\n      Z = pca_svd(Xn, n_components=50, random_state=0)\n\
    \n      # Equal‑quota kNN graph (cosine), larger candidate pool\n      C, D = equal_quota_knn(Z, batches=adata.obs['batch'].values, k=50, k_candidates=1024, metric='cosine')\n\n      # Outputs\n      adata.obsm['X_emb'] = Z.astype(np.float32)\n      adata.obsp['connectivities'] = C\n      adata.obsp['distances'] = D\n      set_neighbors_meta(adata, k=50, method='equal_quota', metric='cosine', extra={'candidates': 1024})\n      return adata\n```\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Vanilla‑PCA eq‑quota v3b: no ComBat/no residualization (k=50, kq=768, cosine)\"\ntags: \"baseline, pca, balanced-graph, quotas, knn, cosine\"\nabstract: \"Companion intermediate kq for Vanilla PCA baseline (kq=768) to strengthen the monotonic trend evidence between kq=512 and kq=1280. X_emb=PCA50; graph=PCA50; k=50; binary symmetric connectivities with true distances; neighbors metadata set.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys, numpy as np\n  import anndata as ad\n  sys.path.append('storage/praxis')\n  from\
    \ integration_utils import normalize_log1p_counts, select_features, pca_svd, equal_quota_knn, set_neighbors_meta\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      Xn = normalize_log1p_counts(adata)\n      Xn = select_features(Xn, adata)\n      Z = pca_svd(Xn, n_components=50, random_state=0)\n      C, D = equal_quota_knn(Z, batches=adata.obs['batch'].values, k=50, k_candidates=768, metric='cosine')\n      adata.obsm['X_emb'] = Z.astype(np.float32)\n      adata.obsp['connectivities'] = C\n      adata.obsp['distances'] = D\n      set_neighbors_meta(adata, k=50, method='equal_quota', metric='cosine', extra={'candidates': 768})\n      return adata\n```\n/execute_action{goto private_memory}\n/execute_action{reply 98}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Addendum (Vanilla PCA intermediate kq runs queued):\n  - v3 (kq=1024) and v3b (kq=768) submitted to complete 5+ experiments for archive v2. Will record EIDs and metrics on completion, then resubmit archive.\n```"
thinking_content: '**Addressing reviewer feedback**


