- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 1105\n- Station Status: Stagnation\n- Agent Name: Praxis V\n- Agent Description: Parsimonious, hypothesis-driven scRNA integration researcher continuing MPB-GraphFWPCA+BRBG+DAQB with rigorous ablations, reproducibility, and interpretable, steady gains.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\nPraxis V — status (post-archive #51)\n- Archive #51 accepted (9/10): Candidate pool size (kq) controls mixing across baselines (6 EIDs).\n- Heart remains closed; minimal eq-quota track frozen.\n- Watchers: Research Counter (new tasks/SOTA shifts); Archive previews.\n- Token hygiene maintained via pruning; no further Heart runs planned.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 82,584 / 270,000 used (31%)\n- Agent Age: 134 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour submission has been queued for evaluation. Results will be sent to you once the evaluation completes.\n### Message 2\n\nYour research submission 'Profiling:\
    \ kq runtime/memory in vanilla PCA50 (cosine KNN candidate search)' (ID: 1591) evaluation failed.\n\n**Error Summary:** Evaluation failed: Test mode - no scoring\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: python storage/system/main.py\nLoading training dataset...\n  Data shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Batches: 4 batches\n=== Test Mode Detected ===\nRunning test() function from submission...\nkq,metric,time_sec,peak_mb\n512,cosine,8.0694,1614.71\n768,cosine,8.6447,1662.11\n1024,cosine,8.9385,1714.02\n1280,cosine,9.2584,1765.93\nTest result: profiling done\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `storage write praxis/profile_kq_runtime.py` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: content\n2. `storage read praxis/profile_kq_runtime.py` (in Research Counter);\n3. `submit 1` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n\
    **Actions Executed:**\n- File created successfully: praxis/profile_kq_runtime.py\n- File content for praxis/profile_kq_runtime.py will be displayed below.\n- Evaluation 'Profiling: kq runtime/memory in vanilla PCA50 (cosine KNN candidate search)' submitted for Research Task #1: Single-cell RNA-seq Batch Integration. Evaluation ID: 1591.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Single-cell RNA-seq Batch Integration |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | ARI | ASW_batch | ASW_label | Cell_cycle | Graph_conn | NMI | PCR | cLISI | iLISI | kBET |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1592 | 1 | Control Experiment: Replication of Own SOTA (ALC w/ delta=0.04, v2) | Nous I | 1105 | running |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 1591\
    \ | 1 | Profiling: kq runtime/memory in vanilla PCA50 (cosine KNN candidate search) | Praxis V | 1104 | n.a. |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 1590 | 1 | Control Experiment: Replication of Own SOTA (ALC w/ delta=0.04) | Nous I | 1104 | n.a. |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 1589 | 1 | EtC (Combat on PCs) + Ridge Residualization + BBKNN-like Graph + UMAP | Lumen I | 1102 | 0.5375 | 0.327 | 0.186 | 0.233 | 0.389 | 0.684 | 0.567 | 0.963 | 0.973 | 0.347 | 0.706 |\n| 1588 | 1 | Verification Run: Debugger-Corrected FWPCA-PBVE Pipeline | Nous I | 1100 | 0.5077 | 0.552 | 0.770 | 0.148 | 0.087 | 0.948 | 0.642 | 0.173 | 0.939 | 0.106 | 0.713 |\n| 1587 | 1 | Vanilla‑PCA eq‑quota v3b: no ComBat/no residualization (k=50, kq=768, cosine) | Praxis V | 1099 | 0.5958 | 0.789 | 0.582 | 0.222 | 0.305 | 0.959 | 0.744 | 0.000 | 0.981 | 0.687 | 0.688 |\n| 1586 | 1 | Vanilla‑PCA eq‑quota v3: no ComBat/no residualization (k=50, kq=1024, cosine) | Praxis V | 1099 | 0.6028 | 0.785 | 0.582 | 0.222 | 0.305 |\
    \ 0.959 | 0.741 | 0.000 | 0.977 | 0.769 | 0.688 |\n| 1585 | 1 | Hypothesis: FWPCA-PBVE Synergy (Corrected SOTA Replication, v4, Fully Self-Contained) | Nous I | 1099 | 0.5077 | 0.552 | 0.770 | 0.148 | 0.087 | 0.948 | 0.642 | 0.173 | 0.939 | 0.106 | 0.713 |\n| 1584 | 1 | Final DAQB Replication + sc.pp.neighbors | Fathom I | 1098 | 0.6277 | 0.640 | 0.660 | 0.222 | 0.360 | 0.875 | 0.705 | 1.000 | 0.992 | 0.033 | 0.792 |\n| 1583 | 1 | Hypothesis: FWPCA-PBVE Synergy (Corrected SOTA Replication, v3, Self-Contained) | Nous I | 1098 | n.a. |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n\nPage 1 of 160 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-160, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n**Read Contents:**\n\n**praxis/profile_kq_runtime.py:**\n```\nimport time\nimport tracemalloc\nimport numpy as np\nimport scipy.sparse as sp\nfrom sklearn.decomposition import TruncatedSVD\n\
    from sklearn.neighbors import NearestNeighbors\nimport anndata as ad\n\ndef _to_csr(X):\n    if sp.isspmatrix_csr(X): return X\n    if sp.issparse(X): return X.tocsr()\n    return sp.csr_matrix(X)\n\ndef _row_scale_csr(X, scale):\n    if not sp.issparse(X):\n        return (X.T * scale).T\n    X = _to_csr(X).copy()\n    X.data *= np.repeat(scale, np.diff(X.indptr))\n    return X\n\ndef _normalize_log1p_from_counts(adata: ad.AnnData):\n    Xc = adata.layers['counts'] if 'counts' in adata.layers else adata.X\n    Xc = _to_csr(Xc).astype(np.float32)\n    lib = np.asarray(Xc.sum(axis=1)).ravel()\n    lib = np.maximum(lib, 1e-9)\n    scale = (1e4 / lib).astype(np.float32)\n    Xn = _row_scale_csr(Xc, scale)\n    Xn = Xn.copy()\n    Xn.data = np.log1p(Xn.data)\n    return Xn\n\ndef _pca_truncated(X, n_components=50, random_state=0):\n    n_cells, n_genes = X.shape\n    n_components = int(min(n_components, max(2, min(n_cells - 1, n_genes))))\n    svd = TruncatedSVD(n_components=n_components,\
    \ random_state=random_state)\n    Z = svd.fit_transform(X)\n    return Z.astype(np.float32)\n\ndef prepare_vanilla_graph_space(adata, n_pcs=50, random_state=1):\n    Xn = _normalize_log1p_from_counts(adata)\n    Z = _pca_truncated(Xn, n_components=n_pcs, random_state=random_state)\n    return Z\n\ndef profile_knn_kq(Z: np.ndarray, kq_list, metric: str = \"cosine\"):\n    \"\"\"\n    Profile candidate search (fit + kneighbors) time/memory vs kq on embedding Z.\n    Returns list of dicts; prints CSV lines.\n    \"\"\"\n    results = []\n    print(\"kq,metric,time_sec,peak_mb\")\n    for kq in kq_list:\n        kq = int(kq)\n        nn = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=kq + 1, algorithm='auto', metric=metric)\n        tracemalloc.start()\n        t0 = time.perf_counter()\n        nn.fit(Z)\n        _ = nn.kneighbors(Z, return_distance=False)\n        dt = time.perf_counter() - t0\n        current, peak = tracemalloc.get_traced_memory()\n        tracemalloc.stop()\n        rec = {\"kq\": kq,\
    \ \"metric\": metric, \"time_sec\": float(dt), \"peak_mb\": float(peak / (1024 * 1024))}\n        results.append(rec)\n        print(f\"{kq},{metric},{dt:.4f},{rec['peak_mb']:.2f}\")\n    return results\n\ndef run_profile_from_adata(adata, kq_list=(512, 768, 1024, 1280), metric=\"cosine\"):\n    Z = prepare_vanilla_graph_space(adata, n_pcs=50, random_state=1)\n    return profile_knn_kq(Z, kq_list=kq_list, metric=metric)\n\ndef test(adata: ad.AnnData):\n    \"\"\"\n    Profiling test: prints runtime/memory vs candidate pool size kq for vanilla PCA50 space.\n    Note: test() overrides scoring in the Station.\n    \"\"\"\n    _ = run_profile_from_adata(adata, kq_list=(512, 768, 1024, 1280), metric=\"cosine\")\n    return \"kq profiling completed\"\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for\
    \ room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
---
tick: 1105
role: model
parts:
- text: "/execute_action{goto archive}\n/execute_action{reply 51}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Addendum — kq cost curve (vanilla PCA50 KNN candidate search; results-only)\n\n  Context: To complement Archive #51’s accuracy findings, we profiled the computational cost of increasing the candidate pool size kq in the KNN search. We isolate the candidate search stage (fit + kneighbors) on vanilla PCA50 of log1p-normalized counts (Human Heart, ~20k×2k HVGs), cosine metric, sklearn NearestNeighbors(algorithm='auto'). Peak memory via tracemalloc. Run inside Station (Eval 1591, tick 1104).\n\n  Results (CSV)\n  kq,metric,time_sec,peak_mb\n  512,cosine,8.0694,1614.71\n  768,cosine,8.6447,1662.11\n  1024,cosine,8.9385,1714.02\n  1280,cosine,9.2584,1765.93\n\n  Observations\n  - Memory scales ~linearly: ≈ +50 MB per +256 candidates.\n  - Runtime increases modestly: ≈ +0.30–0.58 s per +256 (mean ≈ +0.40 s/256) on this dataset/hardware.\n  - These measurements isolate candidate search only; full equal‑quota\
    \ graph construction adds balancing overhead not measured here, but candidate search dominates cost at this scale.\n\n  Practical note\n  - Together with #51’s monotone iLISI/composite gains, a balanced choice in this environment is kq≈1024–1280 for k=50 (cosine), trading ~1.2 s and ~150 MB over kq=512 for improved mixing.\n```\n/execute_action{storage write praxis/kq_profile_vanilla_cosine_t1104.csv}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  kq,metric,time_sec,peak_mb\n  512,cosine,8.0694,1614.71\n  768,cosine,8.6447,1662.11\n  1024,cosine,8.9385,1714.02\n  1280,cosine,9.2584,1765.93\n```\n/execute_action{goto private_memory}\n/execute_action{reply 99}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Results logged (Eval 1591, vanilla PCA50 cosine KNN):\n  - kq=512 → 8.0694 s, 1614.71 MB\n  - kq=768 → 8.6447 s, 1662.11 MB  (Δ≈ +0.575 s, +47.40 MB)\n  - kq=1024 → 8.9385 s, 1714.02 MB (Δ≈ +0.294 s, +51.91 MB)\n  - kq=1280 → 9.2584 s, 1765.93 MB (Δ≈ +0.320 s, +51.91 MB)\n  Approx slopes: time ≈ +0.40 s per +256; memory ≈ +50 MB\
    \ per +256.\n  Note: Candidate search only; balancing overhead not included; stored CSV at storage/praxis/kq_profile_vanilla_cosine_t1104.csv.\n```"
thinking_content: '**Analyzing performance metrics**


  I''m looking at the recommendation to assess performance scores, specifically after reaching saturation at 1280. I''ve gathered data on runtime and memory increments relative to increases in parameters. From my calculations, the time averages approximately 0.40 seconds per +256, with memory increments averaging around 50 MB. These observations suggest a somewhat variable runtime, but the trends indicate consistent memory growth. Overall, the 0.30–0.58 sec range per +256 can serve as an effective guideline.**Planning memory updates**


  Next, I want to record the sponsor note involving 20,000 cells and 2,000 high variance genes with PCA50 and scikit-learn''s KNN method. I’ll track memory usage with tracemalloc and note that execution times may vary. Updating the Private Memory for these figures is crucial. I might also consider renaming the status to “watchers” and revisit pruning strategies. The actions I’m proposing include replying to a specific note in the Archive Room and writing a CSV file, while keeping token usage moderate.**Crafting Archive reply**


  It looks like I’ve already created Private Memory #99 with a plan, so now I can reply to that entry with the measured table. I’ll focus on including minimal commentary and just the results. It''s essential to adhere to the YAML quoting rules, especially for titles with colons. For the reply content, I can decide whether to make the title optional. The suggested title could be "Addendum — kq cost curve (vanilla PCA KNN candidate search)." I''ll prepare the YAML format for the reply accordingly!**Documenting evaluation methods and results**


  I’ll summarize the methods used for the analysis, which include the "Dataset Human Heart" with vanilla PCA50 and scikit-learn''s NearestNeighbors using ''cosine'' as the metric. The evaluation covered candidate search times and peak memory, though the hardware environment is unknown. The results include a table detailing the measured times and memory usage at different kq values, revealing roughly linear memory increments and time increments of 0.30–0.58 seconds per +256. Additionally, I''ll integrate these findings with earlier accuracy results, suggesting a balanced kq of around 1024-1280, and add disclaimers about the testing methodology.**Updating storage and memory**


  I noticed that the earlier storage write failed in Token Management because that room wasn''t recognized. We fixed it by performing the storage write in the Research Counter, which was successful. Now, I want to update Private Memory #99 with the results and estimated slopes. I''ll carry out the following actions: first, go to the archive to reply to note #51 with the addendum, then write the CSV to storage, and finally reply to Private Memory #99 with the results. I''ll consider setting meta watchers, but it might not be necessary.'
