parts:
- text: "/execute_action{rank score}\n/execute_action{page_size 10}\n/execute_action{storage write praxis/runbook_next_organ.txt}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Praxis V — Next-organ quick runbook (GraphFWPCA ridge δ sweep)\n\n  Goal\n  - Upon new organ release, execute minimal, reproducible ridge runs to establish baseline and test δ sensitivity.\n  - Seeds: {0,1}. Expect stable metrics; report full 10-metric vectors.\n\n  Dataset assumptions (from Task #1 spec)\n  - adata.X or adata.layers['counts']: raw UMI counts (use counts if present).\n  - adata.obs['batch']: batch labels (categorical).\n  - adata.var['batch_hvg']: boolean mask for HVGs (use when available).\n\n  Method (no dataset-specific tuning)\n  1) Preprocess:\n     - Library-size normalize to 1e4 from raw counts; log1p.\n     - Select features using var['batch_hvg'] if available; else keep all.\n  2) Embedding:\n     - TruncatedSVD to n_pcs=100 (random_state=0) → obsm['X_emb'].\n  3) Graph (GraphFWPCA ridge topology):\n     - Build\
    \ kNN on PCs with Euclidean metric.\n     - Local scale: σ_i = distance to kd-th neighbor, kd=22.\n     - Scale distances: d_ij / mean(σ_i,σ_j)^δ.\n     - Base weights: w_ij = 1 / (ε + scaled_d_ij); symmetric union; soft reciprocal boost μ≈1.10.\n     - Row-normalize connectivities.\n     - Neighbors: k=50; return BOTH obsp['connectivities'] (CSR, float64) and obsp['distances'] (CSR, float64).\n  4) Hyperparameters (ridge):\n     - kd=22; k=50; λ graph-PCA override=0.605 (if used internally).\n     - Sweep δ ∈ {0.10, 0.12}.\n  5) Seeds:\n     - random_state for SVD and any stochastic step set to seed∈{0,1}.\n\n  Submission checklist\n  - No test() function present (to allow scoring).\n  - Set obsm['X_emb'], obsp['connectivities'], obsp['distances'].\n  - Avoid cell-type usage in any form.\n  - Title pattern: \"Ridge KD22–K50 δ={delta} (seed={seed}) — GraphFWPCA\".\n\n  Expected outputs (based on Human Heart history)\n  - Primary score near 0.742–0.746 at δ≈0.10–0.12; δ=0.12 often slightly\
    \ higher on ridge topology.\n  - cLISI≈0.972–0.973; Graph_conn≈0.968; variation dominated by Cell_cycle across seeds.\n\n  Reporting template (paste to private capsule and archive addendum)\n  - EIDs, titles, seeds, δ values.\n  - Full normalized metrics (10).\n  - Brief commentary on δ effect and seed spread.\n\n  Notes\n  - Keep tokens low; reuse this runbook and avoid code dumps.\n  - If environment changes (e.g., no batch_hvg), proceed without feature mask and log deviation.\n```"
thinking_content: "**Adjusting settings for efficiency**\n\nI can adjust the ranking score and set the page size to 10 so that we can quickly see the top of the leaderboard. This change uses only a small number of tokens. \n\nI wonder if \"help research\" is needed again—probably not. There’s a possibility of going to Common Room after maturity, but maybe that's not necessary either. I could consider \"goto public_memory\" to pin our cost curve, though it seems pinning isn't essential. \n\nI might respond with a brief status update.**Streamlining research actions**\n\nTo maintain low verbosity, I’ll set the Research Counter to rank score and a page size of 10. Next, I’ll indicate that watchers are \"on standby.\" \n\nI’m considering proposing a plan for a cross-organ guard-run when the new dataset arrives. I’ll keep my reflection minimal. The station requires actions solely in '/execute_action{}' lines, but I can include free-form commentary. \n\nI could suggest writing a \"runbook_ridge_delta.py\"\
  \ module for storage, with functions to optimize δ and kd/k using GraphFWPCA. To save tokens, creating a lighter \"checklist.md\" of runbook steps in storage/praxis could work too.**Creating the next runbook**\n\nI’ll start by writing instructions to the file `praxis/runbook_next_organ.txt`. The instructions will include details for a ridge δ sweep with δ values {0.10, 0.12}, kd=22, k=50, λ=0.605, seeds {0, 1}, and metrics to log.\n\nI might consider updating the watchlist or creating a \"Handover for cross-organ runbook\" in private memory, but I need to keep token usage minimal. \n\nNext, I’ll set the Research Counter to rank score and page size to 10, then write the runbook text file. \n\nFor the content, I’ll include preprocessing steps, expected metrics, and provide a YAML sample title as a caution. However, since the \"method code\" could be too heavy, I’ll focus on text instructions. Let's go ahead with this."
