    **ID:** 1601\n**Tags:** graph, pca, candidate-pool, knn, local-scaling, ridge\n**Abstract:** Tests whether expanding the KNN candidate pool (kq) improves ridge GraphFWPCA (keep top‑k=50). We set kq=256 via extra neighbors and retain δ=0.12, kd=22, Euclidean metric, soft reciprocal boost. Hypothesis: larger kq yields better edge selection and mixing with minimal cost.\n**Score:** 0.517778757508422\n**ASW_batch:** 0.667\n**ASW_label:** 0.205\n**ARI:** 0.720\n**NMI:** 0.717\n**Graph_conn:** 0.889\n**kBET:** 0.609\n**iLISI:** 0.096\n**cLISI:** 0.980\n**PCR:** 0.000\n**Cell_cycle:** 0.295\n**Evaluation Details:** Human Dataset (20,000 cells):\nNormalized Scores [0-1]:\n  ASW_batch: 0.667  ASW_label: 0.205  ARI: 0.720  NMI: 0.717\n  Graph_conn: 0.889  kBET: 0.609  iLISI: 0.096  cLISI: 0.980\n  PCR: 0.000  Cell_cycle: 0.295\n\nRaw Scores (before normalization):\n  ASW_batch: 0.833884  ASW_label: 0.529749  ARI: 0.720091  NMI: 0.716872\n  Graph_conn: 0.890908  kBET: 0.583638  iLISI: 0.096465\
    \  cLISI: 0.994092\n  PCR: 0.000000  Cell_cycle: 0.260778\n\n**Submission Code:**\n```python\nimport sys, numpy as np\nimport scipy.sparse as sp\nimport anndata as ad\nsys.path.append('storage/praxis')\nimport graphfwpca_ridge as gr\n\ndef _maybe_hvg(X, adata):\n    try:\n        if 'batch_hvg' in adata.var.columns:\n            mask = adata.var['batch_hvg'].values.astype(bool)\n            if mask.sum() > 0 and mask.sum() < X.shape[1]:\n                return X[:, mask]\n    except Exception:\n        pass\n    return X\n\ndef eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n    # Hyperparameters (ridge)\n    n_pcs = 100\n    k = 50\n    kd = 22\n    delta = 0.12\n    kq = 256  # candidate pool size\n    extra = int(max(0, kq - max(k, kd)))\n\n    # Normalize from counts + optional HVG mask\n    Xn = gr._normalize_log1p_from_counts(adata)\n    Xn = _maybe_hvg(Xn, adata)\n\n    # PCs\n    Z = gr._pca_truncated(Xn, n_components=n_pcs, random_state=0)\n\n    # Graph with enlarged\
    \ candidate pool\n    C, D = gr._build_graph_knn(Z, k=k, kd=kd, delta=delta, extra=extra, metric=\"euclidean\", mutual_boost=1.10)\n\n    # Outputs\n    adata.obsm['X_emb'] = Z.astype(np.float32)\n    adata.obsp['connectivities'] = C\n    adata.obsp['distances'] = D\n    return adata\n\n```\n\n**Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: python storage/system/main.py\nLoading training dataset...\n  Data shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Batches: 4 batches\nFound eliminate_batch_effect_fn, executing...\n\n=== Running batch integration ===\n  Result shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Has embedding: True\n  Has graph: True\n\nResult saved to: storage/shared/tmp/dd7e28af-9b47-4db6-a8b1-2d03a53183e0/result_human.h5ad\n\nRESULT_UUID: dd7e28af-9b47-4db6-a8b1-2d03a53183e0\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n### Message 2\n\n**Evaluation Review: 1602**\n\n**Research Submission Review**\n\n**Title:** Ridge GraphFWPCA — large candidate pool kq=1024 (k=50, kd=22, δ=0.12, seed=0)\n**ID:** 1602\n**Tags:**\
