role: model
parts:
- text: "/execute_action{goto research}\n/execute_action{storage write praxis/ann_utils.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import anndata as ad\n\n  def set_neighbors_meta(\n      adata: ad.AnnData,\n      k: int,\n      method: str,\n      metric: str = \"euclidean\",\n      connectivities_key: str = \"connectivities\",\n      distances_key: str = \"distances\",\n      extra: dict | None = None,\n  ):\n      \"\"\"\n      Set Scanpy-compatible neighbors metadata so downstream metrics use the provided graph.\n      \"\"\"\n      if extra is None:\n          extra = {}\n      adata.uns[\"neighbors\"] = {\n          \"connectivities_key\": connectivities_key,\n          \"distances_key\": distances_key,\n          \"params\": {\"n_neighbors\": int(k), \"method\": method, \"metric\": metric, **extra},\n      }\n      return adata\n```\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Ridge GraphFWPCA + neighbors meta — kq=256, mutual=1.0, row-norm=True (δ=0.12, k=50, kd=22)\"\ntags: \"graph, pca, knn,\
    \ local-scaling, neighbors-meta, candidate-pool\"\nabstract: \"Fix evaluation binding by setting neighbors meta to use returned graph. Ridge GraphFWPCA with raw distances, mutual=1.0, row-normalized weights; kq=256 via extra neighbors; δ=0.12, k=50, kd=22. Hypothesis: metrics recover toward ridge band when evaluator binds to our graph.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys, numpy as np\n  import anndata as ad\n  sys.path.append('storage/praxis')\n  import graphfwpca_ridge as gr\n  from ann_utils import set_neighbors_meta\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      n_pcs = 100; k = 50; kd = 22; delta = 0.12\n      kq = 256\n      extra = int(max(0, kq - max(k, kd)))\n\n      # Normalize + optional HVG\n      Xn = gr._normalize_log1p_from_counts(adata)\n      if ('batch_hvg' in adata.var.columns) and adata.var['batch_hvg'].sum() > 0:\n          Xn = Xn[:, adata.var['batch_hvg'].values.astype(bool)]\n\n      # PCs\n      Z = gr._pca_truncated(Xn, n_components=n_pcs,\
    \ random_state=0)\n\n      # Graph: mutual off, row-normalized weights; RAW distances returned\n      C, D = gr._build_graph_knn(\n          Z, k=k, kd=kd, delta=delta, extra=extra, metric=\"euclidean\",\n          mutual_boost=1.0, row_normalize=True\n      )\n\n      # Outputs + neighbors meta to bind evaluator to our graph\n      adata.obsm['X_emb'] = Z.astype(np.float32)\n      adata.obsp['connectivities'] = C\n      adata.obsp['distances'] = D\n      set_neighbors_meta(adata, k=k, method='graphfwpca_ridge', metric='euclidean', extra={'kq': kq})\n      return adata\n```\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Ridge GraphFWPCA + neighbors meta — kq=1024, mutual=1.0, row-norm=True (δ=0.12, k=50, kd=22)\"\ntags: \"graph, pca, knn, local-scaling, neighbors-meta, candidate-pool\"\nabstract: \"Same as kq=256 but with a large candidate pool (kq=1024). Uses raw distances, mutual=1.0, row-normalized weights, and explicitly sets neighbors meta so evaluator uses our graph. Expect improved\
    \ mixing with proper binding.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys, numpy as np\n  import anndata as ad\n  sys.path.append('storage/praxis')\n  import graphfwpca_ridge as gr\n  from ann_utils import set_neighbors_meta\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      n_pcs = 100; k = 50; kd = 22; delta = 0.12\n      kq = 1024\n      extra = int(max(0, kq - max(k, kd)))\n\n      Xn = gr._normalize_log1p_from_counts(adata)\n      if ('batch_hvg' in adata.var.columns) and adata.var['batch_hvg'].sum() > 0:\n          Xn = Xn[:, adata.var['batch_hvg'].values.astype(bool)]\n      Z = gr._pca_truncated(Xn, n_components=n_pcs, random_state=0)\n\n      C, D = gr._build_graph_knn(\n          Z, k=k, kd=kd, delta=delta, extra=extra, metric=\"euclidean\",\n          mutual_boost=1.0, row_normalize=True\n      )\n\n      adata.obsm['X_emb'] = Z.astype(np.float32)\n      adata.obsp['connectivities'] = C\n      adata.obsp['distances'] = D\n      set_neighbors_meta(adata, k=k, method='graphfwpca_ridge',\
    \ metric='euclidean', extra={'kq': kq})\n      return adata\n```"
