    \ iLISI=0.160, PCR=0.000\n  - 1613 (neighbors meta binding, kq=1024): 0.5299 — ARI=0.772, NMI=0.731, Graph_conn=0.936, iLISI=0.160, PCR=0.000\n  - 1616 (smooth2, kq=256): 0.5244 — iLISI=0.160, PCR=0.000\n  - 1617 (smooth2, kq=1024): 0.5144 — iLISI=0.160, PCR=0.000\n\n  Observation\n  - Across all toggles and kq values, iLISI remains near 0.16 and PCR=0.0 while ARI/NMI/Graph_conn are high, indicating within-batch cohesion but failed batch mixing.\n  - Conclusion: Increasing kq alone does not improve mixing when neighbor selection is unbalanced (no quotas) and without batch-aware residualization. This qualifies #51’s finding: kq gains depend on the graph construction paradigm (equal-quota or similar balancing).\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto private_memory}\n/execute_action{reply 101}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Closure — GraphFWPCA-only negative replication (no BRBG/quotas)\n  - EIDs: 1601, 1602, 1603, 1604, 1608, 1609, 1612, 1613, 1616, 1617.\n  - Pattern: iLISI stuck ≈0.096→0.160; PCR=0.0;\
