role: model
parts:
- text: "/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"GraphFWPCA + Equal-Quota kNN (no BRBG/ComBat): kd=22, δ=0.12, k=50, kq=1024\"\ntags: \"graph, fwpca, equal-quota, knn, batch-aware, sparse\"\nabstract: \"Bridges GraphFWPCA distance scaling with an equal-quota kNN selector to enforce balanced per-batch neighbors. We normalize counts, PCA(100), compute kd=22 local scales and scaled distances with δ=0.12, then select k=50 neighbors per cell with equal quotas across batches from a large candidate pool (kq=1024). Weighted connectivities use 1/(scaled+eps); distances are true (raw PC) distances; soft mutual symmetrization and row-normalization are applied.\"\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n  import scipy.sparse as sp\n  from sklearn.decomposition import TruncatedSVD\n  from sklearn.neighbors import NearestNeighbors\n  import pandas as pd\n  import anndata as ad\n\n  # ---- Utilities ----\n  def _to_csr(X):\n      if sp.isspmatrix_csr(X): return X\n      if sp.issparse(X): return X.tocsr()\n\
    \      return sp.csr_matrix(X)\n\n  def _row_scale_csr(X, scale):\n      if not sp.issparse(X):\n          return (X.T * scale).T\n      X = _to_csr(X).copy()\n      X.data *= np.repeat(scale, np.diff(X.indptr))\n      return X\n\n  def _normalize_log1p_from_counts(adata):\n      Xc = adata.layers['counts'] if 'counts' in adata.layers else adata.X\n      Xc = _to_csr(Xc).astype(np.float32)\n      lib = np.asarray(Xc.sum(axis=1)).ravel()\n      lib = np.maximum(lib, 1e-9)\n      scale = (1e4 / lib).astype(np.float32)\n      Xn = _row_scale_csr(Xc, scale)\n      Xn = Xn.copy()\n      Xn.data = np.log1p(Xn.data)\n      return Xn\n\n  def _pca_svd(X, n_components=100, random_state=0):\n      n_cells, n_genes = X.shape\n      n_components = int(min(n_components, max(2, min(n_cells - 1, n_genes))))\n      svd = TruncatedSVD(n_components=n_components, random_state=random_state)\n      Z = svd.fit_transform(X)\n      return Z.astype(np.float32)\n\n  # ---- Equal-quota selector (per row, balanced\
    \ across batches) ----\n  def _equal_quota_select_per_row(dists_scaled_row, dists_raw_row, idx_row, batch_row, k, nbatches):\n      \"\"\"\n      Select up to k neighbors with equal quotas per batch:\n      base = k // nbatches; remainder distributed to batches with smallest next candidate.\n      Fallback fills from global best if a batch runs out within kq.\n      Returns arrays of (cols, w, d_raw) for this row.\n      \"\"\"\n      base = k // nbatches\n      rem = k - base * nbatches\n      # Build per-batch candidate lists (already ordered by scaled distance)\n      cols_sel = []\n      w_sel = []\n      d_sel = []\n      # pointers per batch\n      ptr = np.zeros(nbatches, dtype=int)\n      # Pre-split candidate positions by batch\n      pos_by_b = [np.where(batch_row == b)[0] for b in range(nbatches)]\n      # 1) Take base from each batch\n      for b in range(nbatches):\n          pos = pos_by_b[b]\n          take = min(base, pos.size)\n          if take > 0:\n              sel_pos\
    \ = pos[:take]\n              ptr[b] = take\n              cols_sel.append(idx_row[sel_pos])\n              # weights on scaled distances; distances matrix stores raw\n              w_sel.append(1.0 / (dists_scaled_row[sel_pos] + 1e-12))\n              d_sel.append(dists_raw_row[sel_pos])\n      if cols_sel:\n          cols_sel = np.concatenate(cols_sel)\n          w_sel = np.concatenate(w_sel)\n          d_sel = np.concatenate(d_sel)\n      else:\n          cols_sel = np.array([], dtype=int)\n          w_sel = np.array([], dtype=float)\n          d_sel = np.array([], dtype=float)\n\n      # 2) Distribute remainder by picking the next-best candidate per batch (smallest next scaled distance)\n      selected_set = set(cols_sel.tolist())\n      for _ in range(rem):\n          best_b = -1\n          best_val = np.inf\n          best_col = None\n          best_w = None\n          best_d = None\n          for b in range(nbatches):\n              pos = pos_by_b[b]\n              p = ptr[b]\n\
    \              if p < pos.size:\n                  j = pos[p]\n                  val = dists_scaled_row[j]\n                  if val < best_val and idx_row[j] not in selected_set:\n                      best_val = val\n                      best_b = b\n                      best_col = idx_row[j]\n                      best_w = 1.0 / (dists_scaled_row[j] + 1e-12)\n                      best_d = dists_raw_row[j]\n          if best_b == -1:  # no batch had a candidate\n              break\n          ptr[best_b] += 1\n          selected_set.add(int(best_col))\n          cols_sel = np.append(cols_sel, best_col)\n          w_sel = np.append(w_sel, best_w)\n          d_sel = np.append(d_sel, best_d)\n\n      # 3) If still short, fill from global best remaining\n      if cols_sel.size < k:\n          # global order by scaled distance\n          order = np.argsort(dists_scaled_row, kind='mergesort')\n          for j in order:\n              col = int(idx_row[j])\n              if col not in selected_set:\n\
    \                  cols_sel = np.append(cols_sel, col)\n                  w_sel = np.append(w_sel, 1.0 / (dists_scaled_row[j] + 1e-12))\n                  d_sel = np.append(d_sel, dists_raw_row[j])\n                  selected_set.add(col)\n                  if cols_sel.size >= k:\n                      break\n\n      # Truncate in rare overfill\n      if cols_sel.size > k:\n          keep = np.argsort(-w_sel)[:k]  # keep strongest\n          cols_sel = cols_sel[keep]\n          w_sel = w_sel[keep]\n          d_sel = d_sel[keep]\n      return cols_sel.astype(int), w_sel.astype(float), d_sel.astype(float)\n\n  # ---- Core integration ----\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      # Hyperparameters (GraphFWPCA + EQ-quota)\n      n_pcs = 100\n      k = 50\n      kd = 22\n      delta = 0.12\n      kq = 1024\n      mutual_boost = 1.10\n      rng_seed = 0\n\n      # 1) Normalize from counts; optional batch-aware HVGs\n      Xn = _normalize_log1p_from_counts(adata)\n\
    \      if 'batch_hvg' in adata.var.columns:\n          mask = adata.var['batch_hvg'].values.astype(bool)\n          if mask.sum() > 0 and mask.sum() < Xn.shape[1]:\n              Xn = Xn[:, mask]\n\n      # 2) PCA embedding (for both embedding output and neighbor search)\n      Z = _pca_svd(Xn, n_components=n_pcs, random_state=rng_seed)\n\n      # 3) kNN candidates on raw PC space (Euclidean)\n      nn = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=kq + 1, metric=\"euclidean\")\n      nn.fit(Z)\n      d_all, idx_all = nn.kneighbors(Z, return_distance=True)\n      # drop self\n      d_raw = d_all[:, 1:]   # (n, kq)\n      idx = idx_all[:, 1:]   # (n, kq)\n\n      n = Z.shape[0]\n      # kd-th local scale (per-row)\n      kd_pos = int(min(kd, d_raw.shape[1])) - 1\n      sigma = np.maximum(d_raw[:, kd_pos], 1e-12)  # shape (n,)\n\n      # scaled distances using mean(σ_i, σ_j)^delta\n      sigma_i = sigma[:, None]\n      sigma_j = sigma[idx]\n      sigma_ij = 0.5 * (sigma_i + sigma_j)\n      d_scaled =\
    \ d_raw / (np.power(sigma_ij, delta) + 1e-12)\n\n      # batch codes for candidates\n      batches = adata.obs['batch']\n      if not pd.api.types.is_categorical_dtype(batches):\n          batches = pd.Categorical(batches)\n      batch_codes = batches.codes.to_numpy()\n      batch_of_idx = batch_codes[idx]  # (n, kq)\n      nbatches = int(batches.categories.size)\n\n      # 4) Equal-quota selection per row\n      rows = []\n      cols = []\n      data_w = []\n      data_d = []\n      for i in range(n):\n          csel, wsel, dsel = _equal_quota_select_per_row(\n              d_scaled[i], d_raw[i], idx[i], batch_of_idx[i], k=k, nbatches=nbatches\n          )\n          if csel.size == 0:\n              continue\n          rows.append(np.full(csel.size, i, dtype=int))\n          cols.append(csel)\n          data_w.append(wsel)\n          data_d.append(dsel)\n      if len(rows) == 0:\n          # degenerate fallback: return identity graph\n          I = sp.eye(n, format='csr', dtype=np.float64)\n\
    \          adata.obsm['X_emb'] = Z.astype(np.float32)\n          adata.obsp['connectivities'] = I\n          adata.obsp['distances'] = I\n          return adata\n\n      rows = np.concatenate(rows)\n      cols = np.concatenate(cols)\n      data_w = np.concatenate(data_w)\n      data_d = np.concatenate(data_d)\n\n      W_dir = sp.coo_matrix((data_w, (rows, cols)), shape=(n, n)).tocsr()\n      D_dir = sp.coo_matrix((data_d, (rows, cols)), shape=(n, n)).tocsr()\n\n      # 5) Symmetrize (union): weights by max, distances by min; soft mutual boost\n      W_sym = W_dir.maximum(W_dir.T)\n      D_sym = D_dir.minimum(D_dir.T)\n      mutual = W_dir.minimum(W_dir.T)\n      if mutual_boost != 1.0:\n          W_sym = W_sym + (mutual_boost - 1.0) * mutual\n\n      # 6) Row-normalize connectivities; ensure CSR float64\n      W_sym = W_sym.tocsr().astype(np.float64)\n      D_sym = D_sym.tocsr().astype(np.float64)\n      row_sum = np.asarray(W_sym.sum(axis=1)).ravel()\n      row_sum[row_sum == 0.0] =\
    \ 1.0\n      W_sym = _row_scale_csr(W_sym, 1.0 / row_sum)\n\n      # 7) Write outputs\n      adata.obsm['X_emb'] = Z.astype(np.float32)\n      adata.obsp['connectivities'] = W_sym\n      adata.obsp['distances'] = D_sym\n      return adata\n```"
thinking_content: "**Planning evaluation submission**\n\nI’m planning to submit a new evaluation for Task #1, where I’ll use \"GraphFWPCA + Equal-Quota kNN\" with specific parameters like δ=0.12, kd=22, and k=50. I’m considering using Euclidean distances in alignment with GraphFWPCA distances, unlike earlier implementations that used cosine. \n\nFor the implementation steps, I’ll normalize counts, apply PCA, and build candidate neighbors using the defined metrics, making sure to properly allocate quotas based on the global batch proportions. This approach should maintain the intended effect.**Implementing equal-quota allocation**\n\nI’m revisiting the earlier equal-quota approach, where the allocation might be done by computing quotas per row. I plan to set these quotas as q_b = floor(k * p_b), where p_b represents the frequency of batch b overall. \n\nI’ll ensure the corrections account for the remainder and allocate it to the batches with the smallest fractional components. This way, I\
  \ can achieve proportional quotas that align with the global batch distribution rather than just fixed quotas. It should create a more effective balance across the batches.**Clarifying equal-quota implementation**\n\nI’m realizing that \"equal-quota\" might have previously referred to equally distributing neighbors across batches, like allocating approximately k / B neighbors to each batch. In the former pipeline, a balanced graph may have aimed for that equality while mixing. \n\nWith four batches, having around k=12 or 13 neighbors each improves iLISI but could affect label metrics. I’ll implement equal quotas as q_b = floor(k / B), distributing the remainder to the nearest distances. For the candidate pool, I'll set kq=1024 to ensure sufficient points per batch, followed by selecting neighbors grouped by batch.**Selecting neighbors and building matrices**\n\nFor each batch, I’ll select up to q_b neighbors based on the smallest distances, s_ij. If the unique selections across all batches\
  \ are less than k, I’ll fill in with the next smallest remaining distances until reaching k; if there are more than k due to rounding, I’ll adjust accordingly.\n\nNext, I’ll build the connectivities matrix, W, using weights defined as w = 1 / (s + eps) and symmetrizing the results. I also need to compute the embedding 'X_emb' as principal components and ensure connectivity metadata is optional. I’ll keep in mind the memory and time requirements for processing these steps.**Preparing equal-quota and distance calculations**\n\nI’m considering the implications of building a large edge set with 20 million records but remember that edges are per row and only for the top-k neighbors (k=50). We don’t store candidate edges, only the selected top-k. \n\nI’ll implement a procedure to maintain selection across batches while being mindful of how we handle the remainder of neighbors. For each batch, I plan to allocate the base number of neighbors and select additional neighbors based on smallest distances.\
  \ After calculating the distance matrices, I’ll ensure the distances align with the specifications for neighbor selection. \n\nI also need to write the function to construct these components accordingly.**Finalizing variable implementation**\n\nIn my code, I'll use 's' for ranking purposes and define the weights 'w' as 1 / (s + 1e-12). For the directional distances matrix, I'll gather raw distances for the selected neighbors, ensuring I reference d[selected positions], avoiding any scaling. \n\nIt's crucial to name my implementation variables clearly to prevent confusion, so everything remains concise. I also want to remember to manage my tokens carefully, making sure to keep the system active. Let’s finalize the code and any necessary actions for this experiment!"
