role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 1135\n- Station Status: Stagnation\n- Agent Name: Praxis V\n- Agent Description: Parsimonious, hypothesis-driven scRNA integration researcher continuing MPB-GraphFWPCA+BRBG+DAQB with rigorous ablations, reproducibility, and interpretable, steady gains.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\nPraxis V — standby (all Heart branches frozen)\n- Publications: #48 (δ topology dependence), #51 (kq across baselines) + cost addendum.\n- Closures: Ridge near‑SOTA stable; Minimal eq‑quota frozen; GraphFWPCA‑only negative.\n- Watchers: Research Counter (new organ/tasks, SOTA shifts), Archive previews.\n- On new organ: run ridge δ∈{0.10,0.12}, kd=22, k=50 with seeds {0,1}; template and runbook in storage/praxis.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 111,479 / 270,000 used (41%)\n- Agent Age: 164 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour submission has been queued for evaluation. Results will be sent to you\
    \ once the evaluation completes.\n### Message 2\n\nYour research submission 'GraphFWPCA + Equal-Quota kNN (no BRBG/ComBat): kd=22, δ=0.12, k=50, kq=1024' (ID: 1631) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 0.517690224899611\n**ASW_batch:** 0.667\n**ASW_label:** 0.205\n**ARI:** 0.720\n**NMI:** 0.717\n**Graph_conn:** 0.889\n**kBET:** 0.608\n**iLISI:** 0.096\n**cLISI:** 0.980\n**PCR:** 0.000\n**Cell_cycle:** 0.295\n**Evaluation Details:** Human Dataset (20,000 cells):\nNormalized Scores [0-1]:\n  ASW_batch: 0.667  ASW_label: 0.205  ARI: 0.720  NMI: 0.717\n  Graph_conn: 0.889  kBET: 0.608  iLISI: 0.096  cLISI: 0.980\n  PCR: 0.000  Cell_cycle: 0.295\n\nRaw Scores (before normalization):\n  ASW_batch: 0.833884  ASW_label: 0.529749  ARI: 0.720091  NMI: 0.716872\n  Graph_conn: 0.890908  kBET: 0.582806  iLISI: 0.096465  cLISI: 0.994092\n  PCR: 0.000000  Cell_cycle: 0.260778\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 1631\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed AttributeError in\
    \ batch code extraction. The code is now running without crashing (300+ seconds of execution).\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original code had an incorrect way of accessing categorical codes from a pandas Series:\n\n```python\nbatches = adata.obs['batch']\nif not pd.api.types.is_categorical_dtype(batches):\n    batches = pd.Categorical(batches)\nbatch_codes = batches.codes.to_numpy()  # ❌ ERROR: Series has no attribute 'codes'\n```\n\nThe issue is that when `batches` is converted to a `pd.Categorical` object directly, it's no longer a Series. However, when `batches` is already categorical (which is the common case with AnnData objects), it remains a Series and requires the `.cat` accessor to access the codes.\n\n## Fix Applied\nModified the batch code extraction logic to handle both cases properly:\n\n```python\nbatches = adata.obs['batch']\nif not pd.api.types.is_categorical_dtype(batches):\n    batches = pd.Categorical(batches)\n    batch_codes = batches.codes  # Direct access for Categorical\
    \ object\nelse:\n    batch_codes = batches.cat.codes.to_numpy()  # Use .cat accessor for categorical Series\n```\n\nAdditionally, updated the nbatches calculation to be more robust:\n\n```python\nnbatches = int(len(batches.categories) if hasattr(batches, 'categories') else batches.cat.categories.size)\n```\n\n## Files Modified\n- `submissions/submission_v2.py` - Fixed version with corrected batch code extraction\n\n## Verification\n- Monitor script confirmed the code ran for 300+ seconds without crashing (exit code 0)\n- Evaluation is still in progress but the absence of runtime errors indicates successful fix\n- The AttributeError has been eliminated\n\n## Technical Details\nThe fix addresses the pandas API difference between:\n- `pd.Categorical` objects (have `.codes` attribute directly)\n- Categorical Series (require `.cat.codes` accessor)\n\nThis is a common pattern when working with AnnData objects where batch information is typically stored as categorical dtype in the obs DataFrame.\n\
    \n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v2):**\n```python\nimport numpy as np\nimport scipy.sparse as sp\nfrom sklearn.decomposition import TruncatedSVD\nfrom sklearn.neighbors import NearestNeighbors\nimport pandas as pd\nimport anndata as ad\n\n# ---- Utilities ----\ndef _to_csr(X):\n    if sp.isspmatrix_csr(X): return X\n    if sp.issparse(X): return X.tocsr()\n    return sp.csr_matrix(X)\n\ndef _row_scale_csr(X, scale):\n    if not sp.issparse(X):\n        return (X.T * scale).T\n    X = _to_csr(X).copy()\n    X.data *= np.repeat(scale, np.diff(X.indptr))\n    return X\n\ndef _normalize_log1p_from_counts(adata):\n    Xc = adata.layers['counts'] if 'counts' in adata.layers else adata.X\n    Xc = _to_csr(Xc).astype(np.float32)\n    lib = np.asarray(Xc.sum(axis=1)).ravel()\n    lib = np.maximum(lib, 1e-9)\n    scale = (1e4 / lib).astype(np.float32)\n\
    \    Xn = _row_scale_csr(Xc, scale)\n    Xn = Xn.copy()\n    Xn.data = np.log1p(Xn.data)\n    return Xn\n\ndef _pca_svd(X, n_components=100, random_state=0):\n    n_cells, n_genes = X.shape\n    n_components = int(min(n_components, max(2, min(n_cells - 1, n_genes))))\n    svd = TruncatedSVD(n_components=n_components, random_state=random_state)\n    Z = svd.fit_transform(X)\n    return Z.astype(np.float32)\n\n# ---- Equal-quota selector (per row, balanced across batches) ----\ndef _equal_quota_select_per_row(dists_scaled_row, dists_raw_row, idx_row, batch_row, k, nbatches):\n    \"\"\"\n    Select up to k neighbors with equal quotas per batch:\n    base = k // nbatches; remainder distributed to batches with smallest next candidate.\n    Fallback fills from global best if a batch runs out within kq.\n    Returns arrays of (cols, w, d_raw) for this row.\n    \"\"\"\n    base = k // nbatches\n    rem = k - base * nbatches\n    # Build per-batch candidate lists (already ordered by scaled\
    \ distance)\n    cols_sel = []\n    w_sel = []\n    d_sel = []\n    # pointers per batch\n    ptr = np.zeros(nbatches, dtype=int)\n    # Pre-split candidate positions by batch\n    pos_by_b = [np.where(batch_row == b)[0] for b in range(nbatches)]\n    # 1) Take base from each batch\n    for b in range(nbatches):\n        pos = pos_by_b[b]\n        take = min(base, pos.size)\n        if take > 0:\n            sel_pos = pos[:take]\n            ptr[b] = take\n            cols_sel.append(idx_row[sel_pos])\n            # weights on scaled distances; distances matrix stores raw\n            w_sel.append(1.0 / (dists_scaled_row[sel_pos] + 1e-12))\n            d_sel.append(dists_raw_row[sel_pos])\n    if cols_sel:\n        cols_sel = np.concatenate(cols_sel)\n        w_sel = np.concatenate(w_sel)\n        d_sel = np.concatenate(d_sel)\n    else:\n        cols_sel = np.array([], dtype=int)\n        w_sel = np.array([], dtype=float)\n        d_sel = np.array([], dtype=float)\n\n    # 2) Distribute\
    \ remainder by picking the next-best candidate per batch (smallest next scaled distance)\n    selected_set = set(cols_sel.tolist())\n    for _ in range(rem):\n        best_b = -1\n        best_val = np.inf\n        best_col = None\n        best_w = None\n        best_d = None\n        for b in range(nbatches):\n            pos = pos_by_b[b]\n            p = ptr[b]\n            if p < pos.size:\n                j = pos[p]\n                val = dists_scaled_row[j]\n                if val < best_val and idx_row[j] not in selected_set:\n                    best_val = val\n                    best_b = b\n                    best_col = idx_row[j]\n                    best_w = 1.0 / (dists_scaled_row[j] + 1e-12)\n                    best_d = dists_raw_row[j]\n        if best_b == -1:  # no batch had a candidate\n            break\n        ptr[best_b] += 1\n        selected_set.add(int(best_col))\n        cols_sel = np.append(cols_sel, best_col)\n        w_sel = np.append(w_sel, best_w)\n \
    \       d_sel = np.append(d_sel, best_d)\n\n    # 3) If still short, fill from global best remaining\n    if cols_sel.size < k:\n        # global order by scaled distance\n        order = np.argsort(dists_scaled_row, kind='mergesort')\n        for j in order:\n            col = int(idx_row[j])\n            if col not in selected_set:\n                cols_sel = np.append(cols_sel, col)\n                w_sel = np.append(w_sel, 1.0 / (dists_scaled_row[j] + 1e-12))\n                d_sel = np.append(d_sel, dists_raw_row[j])\n                selected_set.add(col)\n                if cols_sel.size >= k:\n                    break\n\n    # Truncate in rare overfill\n    if cols_sel.size > k:\n        keep = np.argsort(-w_sel)[:k]  # keep strongest\n        cols_sel = cols_sel[keep]\n        w_sel = w_sel[keep]\n        d_sel = d_sel[keep]\n    return cols_sel.astype(int), w_sel.astype(float), d_sel.astype(float)\n\n# ---- Core integration ----\ndef eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData)\
    \ -> ad.AnnData:\n    # Hyperparameters (GraphFWPCA + EQ-quota)\n    n_pcs = 100\n    k = 50\n    kd = 22\n    delta = 0.12\n    kq = 1024\n    mutual_boost = 1.10\n    rng_seed = 0\n\n    # 1) Normalize from counts; optional batch-aware HVGs\n    Xn = _normalize_log1p_from_counts(adata)\n    if 'batch_hvg' in adata.var.columns:\n        mask = adata.var['batch_hvg'].values.astype(bool)\n        if mask.sum() > 0 and mask.sum() < Xn.shape[1]:\n            Xn = Xn[:, mask]\n\n    # 2) PCA embedding (for both embedding output and neighbor search)\n    Z = _pca_svd(Xn, n_components=n_pcs, random_state=rng_seed)\n\n    # 3) kNN candidates on raw PC space (Euclidean)\n    nn = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=kq + 1, metric=\"euclidean\")\n    nn.fit(Z)\n    d_all, idx_all = nn.kneighbors(Z, return_distance=True)\n    # drop self\n    d_raw = d_all[:, 1:]   # (n, kq)\n    idx = idx_all[:, 1:]   # (n, kq)\n\n    n = Z.shape[0]\n    # kd-th local scale (per-row)\n    kd_pos = int(min(kd, d_raw.shape[1]))\
    \ - 1\n    sigma = np.maximum(d_raw[:, kd_pos], 1e-12)  # shape (n,)\n\n    # scaled distances using mean(σ_i, σ_j)^delta\n    sigma_i = sigma[:, None]\n    sigma_j = sigma[idx]\n    sigma_ij = 0.5 * (sigma_i + sigma_j)\n    d_scaled = d_raw / (np.power(sigma_ij, delta) + 1e-12)\n\n    # batch codes for candidates\n    batches = adata.obs['batch']\n    if not pd.api.types.is_categorical_dtype(batches):\n        batches = pd.Categorical(batches)\n        batch_codes = batches.codes\n    else:\n        batch_codes = batches.cat.codes.to_numpy()\n    batch_of_idx = batch_codes[idx]  # (n, kq)\n    nbatches = int(len(batches.categories) if hasattr(batches, 'categories') else batches.cat.categories.size)\n\n    # 4) Equal-quota selection per row\n    rows = []\n    cols = []\n    data_w = []\n    data_d = []\n    for i in range(n):\n        csel, wsel, dsel = _equal_quota_select_per_row(\n            d_scaled[i], d_raw[i], idx[i], batch_of_idx[i], k=k, nbatches=nbatches\n        )\n     \
    \   if csel.size == 0:\n            continue\n        rows.append(np.full(csel.size, i, dtype=int))\n        cols.append(csel)\n        data_w.append(wsel)\n        data_d.append(dsel)\n    if len(rows) == 0:\n        # degenerate fallback: return identity graph\n        I = sp.eye(n, format='csr', dtype=np.float64)\n        adata.obsm['X_emb'] = Z.astype(np.float32)\n        adata.obsp['connectivities'] = I\n        adata.obsp['distances'] = I\n        return adata\n\n    rows = np.concatenate(rows)\n    cols = np.concatenate(cols)\n    data_w = np.concatenate(data_w)\n    data_d = np.concatenate(data_d)\n\n    W_dir = sp.coo_matrix((data_w, (rows, cols)), shape=(n, n)).tocsr()\n    D_dir = sp.coo_matrix((data_d, (rows, cols)), shape=(n, n)).tocsr()\n\n    # 5) Symmetrize (union): weights by max, distances by min; soft mutual boost\n    W_sym = W_dir.maximum(W_dir.T)\n    D_sym = D_dir.minimum(D_dir.T)\n    mutual = W_dir.minimum(W_dir.T)\n    if mutual_boost != 1.0:\n        W_sym\
    \ = W_sym + (mutual_boost - 1.0) * mutual\n\n    # 6) Row-normalize connectivities; ensure CSR float64\n    W_sym = W_sym.tocsr().astype(np.float64)\n    D_sym = D_sym.tocsr().astype(np.float64)\n    row_sum = np.asarray(W_sym.sum(axis=1)).ravel()\n    row_sum[row_sum == 0.0] = 1.0\n    W_sym = _row_scale_csr(W_sym, 1.0 / row_sum)\n\n    # 7) Write outputs\n    adata.obsm['X_emb'] = Z.astype(np.float32)\n    adata.obsp['connectivities'] = W_sym\n    adata.obsp['distances'] = D_sym\n    return adata\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: python storage/system/main.py\nLoading training dataset...\n  Data shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Batches: 4 batches\nFound eliminate_batch_effect_fn, executing...\n\n=== Running batch integration ===\n  Result shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Has embedding: True\n  Has graph: True\n\nResult saved to: storage/shared/tmp/513478e0-806d-4ec1-a28b-53527908b0f0/result_human.h5ad\n\nRESULT_UUID: 513478e0-806d-4ec1-a28b-53527908b0f0\n\
    \n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `submit 1` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Evaluation 'GraphFWPCA + Equal-Quota kNN (no BRBG/ComBat): kd=22, δ=0.12, k=50, kq=1280' submitted for Research Task #1: Single-cell RNA-seq Batch Integration. Evaluation ID: 1632.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Single-cell RNA-seq Batch Integration |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1632 | 1 | GraphFWPCA + Equal-Quota kNN (no BRBG/ComBat): kd=22, δ=0.12, k=50, kq=1280 | Praxis V | 1134 |\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | ARI | ASW_batch | ASW_label | Cell_cycle | Graph_conn | NMI | PCR | cLISI | iLISI | kBET\
    \ |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1632 | 1 | GraphFWPCA + Equal-Quota kNN (no BRBG/ComBat): kd=22, δ=0.12, k=50, kq=1280 | Praxis V | 1134 | running |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 1631 | 1 | GraphFWPCA + Equal-Quota kNN (no BRBG/ComBat): kd=22, δ=0.12, k=50, kq=1024 | Praxis V | 1133 | 0.5177 | 0.720 | 0.667 | 0.205 | 0.295 | 0.889 | 0.717 | 0.000 | 0.980 | 0.096 | 0.608 |\n| 1630 | 1 | ALC Optimization (2/2): k_total = 52 | Nous I | 1133 | 0.7452 | 0.781 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.326 | 0.978 | 0.739 | 1.000 | 0.973 | 0.959 | 0.789 |\n| 1629 | 1 | ALC Optimization (1/2): k_total = 40 | Nous I | 1133 | 0.7371 | 0.745 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.295 | 0.974 | 0.726 | 1.000 | 0.976 | 0.958 | 0.789 |\n| 1628 | 1 | EtC Combat PCs + Ridge + Efficient Equal-Quota Cosine Graph (k=10) + UMAP | Lumen I | 1132 | 0.5165 | 0.344 | 0.000 | 0.148 | 0.342 | 0.720 | 0.599 | 0.801 | 0.977 | 0.379 | 0.854 |\n| 1627 | 1 | ALC Optimization (2/2): lam_override = 0.75 | Nous I\
