parts:
- text: "/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"ComBat-PC Equal-Quota Graph (no BRBG): k=50, kq=1280, kd=22, δ=0.12\"\ntags: \"embed-then-correct, combat, equal-quota, knn, graph, sparse\"\nabstract: \"Ablation: ComBat-corrected PC embedding with equal-quota kNN graph (no residualization). Normalize counts, PCA(100) → ComBat on PCs, then build a k=50 equal-quota graph from kq=1280 Euclidean candidates using GraphFWPCA-style local scaling (kd=22, δ=0.12). Weighted symmetric connectivities via 1/(scaled+eps), true distances retained, row-normalized.\"\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n  import scipy.sparse as sp\n  import pandas as pd\n  import anndata as ad\n  import scanpy as sc\n  from sklearn.decomposition import TruncatedSVD\n  from sklearn.neighbors import NearestNeighbors\n\n  # --- Utilities ---\n  def _to_csr(X):\n      if sp.isspmatrix_csr(X): return X\n      if sp.issparse(X): return X.tocsr()\n      return sp.csr_matrix(X)\n\n  def _row_scale_csr(X, scale):\n      if not\
    \ sp.issparse(X):\n          return (X.T * scale).T\n      X = _to_csr(X).copy()\n      X.data *= np.repeat(scale, np.diff(X.indptr))\n      return X\n\n  def _normalize_log1p_from_counts(adata):\n      Xc = adata.layers['counts'] if 'counts' in adata.layers else adata.X\n      Xc = _to_csr(Xc).astype(np.float32)\n      lib = np.asarray(Xc.sum(axis=1)).ravel()\n      lib = np.maximum(lib, 1e-9)\n      scale = (1e4 / lib).astype(np.float32)\n      Xn = _row_scale_csr(Xc, scale)\n      Xn = Xn.copy()\n      Xn.data = np.log1p(Xn.data)\n      return Xn\n\n  def _pca_svd(X, n_components=100, random_state=0):\n      n_cells, n_genes = X.shape\n      n_components = int(min(n_components, max(2, min(n_cells - 1, n_genes))))\n      svd = TruncatedSVD(n_components=n_components, random_state=random_state)\n      Z = svd.fit_transform(X)\n      return Z.astype(np.float32)\n\n  def _safe_batch_codes(series):\n      # Returns (codes ndarray, nbatches)\n      if not pd.api.types.is_categorical_dtype(series):\n\
    \          cats = pd.Categorical(series)\n          return cats.codes, int(len(cats.categories))\n      else:\n          return series.cat.codes.to_numpy(), int(series.cat.categories.size)\n\n  def _equal_quota_select_per_row(d_scaled_row, d_raw_row, idx_row, batch_row_codes, k, nbatches):\n      base = k // nbatches\n      rem = k - base * nbatches\n      cols_sel, w_sel, d_sel = [], [], []\n      ptr = np.zeros(nbatches, dtype=int)\n      pos_by_b = [np.where(batch_row_codes == b)[0] for b in range(nbatches)]\n      # base picks per batch\n      for b in range(nbatches):\n          pos = pos_by_b[b]\n          take = min(base, pos.size)\n          if take > 0:\n              sel_pos = pos[:take]\n              ptr[b] = take\n              cols_sel.append(idx_row[sel_pos])\n              w_sel.append(1.0 / (d_scaled_row[sel_pos] + 1e-12))\n              d_sel.append(d_raw_row[sel_pos])\n      if cols_sel:\n          cols_sel = np.concatenate(cols_sel); w_sel = np.concatenate(w_sel);\
    \ d_sel = np.concatenate(d_sel)\n      else:\n          cols_sel = np.array([], dtype=int); w_sel = np.array([], dtype=float); d_sel = np.array([], dtype=float)\n      selected = set(cols_sel.tolist())\n      # remainder allocation\n      for _ in range(rem):\n          best_b = -1; best_val = np.inf; best_col = None; best_w = None; best_d = None\n          for b in range(nbatches):\n              pos = pos_by_b[b]; p = ptr[b]\n              if p < pos.size:\n                  j = pos[p]; val = d_scaled_row[j]; cand = int(idx_row[j])\n                  if val < best_val and cand not in selected:\n                      best_val = val; best_b = b; best_col = cand\n                      best_w = 1.0 / (d_scaled_row[j] + 1e-12); best_d = d_raw_row[j]\n          if best_b == -1: break\n          ptr[best_b] += 1; selected.add(best_col)\n          cols_sel = np.append(cols_sel, best_col); w_sel = np.append(w_sel, best_w); d_sel = np.append(d_sel, best_d)\n      # global fill if needed\n  \
    \    if cols_sel.size < k:\n          order = np.argsort(d_scaled_row, kind='mergesort')\n          for j in order:\n              cand = int(idx_row[j])\n              if cand not in selected:\n                  cols_sel = np.append(cols_sel, cand)\n                  w_sel = np.append(w_sel, 1.0 / (d_scaled_row[j] + 1e-12))\n                  d_sel = np.append(d_sel, d_raw_row[j])\n                  selected.add(cand)\n                  if cols_sel.size >= k: break\n      # truncate if overfull\n      if cols_sel.size > k:\n          keep = np.argsort(-w_sel)[:k]\n          cols_sel = cols_sel[keep]; w_sel = w_sel[keep]; d_sel = d_sel[keep]\n      return cols_sel.astype(int), w_sel.astype(float), d_sel.astype(float)\n\n  # --- Entrypoint ---\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      # Hyperparameters\n      n_pcs = 100; k = 50; kd = 22; delta = 0.12; kq = 1280; mutual_boost = 1.10\n\n      # 1) Normalize and feature select\n      Xn = _normalize_log1p_from_counts(adata)\n\
    \      if 'batch_hvg' in adata.var.columns:\n          m = adata.var['batch_hvg'].values.astype(bool)\n          if 0 < m.sum() < Xn.shape[1]:\n              Xn = Xn[:, m]\n\n      # 2) PCs then ComBat on PCs (EtC on embedding path)\n      Z0 = _pca_svd(Xn, n_components=n_pcs, random_state=0)\n      ad_pca = ad.AnnData(X=Z0.copy(), obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n      sc.pp.combat(ad_pca, key='batch')\n      Z = np.asarray(ad_pca.X, dtype=np.float32)\n\n      # 3) Candidate neighbors in ComBat-PC space (Euclidean)\n      nn = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=kq + 1, metric=\"euclidean\")\n      nn.fit(Z)\n      d_all, idx_all = nn.kneighbors(Z, return_distance=True)\n      d_raw = d_all[:, 1:]; idx = idx_all[:, 1:]  # drop self\n      n = Z.shape[0]\n\n      # 4) Local scaling (GraphFWPCA-style) on ComBat-PC distances\n      kd_pos = int(min(kd, d_raw.shape[1])) - 1\n      sigma = np.maximum(d_raw[:, kd_pos], 1e-12)\n      sigma_i = sigma[:, None]; sigma_j = sigma[idx]; sigma_ij = 0.5\
    \ * (sigma_i + sigma_j)\n      d_scaled = d_raw / (np.power(sigma_ij, delta) + 1e-12)\n\n      # 5) Equal-quota selection per row\n      batch_codes, nbatches = _safe_batch_codes(adata.obs['batch'])\n      batch_of_idx = batch_codes[idx]\n      rows = []; cols = []; data_w = []; data_d = []\n      for i in range(n):\n          csel, wsel, dsel = _equal_quota_select_per_row(d_scaled[i], d_raw[i], idx[i], batch_of_idx[i], k=k, nbatches=nbatches)\n          if csel.size == 0: continue\n          rows.append(np.full(csel.size, i, dtype=int)); cols.append(csel)\n          data_w.append(wsel); data_d.append(dsel)\n      if not rows:\n          I = sp.eye(n, format='csr', dtype=np.float64)\n          adata.obsm['X_emb'] = Z; adata.obsp['connectivities'] = I; adata.obsp['distances'] = I\n          return adata\n\n      rows = np.concatenate(rows); cols = np.concatenate(cols)\n      data_w = np.concatenate(data_w); data_d = np.concatenate(data_d)\n\n      W_dir = sp.coo_matrix((data_w, (rows,\
    \ cols)), shape=(n, n)).tocsr()\n      D_dir = sp.coo_matrix((data_d, (rows, cols)), shape=(n, n)).tocsr()\n\n      # 6) Symmetrize and soft mutual boost\n      W_sym = W_dir.maximum(W_dir.T); D_sym = D_dir.minimum(D_dir.T)\n      mutual = W_dir.minimum(W_dir.T)\n      if mutual_boost != 1.0:\n          W_sym = W_sym + (mutual_boost - 1.0) * mutual\n\n      # 7) Row-normalize; set outputs\n      W_sym = W_sym.tocsr().astype(np.float64); D_sym = D_sym.tocsr().astype(np.float64)\n      row_sum = np.asarray(W_sym.sum(axis=1)).ravel(); row_sum[row_sum == 0.0] = 1.0\n      W_sym = _row_scale_csr(W_sym, 1.0 / row_sum)\n\n      adata.obsm['X_emb'] = Z\n      adata.obsp['connectivities'] = W_sym\n      adata.obsp['distances'] = D_sym\n      return adata\n```"
thinking_content: "**Considering ComBat embedding**\n\nI’m looking at the ComBat embedding eq-quota and deciding between Euclidean and cosine distances. I think I’ll choose Euclidean since it showed improvement before, even though the previous equal-quota setup used cosine. Testing both makes sense, especially with our limited concurrency, so I can add another run. I’ll also explore adding safe category codes and writing a utility function for that. Lastly, I need to clarify our active experiments and update any memory watchers.**Planning new experiments**\n\nI’m submitting new experiments, specifically a \"EtC-only + equal-quota Graph\" using ComBat embedding. I plan to extract implementation code from a minimal pipeline but without residualization, using equal-quota with kq=1280. I want a safe function for handling category codes, along with robust code. After submission, I might update private memory with a note. To keep things concise, I’ll combine tasks in one tick. The embedding will\
  \ involve computing PCA60 before running ComBat, ensuring everything is in order.**Simplifying the approach**\n\nI’m thinking about simplifying the process for the equivalent \"EtC,\" which means applying ComBat on PCs. I plan to replicate that setup. For the graph neighbor search, I’ll use the same embedding, Z_graph, as ComBat. By implementing equal-quota graph distance scaled by kd 22, I believe we can enhance the mix. This will create what I’ll call the \"ComBat-corrected PC space eq-quota.\" It feels like this will lead to a better outcome.**Writing the code**\n\nI’m working on the function `eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata)` and starting with getting normalized counts. I’ll use feature selection based on `adata.var['batch_hvg']`. For computing PCs, I think keeping it at 100 makes sense as we used that before. Then, I’ll construct an `adata` for ComBat, ensuring to import the necessary libraries. \n\nNext, I’ll build neighbor candidates using Euclidean distances with kq=1280 and compute\
  \ the kd-th local scale. For neighbors, I’ll follow the earlier selection logic, apply soft mutual and row normalization while also implementing safe categorical codes to maintain robustness and avoid dependencies.**Implementing actions**\n\nI’m ready to implement the necessary actions now. I’ll execute the action to submit the first experiment, titled \"ComBat-PC eq-quota kq=1280.\" While I could add some utility functions for storage, it’s not strictly needed right now. \n\nI’ll make sure to keep the code minimal and clear. I’ll import essential libraries like NumPy, SciPy, Pandas, Scanpy, and AnnData. For normalization and PCA functions, I’ll follow the same approach as before. I'll ensure batch codes are detected correctly, taking care to define `nbatches` properly across different branches to avoid potential pitfalls. Lastly, I’ll check for connectivity values and confirm there’s no test function for scoring."
