- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 1136\n- Station Status: Stagnation\n- Agent Name: Praxis V\n- Agent Description: Parsimonious, hypothesis-driven scRNA integration researcher continuing MPB-GraphFWPCA+BRBG+DAQB with rigorous ablations, reproducibility, and interpretable, steady gains.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\nPraxis V — standby (all Heart branches frozen)\n- Publications: #48 (δ topology dependence), #51 (kq across baselines) + cost addendum.\n- Closures: Ridge near‑SOTA stable; Minimal eq‑quota frozen; GraphFWPCA‑only negative.\n- Watchers: Research Counter (new organ/tasks, SOTA shifts), Archive previews.\n- On new organ: run ridge δ∈{0.10,0.12}, kd=22, k=50 with seeds {0,1}; template and runbook in storage/praxis.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 118,669 / 270,000 used (44%)\n- Agent Age: 165 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour submission has been queued for evaluation. Results will be sent to you\
    \ once the evaluation completes.\n### Message 2\n\nYour research submission 'GraphFWPCA + Equal-Quota kNN (no BRBG/ComBat): kd=22, δ=0.12, k=50, kq=1280' (ID: 1632) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 0.5175513253382193\n**ASW_batch:** 0.667\n**ASW_label:** 0.205\n**ARI:** 0.720\n**NMI:** 0.717\n**Graph_conn:** 0.889\n**kBET:** 0.607\n**iLISI:** 0.096\n**cLISI:** 0.980\n**PCR:** 0.000\n**Cell_cycle:** 0.295\n**Evaluation Details:** Human Dataset (20,000 cells):\nNormalized Scores [0-1]:\n  ASW_batch: 0.667  ASW_label: 0.205  ARI: 0.720  NMI: 0.717\n  Graph_conn: 0.889  kBET: 0.607  iLISI: 0.096  cLISI: 0.980\n  PCR: 0.000  Cell_cycle: 0.295\n\nRaw Scores (before normalization):\n  ASW_batch: 0.833884  ASW_label: 0.529749  ARI: 0.720091  NMI: 0.716872\n  Graph_conn: 0.890908  kBET: 0.581500  iLISI: 0.096465  cLISI: 0.994092\n  PCR: 0.000000  Cell_cycle: 0.260778\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 1632\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed pandas Categorical\
    \ accessor bugs in batch processing code. The submission now runs without errors and achieves a score of 0.517.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original code had incorrect pandas API usage when working with Categorical data. In pandas, when you have a Series containing categorical values, you must use the `.cat` accessor to access categorical-specific attributes:\n\n1. **Line 59 (v1)**: `batches.codes` - Attempted to access `.codes` directly on the Series\n2. **Line 59 (v1)**: `batches.categories.size` - Attempted to access `.categories` directly on the Series\n\nBoth of these caused `AttributeError` because the Series object doesn't have these attributes at the top level - they're only accessible through the `.cat` accessor.\n\n## Fix Applied\n\n### Version 2 (v2)\nChanged line 59 from:\n```python\nbatch_codes = batches.codes.to_numpy()\n```\nTo:\n```python\nbatch_codes = batches.cat.codes.to_numpy()\n```\n\n**Result**: Fixed the first error, but revealed a second error with `batches.categories.size`.\n\
    \n### Version 3 (v3) - SUCCESSFUL\nChanged the complete line from:\n```python\nbatch_codes = batches.cat.codes.to_numpy(); batch_of_idx = batch_codes[idx]; nbatches = int(batches.categories.size)\n```\nTo:\n```python\nbatch_codes = batches.cat.codes.to_numpy(); batch_of_idx = batch_codes[idx]; nbatches = int(batches.cat.categories.size)\n```\n\n**Result**: Code runs successfully without crashes.\n\n## Evaluation Results\n- **Status**: Completed\n- **Score**: 0.5175513253382193\n- **Success**: True\n- **Fixed in**: Version v3 (submission_v3.py)\n\n## Technical Details\nThe fix ensures proper pandas API usage:\n- `batches.cat.codes` - Returns the integer codes for categorical values\n- `batches.cat.categories.size` - Returns the number of unique categories\n\nThis is the correct way to access categorical attributes when working with pandas Series objects that contain categorical data.\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies\
    \ on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v3):**\n```python\nimport numpy as np\nimport scipy.sparse as sp\nfrom sklearn.decomposition import TruncatedSVD\nfrom sklearn.neighbors import NearestNeighbors\nimport pandas as pd\nimport anndata as ad\n\ndef _to_csr(X):\n    if sp.isspmatrix_csr(X): return X\n    if sp.issparse(X): return X.tocsr()\n    return sp.csr_matrix(X)\n\ndef _row_scale_csr(X, scale):\n    if not sp.issparse(X):\n        return (X.T * scale).T\n    X = _to_csr(X).copy()\n    X.data *= np.repeat(scale, np.diff(X.indptr))\n    return X\n\ndef _normalize_log1p_from_counts(adata):\n    Xc = adata.layers['counts'] if 'counts' in adata.layers else adata.X\n    Xc = _to_csr(Xc).astype(np.float32)\n    lib = np.asarray(Xc.sum(axis=1)).ravel()\n    lib = np.maximum(lib, 1e-9)\n    scale = (1e4 / lib).astype(np.float32)\n    Xn = _row_scale_csr(Xc, scale)\n    Xn = Xn.copy()\n    Xn.data = np.log1p(Xn.data)\n    return Xn\n\ndef _pca_svd(X,\
    \ n_components=100, random_state=0):\n    n_cells, n_genes = X.shape\n    n_components = int(min(n_components, max(2, min(n_cells - 1, n_genes))))\n    svd = TruncatedSVD(n_components=n_components, random_state=random_state)\n    Z = svd.fit_transform(X)\n    return Z.astype(np.float32)\n\ndef _equal_quota_select_per_row(dists_scaled_row, dists_raw_row, idx_row, batch_row, k, nbatches):\n    base = k // nbatches\n    rem = k - base * nbatches\n    cols_sel, w_sel, d_sel = [], [], []\n    ptr = np.zeros(nbatches, dtype=int)\n    pos_by_b = [np.where(batch_row == b)[0] for b in range(nbatches)]\n    for b in range(nbatches):\n        pos = pos_by_b[b]\n        take = min(base, pos.size)\n        if take > 0:\n            sel_pos = pos[:take]\n            ptr[b] = take\n            cols_sel.append(idx_row[sel_pos])\n            w_sel.append(1.0 / (dists_scaled_row[sel_pos] + 1e-12))\n            d_sel.append(dists_raw_row[sel_pos])\n    if cols_sel:\n        cols_sel = np.concatenate(cols_sel);\
    \ w_sel = np.concatenate(w_sel); d_sel = np.concatenate(d_sel)\n    else:\n        cols_sel = np.array([], dtype=int); w_sel = np.array([], dtype=float); d_sel = np.array([], dtype=float)\n    selected_set = set(cols_sel.tolist())\n    for _ in range(rem):\n        best_b = -1; best_val = np.inf; best_col = None; best_w = None; best_d = None\n        for b in range(nbatches):\n            pos = pos_by_b[b]; p = ptr[b]\n            if p < pos.size:\n                j = pos[p]; val = dists_scaled_row[j]\n                cand = int(idx_row[j])\n                if val < best_val and cand not in selected_set:\n                    best_val = val; best_b = b; best_col = cand\n                    best_w = 1.0 / (dists_scaled_row[j] + 1e-12); best_d = dists_raw_row[j]\n        if best_b == -1: break\n        ptr[best_b] += 1; selected_set.add(best_col)\n        cols_sel = np.append(cols_sel, best_col); w_sel = np.append(w_sel, best_w); d_sel = np.append(d_sel, best_d)\n    if cols_sel.size <\
    \ k:\n        order = np.argsort(dists_scaled_row, kind='mergesort')\n        for j in order:\n            cand = int(idx_row[j])\n            if cand not in selected_set:\n                cols_sel = np.append(cols_sel, cand)\n                w_sel = np.append(w_sel, 1.0 / (dists_scaled_row[j] + 1e-12))\n                d_sel = np.append(d_sel, dists_raw_row[j])\n                selected_set.add(cand)\n                if cols_sel.size >= k: break\n    if cols_sel.size > k:\n        keep = np.argsort(-w_sel)[:k]\n        cols_sel = cols_sel[keep]; w_sel = w_sel[keep]; d_sel = d_sel[keep]\n    return cols_sel.astype(int), w_sel.astype(float), d_sel.astype(float)\n\ndef eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n    n_pcs = 100; k = 50; kd = 22; delta = 0.12; kq = 1280; mutual_boost = 1.10\n    Xn = _normalize_log1p_from_counts(adata)\n    if 'batch_hvg' in adata.var.columns:\n        mask = adata.var['batch_hvg'].values.astype(bool)\n        if 0 < mask.sum() < Xn.shape[1]:\
    \ Xn = Xn[:, mask]\n    Z = _pca_svd(Xn, n_components=n_pcs, random_state=0)\n    nn = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=kq + 1, metric=\"euclidean\"); nn.fit(Z)\n    d_all, idx_all = nn.kneighbors(Z, return_distance=True)\n    d_raw = d_all[:, 1:]; idx = idx_all[:, 1:]\n    n = Z.shape[0]; kd_pos = int(min(kd, d_raw.shape[1])) - 1\n    sigma = np.maximum(d_raw[:, kd_pos], 1e-12)\n    sigma_i = sigma[:, None]; sigma_j = sigma[idx]; sigma_ij = 0.5 * (sigma_i + sigma_j)\n    d_scaled = d_raw / (np.power(sigma_ij, delta) + 1e-12)\n    batches = adata.obs['batch'];\n    if not pd.api.types.is_categorical_dtype(batches): batches = pd.Categorical(batches)\n    batch_codes = batches.cat.codes.to_numpy(); batch_of_idx = batch_codes[idx]; nbatches = int(batches.cat.categories.size)\n    rows = []; cols = []; data_w = []; data_d = []\n    for i in range(n):\n        csel, wsel, dsel = _equal_quota_select_per_row(d_scaled[i], d_raw[i], idx[i], batch_of_idx[i], k=k, nbatches=nbatches)\n        if csel.size\
    \ == 0: continue\n        rows.append(np.full(csel.size, i, dtype=int)); cols.append(csel); data_w.append(wsel); data_d.append(dsel)\n    if len(rows) == 0:\n        I = sp.eye(n, format='csr', dtype=np.float64)\n        adata.obsm['X_emb'] = Z.astype(np.float32); adata.obsp['connectivities'] = I; adata.obsp['distances'] = I\n        return adata\n    rows = np.concatenate(rows); cols = np.concatenate(cols); data_w = np.concatenate(data_w); data_d = np.concatenate(data_d)\n    W_dir = sp.coo_matrix((data_w, (rows, cols)), shape=(n, n)).tocsr()\n    D_dir = sp.coo_matrix((data_d, (rows, cols)), shape=(n, n)).tocsr()\n    W_sym = W_dir.maximum(W_dir.T); D_sym = D_dir.minimum(D_dir.T)\n    mutual = W_dir.minimum(W_dir.T)\n    if mutual_boost != 1.0: W_sym = W_sym + (mutual_boost - 1.0) * mutual\n    W_sym = W_sym.tocsr().astype(np.float64); D_sym = D_sym.tocsr().astype(np.float64)\n    row_sum = np.asarray(W_sym.sum(axis=1)).ravel(); row_sum[row_sum == 0.0] = 1.0\n    W_sym = _row_scale_csr(W_sym,\
    \ 1.0 / row_sum)\n    adata.obsm['X_emb'] = Z.astype(np.float32); adata.obsp['connectivities'] = W_sym; adata.obsp['distances'] = D_sym\n    return adata\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: python storage/system/main.py\nLoading training dataset...\n  Data shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Batches: 4 batches\nFound eliminate_batch_effect_fn, executing...\n\n=== Running batch integration ===\n  Result shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Has embedding: True\n  Has graph: True\n\nResult saved to: storage/shared/tmp/bf02c301-8916-43a6-9d41-c97636b5ede4/result_human.h5ad\n\nRESULT_UUID: bf02c301-8916-43a6-9d41-c97636b5ede4\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n### Message 3\n\n**Automatic System Tips**\nTo investigate the research landscape of a given direction, use Research Counter's `filter tag` to obtain an overview of relevant submissions, and `preview ids` to preview those submissions by their IDs. Use `page_size 100` if you want to see more IDs — but remember to\
    \ set it back to 10 in a later tick, or it will consume too many tokens!\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `submit 1` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Evaluation 'ComBat-PC Equal-Quota Graph (no BRBG): k=50, kq=1280, kd=22, δ=0.12' submitted for Research Task #1: Single-cell RNA-seq Batch Integration. Evaluation ID: 1633.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Single-cell RNA-seq Batch Integration |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1633 | 1 | ComBat-PC Equal-Quota Graph (no BRBG): k=50, kq=1280, kd=22, δ=0.12 | Praxis V | 1135 |\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | ARI | ASW_batch | ASW_label | Cell_cycle | Graph_conn\
