thinking_content: "**Evaluating scaling and quotas**\n\nI'm considering how quotas should enhance mixing. However, it seems the d_scaled using ComBat distances can lead to very small scaled distances, which might weight near-identical global structures too heavily. I've noticed mixing collapse previously with GraphFWPCA-only runs, and the iLISI value of 0.096 aligns with those. It appears the equal-quota isn't fixing mixing effectively. I’m thinking about testing cosine instead. We’re at 46% tokens used in a multi-agent environment, which is manageable. I’ll wait for the results from 1637/1638 and then make further adjustments.**Planning actions**\n\nFirst, I want to review the results from tasks 1637 and 1638 when they're finished, but they're still running. I could make a note in private memory about the watchlist, though it feels like it might not be necessary. \n\nI’m considering combining ComBat PC with BRBG for a small generalization test to see if that recovers iLISI, but we’ve had\
  \ minimal eq-quota previously. Still, I should avoid running extra experiments since the meta suggests freezing. Instead, I’ll create a closure note for the ComBat eq-quota ablation and await results. It’s important to manage state based on the last user message.**Deciding next steps**\n\nI think it’s fine that the \"Action not necessary\" note is there, but I want to make sure to perform relevant actions like filtering tags, reviewing results, and setting watchers before going to Reflection or exiting. \n\nThere's also an \"Exit\" option if we run out of tasks, although we typically stick around. I’m considering producing a \"rank author\" to elevate our submissions. Setting watchers to manage \"meta\" seems like a good idea. \n\nI should also think about token management to prune some ticks, but it looks like we're on cooldown for that; we have about two ticks left.**Assessing next actions**\n\nIt seems we can’t prune at the moment. I’m thinking about preparing the code for a new organ,\
  \ specifically working with new_organ_entry.py and the runbook. \n\nWe could reply to Aethel’s previous email, but I think we've already done that. I want to check if tasks 1637 and 1638 are finished, so maybe I can use rank author with a page size of 100. \n\nSince reviewing would require logs that aren’t available yet, I’ll hold off on that. Perhaps I can log watchers in Private Memory or go to the Archive. I’m also considering whether to enter the Reflection Chamber for some thoughts. There’s a \"reflect\" action there, so I might give that a try!**Continuing with minimal actions**\n\nIt looks like the user hasn’t asked anything specific; they only posted system information. I think it makes sense to continue with minimal actions. \n\nI’ll head to research, using rank author with a page size of 20, which is a default setting. To be proactive, I’ll unify our efforts by checking if tasks 1637 and 1638 are complete; if so, I’ll read them next tick. My plan is to set up meta watchers and\
  \ freeze the branch. \n\nI’ll also create a closure note in Private Memory regarding ComBat eq-quota based on the results, while keeping things minimal and avoiding heavy YAML content. Let's implement that!"
