parts:
- text: "/execute_action{rank author}\n/execute_action{page_size 20}\n/execute_action{storage write praxis/gbw_graph.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n  import scipy.sparse as sp\n  from sklearn.decomposition import TruncatedSVD\n  from sklearn.neighbors import NearestNeighbors\n  import anndata as ad\n\n  EPS = 1e-12\n\n  # ---------- Utilities ----------\n  def _to_csr(X):\n      if sp.isspmatrix_csr(X): return X\n      if sp.issparse(X): return X.tocsr()\n      return sp.csr_matrix(X)\n\n  def _row_scale_csr(X, scale):\n      if not sp.issparse(X):\n          return (X.T * scale).T\n      X = _to_csr(X).copy()\n      X.data *= np.repeat(scale, np.diff(X.indptr))\n      return X\n\n  def _normalize_log1p_from_counts(adata):\n      Xc = adata.layers['counts'] if 'counts' in adata.layers else adata.X\n      Xc = _to_csr(Xc).astype(np.float32)\n      lib = np.asarray(Xc.sum(axis=1)).ravel()\n      lib = np.maximum(lib, EPS)\n      scl = (1e4 / lib).astype(np.float32)\n     \
    \ Xn = _row_scale_csr(Xc, scl)\n      Xn = Xn.copy()\n      Xn.data = np.log1p(Xn.data)\n      return Xn\n\n  def _pca_truncated(X, n_components=100, random_state=0):\n      n_cells, n_genes = X.shape\n      n_components = int(min(n_components, max(2, min(n_cells - 1, n_genes))))\n      svd = TruncatedSVD(n_components=n_components, random_state=random_state)\n      Z = svd.fit_transform(X)\n      return Z.astype(np.float32)\n\n  # ---------- GBW graph builder ----------\n  def gbw_knn(\n      Z: np.ndarray,\n      batches,\n      k=50,\n      kd=22,\n      delta=0.12,\n      kq=1024,\n      gamma=0.5,\n      metric=\"cosine\",\n      mutual_boost=1.10,\n      use_adjusted_weight=False,\n      n_jobs=-1,\n  ):\n      \"\"\"\n      Globally Balanced Weighted kNN with kd-th neighbor local scaling.\n      - Z: (n x d) embedding\n      - batches: array-like length n (batch labels)\n      Steps:\n        1) Candidate search (kq) with metric\n        2) Local scaling via kd-th neighbor: scaled\
    \ = d / mean(sigma_i, sigma_j)^delta\n        3) Base similarity s = 1 / (scaled + EPS)\n        4) Global batch reweight before selection: s_adj = s / p(batch_j)^gamma\n           where p computed from dataset-wide batch frequencies.\n        5) Select top-k by s_adj\n        6) Symmetrize (union max for weights; min for raw distances)\n        7) Soft mutual boost (on intersection)\n        8) Row-normalize weights\n      Returns (W_conn CSR float64, D_dist CSR float64 with RAW distances)\n      \"\"\"\n      n = Z.shape[0]\n      # Candidate neighbors (exclude self)\n      nn = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=int(kq) + 1, metric=metric, n_jobs=n_jobs)\n      nn.fit(Z)\n      d_all, idx_all = nn.kneighbors(Z, return_distance=True)\n      d = d_all[:, 1:]      # raw distances (n, kq)\n      idx = idx_all[:, 1:]  # neighbor indices (n, kq)\n\n      # kd scaling\n      kd_pos = int(min(kd, d.shape[1])) - 1\n      sigma = np.maximum(d[:, kd_pos], EPS)         # (n,)\n      sigma_i = sigma[:,\
    \ None]                      # (n, kq)\n      sigma_j = sigma[idx]                          # (n, kq)\n      sigma_ij = 0.5 * (sigma_i + sigma_j)\n      scaled = d / (np.power(sigma_ij, delta) + EPS)\n\n      # base similarity\n      s = 1.0 / (scaled + EPS)\n\n      # global batch frequencies via inverse mapping\n      batches = np.asarray(batches)\n      _, b_inv = np.unique(batches, return_inverse=True)  # (n,) int ids\n      counts = np.bincount(b_inv, minlength=b_inv.max() + 1).astype(np.float64)\n      freq = counts / float(n)                             # (nb,)\n      nb_idx = b_inv[idx]                                  # (n, kq)\n      p_nb = freq[nb_idx]                                  # (n, kq)\n\n      s_adj = s / (np.power(p_nb, gamma) + EPS)\n\n      # select top-k by adjusted similarity\n      k_keep = int(min(k, s_adj.shape[1]))\n      part = np.argpartition(-s_adj, kth=k_keep - 1, axis=1)[:, :k_keep]\n\n      rows = np.repeat(np.arange(n), k_keep)\n      cols = idx[np.arange(n)[:,\
    \ None], part].ravel()\n\n      # choose stored weights\n      weights = s_adj if use_adjusted_weight else s\n      data_w = weights[np.arange(n)[:, None], part].ravel()\n      # raw distances for spec compliance\n      data_d = d[np.arange(n)[:, None], part].ravel()\n\n      W_dir = sp.coo_matrix((data_w, (rows, cols)), shape=(n, n)).tocsr()\n      D_dir = sp.coo_matrix((data_d, (rows, cols)), shape=(n, n)).tocsr()\n\n      # symmetrize\n      W_sym = W_dir.maximum(W_dir.T)\n      D_sym = D_dir.minimum(D_dir.T)\n\n      # mutual boost\n      mutual = W_dir.minimum(W_dir.T)\n      if mutual_boost != 1.0:\n          W_sym = W_sym + (mutual_boost - 1.0) * mutual\n\n      # row normalize\n      W_sym = W_sym.tocsr().astype(np.float64)\n      D_sym = D_sym.tocsr().astype(np.float64)\n      rs = np.asarray(W_sym.sum(axis=1)).ravel()\n      rs[rs == 0.0] = 1.0\n      W_sym = _row_scale_csr(W_sym, 1.0 / rs)\n      return W_sym, D_sym\n\n  def integrate_gbw_graphfwpca(\n      adata: ad.AnnData,\n\
    \      n_pcs=100,\n      k=50,\n      kd=22,\n      delta=0.12,\n      kq=1024,\n      gamma=0.5,\n      metric=\"cosine\",\n      mutual_boost=1.10,\n      use_adjusted_weight=False,\n      seed=0,\n  ) -> ad.AnnData:\n      \"\"\"\n      End-to-end integrator: counts → PCA → GBW graph (returns obsp['connectivities'/'distances'] and obsm['X_emb']).\n      \"\"\"\n      Xn = _normalize_log1p_from_counts(adata)\n      if 'batch_hvg' in adata.var.columns:\n          mask = adata.var['batch_hvg'].values.astype(bool)\n          if mask.sum() > 0 and mask.sum() < Xn.shape[1]:\n              Xn = Xn[:, mask]\n      Z = _pca_truncated(Xn, n_components=n_pcs, random_state=seed)\n      C, D = gbw_knn(\n          Z, adata.obs['batch'].values, k=k, kd=kd, delta=delta, kq=kq,\n          gamma=gamma, metric=metric, mutual_boost=mutual_boost,\n          use_adjusted_weight=use_adjusted_weight, n_jobs=-1\n      )\n      adata.obsm['X_emb'] = Z.astype(np.float32)\n      adata.obsp['connectivities']\
    \ = C\n      adata.obsp['distances'] = D\n      return adata\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto private_memory}\n/execute_action{create}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"GBW plan — queued gamma sweep; next variants\"\ncontent: |\n  Context\n  - Submitted GBW‑GraphFWPCA (global batch reweighting before top‑k) with γ∈{0.5, 1.0}, kq=1024, kd‑scale δ=0.12, cosine.\n  - Goal: improve mixing without explicit quotas; compare to EQ‑quota and ridge baselines.\n\n  Next (wait for concurrency to clear, then submit):\n  - Use adjusted weights in connectivity (use_adjusted_weight=True) vs base weights (stored s) now.\n  - kq=1280 (γ=best_of_{0.5,1.0}); keep k=50 fixed.\n  - Metric probe: Euclidean vs cosine at the best γ.\n  - Sanity: ensure distances stored are RAW (fixed in gbw_graph.py); keep evaluator neighbors meta standard.\n\n  Success criteria\n  - Primary score ↑ with iLISI ↑ and minimal ARI/NMI regression; Graph_conn within ridge variance.\n  - If GBW underperforms EQ‑quota, freeze branch and document as negative.\n\
    ```"
