  I’m working through edge weights. I have formulas for s and s_adj, which I''ll use based on whether I need adjusted weights. I need to decide if distances represent actual distances or scaled ones. The spec indicates they should be actual distances between connected neighbors, but past implementations used scaled distances. For compliance, I should store raw distances instead. So, I’ll switch to ensuring we''re using raw distances ''d'' for the selected pairs.**Finalizing distance selection**


  After selecting neighbors using s_adj, I''ve got ''idx'' and ''part'' to work with. I can pull ''data_d_raw = d[row, colIndices]'', but I''ll need to ensure I get ''raw_d'' accurately shaped since ''d'' is from full kq. I’ll store D_dir from raw distances and adjust W based on the chosen weights. To symmetrize distances, I''ll take the minimum, while connecting max union for connectivities. Okay, I’ll write ''gbw_graph.py'' and make a memory note before wrapping up!'
