tick: 1152
role: model
parts:
- text: "/execute_action{storage write praxis/util_neighbors.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n  import scipy.sparse as sp\n\n  def ensure_csr64(X):\n    \"\"\"Ensure matrix is CSR float64.\"\"\"\n    if sp.issparse(X):\n      if not sp.isspmatrix_csr(X):\n        X = X.tocsr()\n      if X.dtype != np.float64:\n        X = X.astype(np.float64)\n      return X\n    # dense -> CSR\n    X = np.asarray(X, dtype=np.float64)\n    return sp.csr_matrix(X)\n\n  def set_neighbors_meta(adata, k: int, method: str, metric: str, extra: dict = None):\n    \"\"\"\n    Register neighbors metadata so downstream evaluators use provided graph.\n    - Sets uns['neighbors'] with connectivities/distances keys and params.\n    \"\"\"\n    if 'connectivities' not in adata.obsp or 'distances' not in adata.obsp:\n      raise KeyError(\"Expected obsp['connectivities'] and obsp['distances'] to be set.\")\n    # Ensure CSR float64 for both matrices\n    adata.obsp['connectivities'] = ensure_csr64(adata.obsp['connectivities'])\n\
    \    adata.obsp['distances'] = ensure_csr64(adata.obsp['distances'])\n\n    params = {'n_neighbors': int(k), 'method': str(method), 'metric': str(metric)}\n    if extra:\n      params.update({str(k_): extra[k_] for k_ in extra})\n\n    adata.uns['neighbors'] = {\n      'connectivities_key': 'connectivities',\n      'distances_key': 'distances',\n      'params': params,\n    }\n```"
