tick: 1161
role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 1161\n- Station Status: Stagnation\n- Agent Name: Praxis V\n- Agent Description: Parsimonious, hypothesis-driven scRNA integration researcher continuing MPB-GraphFWPCA+BRBG+DAQB with rigorous ablations, reproducibility, and interpretable, steady gains.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\nPraxis V — standby (GBW closed)\n- New negatives: GBW‑GraphFWPCA γ∈{0.5,1.0} both fail (iLISI≈0.096, PCR=0.0). Branch frozen and documented in Archive #51 addendum and private plan.\n- Heart remains fully closed; near‑SOTA ridge stable; minimal track frozen.\n- Next action only on new organ: run ridge δ∈{0.10,0.12}, kd=22, k=50 with seeds {0,1} using stored entrypoints.\n- Watchers active; maintain token hygiene.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 136,041 / 270,000 used (50%)\n- Agent Age: 190 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Evaluation Review: 1662**\n\n**Research Submission Review**\n\n**Title:**\
    \ Ridge GraphFWPCA + gene-wise unit-variance scaling (zero_center=False): δ=0.12, k=50, kd=22\n**ID:** 1662\n**Tags:** graph, pca, scaling, standardization, kd-scaling\n**Abstract:** One-probe test: apply column-wise unit-variance scaling to log1p-normalized counts (no centering) before PCA, then build GraphFWPCA ridge (δ=0.12, k=50, kd=22). Returns weighted connectivities/distances and PCA embedding; logs graph stats and σ_kd summary for diagnostics.\n**Score:** 0.5394121789745605\n**ASW_batch:** 0.644\n**ASW_label:** 0.195\n**ARI:** 0.785\n**NMI:** 0.749\n**Graph_conn:** 0.964\n**kBET:** 0.633\n**iLISI:** 0.132\n**cLISI:** 0.955\n**PCR:** 0.104\n**Cell_cycle:** 0.235\n**Evaluation Details:** Human Dataset (20,000 cells):\nNormalized Scores [0-1]:\n  ASW_batch: 0.644  ASW_label: 0.195  ARI: 0.785  NMI: 0.749\n  Graph_conn: 0.964  kBET: 0.633  iLISI: 0.132  cLISI: 0.955\n  PCR: 0.104  Cell_cycle: 0.235\n\nRaw Scores (before normalization):\n  ASW_batch: 0.823410  ASW_label: 0.524050\
    \  ARI: 0.784819  NMI: 0.748856\n  Graph_conn: 0.964433  kBET: 0.605963  iLISI: 0.131632  cLISI: 0.986789\n  PCR: 0.104352  Cell_cycle: 0.209445\n\n**Submission Code:**\n```python\nimport sys\nimport numpy as np\nimport scipy.sparse as sp\nfrom sklearn.decomposition import TruncatedSVD\nfrom sklearn.neighbors import NearestNeighbors\nimport anndata as ad\n\n# Optional diagnostics from storage\nsys.path.append('storage/praxis')\ntry:\n    from runtime_logging import log_graph_stats\nexcept Exception:\n    def log_graph_stats(adata, title=\"Graph summary\"): pass\ntry:\n    from diag_sigma_kd import summarize_sigma_kd\nexcept Exception:\n    def summarize_sigma_kd(*args, **kwargs): return {}, None\ntry:\n    from util_neighbors import set_neighbors_meta\nexcept Exception:\n    def set_neighbors_meta(adata, k, method, metric, extra=None): pass\n\n# ---- Utilities ----\n\ndef _to_csr(X):\n    if sp.isspmatrix_csr(X): return X\n    if sp.issparse(X): return X.tocsr()\n    return sp.csr_matrix(X)\n\
    \ndef _row_scale_csr(X, scale):\n    if not sp.issparse(X):\n        return (X.T * scale).T\n    X = _to_csr(X).copy()\n    X.data *= np.repeat(scale, np.diff(X.indptr))\n    return X\n\ndef _normalize_log1p_from_counts(adata):\n    Xc = adata.layers['counts'] if 'counts' in adata.layers else adata.X\n    Xc = _to_csr(Xc).astype(np.float32)\n    lib = np.asarray(Xc.sum(axis=1)).ravel()\n    lib = np.maximum(lib, 1e-9)\n    scale = (1e4 / lib).astype(np.float32)\n    Xn = _row_scale_csr(Xc, scale)\n    Xn = Xn.copy()\n    Xn.data = np.log1p(Xn.data)\n    return Xn\n\ndef _hvg_mask(adata, X):\n    if hasattr(adata, \"var\") and 'batch_hvg' in adata.var.columns:\n        mask = adata.var['batch_hvg'].values.astype(bool)\n        if 0 < mask.sum() < X.shape[1]:\n            return mask\n    return None\n\ndef _scale_unit_variance_cols(X):\n    \"\"\"\n    Column-wise unit-variance scaling without centering (zero_center=False analogue).\n    Works on sparse CSR using right-multiplication\
    \ by diag(1/sigma).\n    \"\"\"\n    X = _to_csr(X).astype(np.float32)\n    n = X.shape[0]\n    sum_ = np.asarray(X.sum(axis=0)).ravel().astype(np.float64)\n    sumsq_ = np.asarray(X.multiply(X).sum(axis=0)).ravel().astype(np.float64)\n    mean = sum_ / max(1, n)\n    m2 = sumsq_ / max(1, n)\n    var = m2 - mean**2\n    var[var <= 1e-8] = 1.0\n    inv_std = (1.0 / np.sqrt(var)).astype(np.float32)\n    D = sp.diags(inv_std, format='csr')\n    Xs = (X @ D).tocsr()\n    return Xs\n\ndef _pca_truncated(X, n_components=100, random_state=0):\n    n_cells, n_genes = X.shape\n    n_components = int(min(n_components, max(2, min(n_cells - 1, n_genes))))\n    svd = TruncatedSVD(n_components=n_components, random_state=random_state)\n    Z = svd.fit_transform(X)\n    return Z.astype(np.float32)\n\ndef _build_knn(Z, k=50, kd=22, delta=0.12, extra=10, metric='euclidean'):\n    n = Z.shape[0]\n    kq = int(max(k, kd) + extra)\n    nn = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=kq + 1, metric=metric)\n    nn.fit(Z)\n\
    \    d_all, idx_all = nn.kneighbors(Z, return_distance=True)\n    d = d_all[:, 1:]\n    idx = idx_all[:, 1:]\n\n    kd_pos = int(min(kd, d.shape[1])) - 1\n    sigma = np.maximum(d[:, kd_pos], 1e-12)\n    sigma_i = sigma[:, None]\n    sigma_j = sigma[idx]\n    sigma_ij = 0.5 * (sigma_i + sigma_j)\n    scaled = d / (np.power(sigma_ij, delta) + 1e-12)\n\n    w = 1.0 / (scaled + 1e-12)\n    k_keep = int(min(k, w.shape[1]))\n    part = np.argpartition(-w, kth=k_keep - 1, axis=1)[:, :k_keep]\n    rows = np.repeat(np.arange(n), k_keep)\n    cols = idx[np.arange(n)[:, None], part].ravel()\n    data_w = w[np.arange(n)[:, None], part].ravel()\n    data_d = scaled[np.arange(n)[:, None], part].ravel()\n\n    W_dir = sp.coo_matrix((data_w, (rows, cols)), shape=(n, n)).tocsr()\n    D_dir = sp.coo_matrix((data_d, (rows, cols)), shape=(n, n)).tocsr()\n    W_sym = W_dir.maximum(W_dir.T)\n    D_sym = D_dir.minimum(D_dir.T)\n\n    mutual = W_dir.minimum(W_dir.T)\n    mu = 1.10\n    if mu != 1.0:\n    \
    \    W_sym = W_sym + (mu - 1.0) * mutual\n\n    W_sym = W_sym.tocsr().astype(np.float64)\n    D_sym = D_sym.tocsr().astype(np.float64)\n\n    row_sum = np.asarray(W_sym.sum(axis=1)).ravel()\n    row_sum[row_sum == 0] = 1.0\n    W_sym = _row_scale_csr(W_sym, 1.0 / row_sum)\n    return W_sym, D_sym\n\n# ---- Submission entrypoint ----\n\ndef eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n    \"\"\"\n    Pipeline:\n      1) counts -> library-size normalize (1e4) + log1p\n      2) Optional HVG mask\n      3) Column-wise unit-variance scaling (no centering)\n      4) PCA (100)\n      5) GraphFWPCA ridge: k=50, kd=22, δ=0.12, soft mutual boost\n    Returns obsm['X_emb'], obsp['connectivities'], obsp['distances']; logs diagnostics.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Hyperparameters\n    n_pcs = 100\n    k, kd, delta = 50, 22, 0.12\n\n    # 1) Normalize\n    Xn = _normalize_log1p_from_counts(adata)\n\n    # 2) HVG mask if available\n    mask = _hvg_mask(adata, Xn)\n    if mask is not None:\n \
    \       Xn = Xn[:, mask]\n\n    # 3) Unit-variance scaling (zero_center=False analogue)\n    Xs = _scale_unit_variance_cols(Xn)\n\n    # 4) PCA\n    Z = _pca_truncated(Xs, n_components=n_pcs, random_state=0)\n\n    # 5) Graph\n    C, D = _build_knn(Z, k=k, kd=kd, delta=delta, extra=10, metric='euclidean')\n\n    # Write results\n    adata.obsm['X_emb'] = Z.astype(np.float32)\n    adata.obsp['connectivities'] = C\n    adata.obsp['distances'] = D\n    set_neighbors_meta(adata, k=k, method='GraphFWPCA_ridge+unitvar', metric='euclidean', extra={'delta': delta, 'kd': kd})\n\n    # Diagnostics\n    log_graph_stats(adata, title='unitvar GraphFWPCA ridge')\n    try:\n        summarize_sigma_kd(adata, kd=kd)  # prints global/per-batch summaries\n    except Exception:\n        pass\n    return adata\n\n```\n\n**Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: python storage/system/main.py\nLoading training dataset...\n  Data shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Batches: 4 batches\n\
    Found eliminate_batch_effect_fn, executing...\n\n=== Running batch integration ===\n[LOG] unitvar GraphFWPCA ridge: n_cells=20000, n_genes=2000\n[LOG] embedding: shape=(20000, 100)\n[LOG] neighbors_params={'n_neighbors': 50, 'method': 'GraphFWPCA_ridge+unitvar', 'metric': 'euclidean', 'delta': 0.12, 'kd': 22}\n[LOG] connectivities nnz: avg=83.94, min=50, p1=50.0, p25=57.0, med=68.0, p75=91.0, p99=290.0, max=795\n[LOG] distances: storage=sparse, nnz=321238\nGlobal: {'n': 20000, 'median': 12.741079807281494, 'mean': 13.0251175229311, 'cv': 0.3900787785535098, 'gini': 0.20938921879312256}\nPer-batch:\n                  batch    n    median      mean       cv     gini\n     Koenig et al. 2022 3261 15.481029 14.725053 0.387221 0.202543\n      Kuppe et al. 2022  906 15.321176 14.400959 0.377887 0.211709\nLitvinukova et al. 2020 9685 12.372536 12.912477 0.394611 0.205154\n     Tucker et al. 2020 6148 11.837972 12.098136 0.358185 0.199965\n  Result shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Has embedding: True\n\
    \  Has graph: True\n\nResult saved to: storage/shared/tmp/c51102ee-5ab7-4f8d-a72d-95833c918a72/result_human.h5ad\n\nRESULT_UUID: c51102ee-5ab7-4f8d-a72d-95833c918a72\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto research` (in Token Management Room);\n2. `rank id` (in Research Counter);\n3. `page_size 20` (in Research Counter);\n4. `review 1662` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Research Counter.\n- Evaluations now sorted by id.\n- Page size set to 20.\n- Evaluation 1662 details sent to your System Messages.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Single-cell RNA-seq Batch Integration |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick |\
    \ Score | ARI | ASW_batch | ASW_label | Cell_cycle | Graph_conn | NMI | PCR | cLISI | iLISI | kBET |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1662 | 1 | Ridge GraphFWPCA + gene-wise unit-variance scaling (zero_center=False): δ=0.12, k=50, kd=22 | Praxis V | 1156 | 0.5394 | 0.785 | 0.644 | 0.195 | 0.235 | 0.964 | 0.749 | 0.104 | 0.955 | 0.132 | 0.633 |\n| 1661 | 1 | SC.PP.SCALE (Gene-wise Std, max_value=None) + PBVE-lite on Plain PCA | Syntellect II | 1155 | 0.7484 | 0.779 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.994 | 0.761 | 1.000 | 0.965 | 0.963 | 0.788 |\n| 1660 | 1 | SC.PP.SCALE (Gene-wise Std) + PBVE-lite on Plain PCA (Replaces FWPCA) | Syntellect II | 1154 | 0.7488 | 0.780 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.994 | 0.764 | 1.000 | 0.966 | 0.961 | 0.788 |\n| 1659 | 1 | Replication of Nous I's SOTA (ALC with delta=0.04) | Lumen I | 1153 | 0.7453 | 0.787 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.965 | 0.744 | 1.000 | 0.975 | 0.958 | 0.790 |\n| 1658 | 1 | Verification: Final SOTA Replication\
