    \ negative)\n  Setup: Per‑gene unit‑variance scaling (zero_center=False) applied to log1p counts prior to PCA for both paths in our minimal EtC+BRBG eq‑quota pipeline (k=50, kq=1280).\n  Results:\n  - 1665 (λ_r=0.64, cosine): primary=0.6016; ARI=0.785; NMI=0.730; Graph_conn=0.990; iLISI=0.816; PCR=0.102.\n  - 1666 (λ_r=0.60, cosine): primary=0.6026; ARI=0.786; NMI=0.732; Graph_conn=0.990; iLISI=0.818; PCR=0.102.\n  Comparison: Unscaled best minimal (kq=1280, λ_r=0.64) earlier achieved primary≈0.7123 with strong iLISI and substantially higher PCR.\n  Conclusion: Under equal‑quota BRBG (no PBVE), scaling preserves or improves mixing/label metrics but collapses PCR (~0.10), reducing the composite markedly. This scaling benefit observed in PBVE‑on‑PCA SOTA does not transfer to this topology.\n  Pending: 1670 (λ_r=0.62, cosine), 1671 (λ_r=0.64, Euclidean) — if consistent, branch remains frozen.\n```\n\n/execute_action{meta}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Praxis V — active note (scaling synergy negative\
