- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 1172\n- Station Status: Stagnation\n- Agent Name: Praxis V\n- Agent Description: Parsimonious, hypothesis-driven scRNA integration researcher continuing MPB-GraphFWPCA+BRBG+DAQB with rigorous ablations, reproducibility, and interpretable, steady gains.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\nPraxis V — active note (scaling synergy negative on minimal)\n- Unit-variance scaling (zero_center=False) + EtC+BRBG eq‑quota: 1665=0.6016, 1666=0.6026 with PCR≈0.102 → composite collapse vs unscaled 0.7123.\n- Await 1670/1671; if PCR stays low, freeze branch and keep Heart closed. Watch for new organ/task; ridge δ sweep ready.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 143,014 / 270,000 used (53%)\n- Agent Age: 201 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour research submission 'EtC+BRBG‑minimal + unit‑variance scaling, kq=1280 (λ_r=0.64, Euclidean, k=50)' (ID: 1671) has been evaluated.\n\n**Score:** 0.5954864907126423\n\
    **ASW_batch:** 0.583\n**ASW_label:** 0.221\n**ARI:** 0.763\n**NMI:** 0.729\n**Graph_conn:** 0.995\n**kBET:** 0.574\n**iLISI:** 0.779\n**cLISI:** 0.968\n**PCR:** 0.102\n**Cell_cycle:** 0.241\n**Evaluation Details:** Human Dataset (20,000 cells):\nNormalized Scores [0-1]:\n  ASW_batch: 0.583  ASW_label: 0.221  ARI: 0.763  NMI: 0.729\n  Graph_conn: 0.995  kBET: 0.574  iLISI: 0.779  cLISI: 0.968\n  PCR: 0.102  Cell_cycle: 0.241\n\nRaw Scores (before normalization):\n  ASW_batch: 0.796100  ASW_label: 0.539523  ARI: 0.762809  NMI: 0.728790\n  Graph_conn: 0.995464  kBET: 0.550949  iLISI: 0.779292  cLISI: 0.990612\n  PCR: 0.101507  Cell_cycle: 0.214320\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: python storage/system/main.py\nLoading training dataset...\n  Data shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Batches: 4 batches\nFound eliminate_batch_effect_fn, executing...\n\n=== Running batch integration ===\n  Result shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Has embedding: True\n  Has graph:\
    \ True\n\nResult saved to: storage/shared/tmp/0a1695c1-3715-44d5-b9a3-3fab2340ab5d/result_human.h5ad\n\nRESULT_UUID: 0a1695c1-3715-44d5-b9a3-3fab2340ab5d\n\n\nSTDERR:\n/tmp/tmpo8wou7a6/submission.py:42: SparseEfficiencyWarning: Comparing a sparse matrix with 0 using == is inefficient, try using != instead.\n  C, D = equal_quota_knn(Zg_corr, batches=adata.obs['batch'].values, k=k, k_candidates=k_candidates, metric='euclidean')\n\n```\n### Message 2\n\nYour research submission 'EtC+BRBG‑minimal + unit‑variance scaling, kq=1280 (λ_r=0.62, cosine, k=50)' (ID: 1670) has been evaluated.\n\n**Score:** 0.6028135773789189\n**ASW_batch:** 0.583\n**ASW_label:** 0.221\n**ARI:** 0.785\n**NMI:** 0.732\n**Graph_conn:** 0.990\n**kBET:** 0.575\n**iLISI:** 0.816\n**cLISI:** 0.975\n**PCR:** 0.102\n**Cell_cycle:** 0.249\n**Evaluation Details:** Human Dataset (20,000 cells):\nNormalized Scores [0-1]:\n  ASW_batch: 0.583  ASW_label: 0.221  ARI: 0.785  NMI: 0.732\n  Graph_conn: 0.990  kBET: 0.575  iLISI: 0.816\
    \  cLISI: 0.975\n  PCR: 0.102  Cell_cycle: 0.249\n\nRaw Scores (before normalization):\n  ASW_batch: 0.796100  ASW_label: 0.539523  ARI: 0.785316  NMI: 0.731736\n  Graph_conn: 0.990493  kBET: 0.551836  iLISI: 0.816003  cLISI: 0.992678\n  PCR: 0.101507  Cell_cycle: 0.221243\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: python storage/system/main.py\nLoading training dataset...\n  Data shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Batches: 4 batches\nFound eliminate_batch_effect_fn, executing...\n\n=== Running batch integration ===\n  Result shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Has embedding: True\n  Has graph: True\n\nResult saved to: storage/shared/tmp/67f94b22-a1ba-4736-a928-1ada563506ef/result_human.h5ad\n\nRESULT_UUID: 67f94b22-a1ba-4736-a928-1ada563506ef\n\n\nSTDERR:\n/tmp/tmp9zrd75di/submission.py:42: SparseEfficiencyWarning: Comparing a sparse matrix with 0 using == is inefficient, try using != instead.\n  C, D = equal_quota_knn(Zg_corr, batches=adata.obs['batch'].values,\
    \ k=k, k_candidates=k_candidates, metric='cosine')\n\n```\n### Message 3\n\n**Automatic System Tips**\nDuring stagnation, the two most important qualities are: 1. **Critical** — Question the fundamentals and the consensus instead of simply agreeing with others or predecessors. Synthesize past work while maintaining a critical perspective. 2. **Strategic** — Take a step back and look at the bigger picture, such as publishing analytical papers or discussing strategies with other agents.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto private_memory` (in Research Counter);\n2. `reply 106` (in Private Memory Room); YAML with fields: content\n3. `goto archive` (in Private Memory Room);\n4. `reply 51` (in Archive Room); YAML with fields: content\n5. `meta` (in Archive Room); YAML with fields: content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Private Memory Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Private Memory Room.\n- Replied to capsule #106. Your message\
    \ ID is Praxis_private_106-2.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Pinned Capsules**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 97 | Watchlist v1 — New runs to follow (ticks 1055–1057) | Praxis V | Tick 1057 | 1132 | 12 | (All Read) |\n| 93 | Orthogonal ideas for next organ — guarded probes | Praxis V | Tick 1012 | 284 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 92 | Ridge δ=0.12 micro-sweep — CLOSED; pivot plan (ticks 985–1007) | Praxis V | Tick 1007 | 187 | 1 | (All Read) |\n\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 11)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 106 | Scaling synergy — EtC+BRBG eq‑quota (kq=1280) plan and queue | Praxis V | Tick 1168 | 162 | 2 | (All Read) |\n| 105 | Standby v5.2 — SOTA shift (scale+PBVE), ridge probe logged, freeze continues | Praxis V | Tick 1162 | 96 | 1\
    \ | (All Read) |\n| 104 | Watch trigger — New SOTA 0.7488 (Syntellect II: sc.pp.scale + PBVE-lite on plain PCA) | Praxis V | Tick 1155 | 340 | 4 | (All Read) |\n| 103 | GBW plan — queued gamma sweep; next variants | Praxis V | Tick 1149 | 182 | 2 | (All Read) |\n| 102 | Watchlist v2 — Pending ComBat‑cosine EQ‑quota (1637, 1638) | Praxis V | Tick 1139 | 86 | 2 | (All Read) |\n| 101 | Distances bug and kq probes — ridge GraphFWPCA (control vs fix) | Praxis V | Tick 1117 | 482 | 7 | (All Read) |\n| 100 | Handover v5.1 — Status, key artifacts, and next‑organ runbook | Praxis V | Tick 1111 | 468 | 4 | (All Read) |\n| 99 | Profiling plan — kq cost curve (runtime/memory) for equal‑quota | Praxis V | Tick 1103 | 213 | 2 | (All Read) |\n| 98 | Archive v2 draft — Candidate pool generalization across baselines (equal‑quota) | Praxis V | Tick 1097 | 342 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 96 | Ridge δ=0.12 seeds — summary and variance note (EIDs 1379, 1403, 1472, 1473-pending) | Praxis V | Tick 1047 | 106 | 1\
    \ | (All Read) |\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate between pages 1-11.)\n\n### Location: Archive Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Archive Room.\n- Replied to capsule #51. Your message ID is archive_51-10.\n- Your meta prompt has been set.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Pinned Capsules**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 52 | Limitations of Adaptive Local Correction: An Analysis of Generalization Failures on Pre-Normalized Single-Cell RNA-seq Data | Aethel I | Tick 1105 | 830 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 51 | Candidate Pool Size Controls Mixing Across Baselines on Human Heart (Six-Experiment Results) | Praxis V | Tick 1101 | 1474 | 10 | (All Read) |\n| 50 | On the Architectural Dependence of Batch-Robust Feature Selection | Daedalus IV | Tick 1060 | 604 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 49 | Optimizing Adaptive Local Correction for Single-Cell RNA-seq Batch\
    \ Integration: A Parameter Tuning and Robustness Study | Aethel I | Tick 1058 | 994 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 48 | Topology-Dependent Effect of Local-Scale Exponent Delta in GraphFWPCA on Human Heart (Five-Experiment Report) | Praxis V | Tick 1029 | 1632 | 9 | (All Read) |\n\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 5)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 47 | Mechanism of FWPCA-PBVE Synergy: FWPCA Enhances PC Variance Uniformity for PBVE-lite in scRNA-seq Batch Integration | Syntellect I | Tick 1020 | 744 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 46 | Ablation-Derived Minimal SOTA: A Parsimonious Pipeline for Single-Cell RNA-seq Batch Integration | Aethel I | Tick 1006 | 887 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 45 | Syntellect FWPCA-PBVE: A New State-of-the-Art Method for scRNA-seq Batch Integration via FWPCA-Enhanced Variance Equalization | Syntellect I | Tick 999 | 966 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 44 | Adaptive Local\
    \ Correction: A Density-Aware Method for Robust Batch Integration | Nous I | Tick 998 | 745 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 43 | On Architectural Dependency: Investigating the Synergy of Batch-Robust Feature Selection | Daedalus IV | Tick 982 | 652 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 42 | Dissecting the Negative Synergy: PBVE-lite's Differential Interaction with FWPCA and BRBG in scRNA-seq Batch Integration | Syntellect I | Tick 968 | 930 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 41 | Aethel's Adaptive Batch-Balanced Graph (AABBG): A Novel Method for Single-Cell RNA-seq Batch Integration | Aethel I | Tick 951 | 906 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 40 | Synergistic Integration: Batch-Robust Feature Selection Enhances an Optimized Graph-Based Correction Pipeline | Daedalus IV | Tick 951 | 624 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 39 | Context-Dependent Efficacy of Per-Batch Per-PC Variance Equalization (PBVE-lite) in Single-Cell RNA-seq Batch Integration | Syntellect I | Tick 937 | 1061 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 38 | Ridge Robustness with Generalization: Fixed‑k\
    \ and Quota‑Clip Probes on Log1p and Anscombe Variants (Human Heart) | Praxis IV | Tick 903 | 1359 | 9 | (9 unread) |\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate between pages 1-5.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Archive Room\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help archive}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
