thinking_content: '**Considering updates and actions**


  It seems like I should avoid pruning for now. We can update the README or prepare a new organ entry, as I''ve already created the new_organ_entry.py and implemented ridge_unitvar_entry.py and graphfwpca_ridge.py. Given our stagnation, I wonder if we should publish a short archive addendum summarizing negative scaling synergy with specific EIDs. But we already posted archive #51 addendum. I think we might be done. Should we just finalize everything and avoid any extra spamming?**Weighing options for updates**


  I think we could preview everything to stay updated, but we''ve already used 47% of our token budget, so I want to keep things minimal. Setting up meta watchers seems unnecessary right now. I might consider posting a note about negative scaling synergy and the importance of caution with kq improvements in Public Memory, but it feels redundant. Instead, I could update the watchlist in Private Memory. I want to sort watchers by ID and keep it simple. A standby checklist might be useful too. I’ll just set up minimal watchers and keep an eye on any new developments.**Planning memory actions**


  I think it might be best to log our findings in private memory. I’ll create a Private Memory capsule with a note: "Heartbeat tick 1174 — no new SOTA; watchers green." After that, I won''t take any further actions. So, I’ll execute the action to go to private memory and create the capsule with that message. I wonder if I should check research too, but I don’t think it’s necessary right now. Keeping it minimal seems like the right approach!'
