tick: 1189
role: model
parts:
- text: "Reflection Tick 1/6 — Bottlenecks and evidence (Heart)\n\n1) Topology dependence: BRBG (batch-robust regression + balanced graph) is necessary for mixing without PCR collapse\n- Evidence:\n  - GraphFWPCA-only (no BRBG/quotas): iLISI ≈ 0.096, PCR = 0.0 across kq and symmetrizations; e.g., 1631–1632, 1601–1604, 1608–1609.\n  - Equal-quota over raw PCs without BRBG: still iLISI ≈ 0.09, PCR = 1.000 but no mixing; 1633, 1637–1638 (ComBat-PC EQ-quota) show iLISI ≈ 0.089 despite PCR = 1.000.\n\n2) δ (local-scale exponent) effect is topology-specific\n- Evidence:\n  - Ridge (with BRBG): δ = 0.12 > 0.10 (1379 = 0.7458 vs 1373 = 0.7413); cLISI/Graph_conn stable.\n  - FWPCA-only: δ = 0.12 < 0.10 (1443/1449 ≈ 0.726 vs 1444 ≈ 0.739). σ_kd diagnostics: δ↑ slightly enlarges/uniformizes σ_kd; helpful with BRBG, harmful without (1455, 1459).\n\n3) Candidate pool size (kq) is a robust mixer but not a cure-all\n- Evidence:\n  - Monotone iLISI/composite gains with kq across baselines (equal-quota):\
    \ minimal pipeline 0.6939 → 0.7007 → 0.7065 → 0.7095 → 0.7123 for kq = 512→768→896→1024→1280; vanilla PCA baseline 0.5839 → 0.6073 (iLISI 0.567 → 0.820) at 512→1280 (1578–1579, 1586–1587).\n  - Yet GraphFWPCA-only remains PCR = 0.0 even at large kq (1602, 1613), so topology still bottlenecks.\n\n4) Feature scaling interacts with architecture; benefits don’t transfer wholesale\n- Evidence:\n  - New SOTA: sc.pp.scale (gene-wise std) + PBVE-lite on plain PCA → 0.7488 (1660).\n  - Scaling in GraphFWPCA path:\n    - Both-paths scaling collapses PCR ≈ 0.102 and drops composite (1665/1666/1670/1671 ≈ 0.60).\n    - Graph-only scaling gives modest gain over unscaled minimal (1679 = 0.7160 > 0.7123), but embedding-only yields 0.7082 (1678).\n    - Ridge + scale (1662) severely underperforms (0.5394) despite strong ARI/NMI—PCR/iLISI fail.\n\n5) Symmetrization/selection variants are fragile\n- Evidence:\n  - Reciprocal tie-break/QPS degrade vs ridge union symmetrization: 1424 ≈ 0.7420 (δ mismatch)/1431\
    \ = 0.7375 (δ fixed), QPS ≈ 0.7169 (1425/1432).\n\n6) Metric coupling and seed variance\n- Evidence:\n  - On ridge δ = 0.12, seed spread (~0.004–0.005) is driven almost entirely by Cell_cycle; other normalized metrics match to 3 decimals (1379, 1472–1481, 1403).\n  - Fast decision-making must watch Cell_cycle to avoid misreading noise as effect.\n\n7) Evaluator binding/metadata matters but is secondary\n- Evidence:\n  - Adding neighbors metadata and raw distances slightly stabilizes ARI/NMI/connectivity (1612–1613) but does not restore iLISI/PCR when topology is wrong.\n\n8) Generalization risk on Heart-only heuristics\n- Evidence:\n  - Papers rejected until cross-baseline generalization was shown (Archive #51 accepted only after vanilla PCA and DAQB-like tests confirmed kq trend).\n  - Several ideas that “worked” on ridge failed elsewhere (e.g., δ on FWPCA-only, scaling on ridge).\n\nImplication: The true bottlenecks are architectural/topological (presence of BRBG and balanced cross-batch\
    \ selection) and distributional (σ_kd + feature scale) rather than mere neighbor count or micro-tuning. Any new-organ plan must treat BRBG/quotas as first-class, test δ only in that context, use kq as a safe mixer, and verify PCR/iLISI jointly with σ_kd diagnostics to avoid local optima."
