tick: 1189
role: model
parts:
- text: "Reflection Tick 2/6 — Minimal falsifiable hypotheses for a new organ (with fast decision rules)\n\nH1 — Ridge δ generalizes (BRBG present)\n- Hypothesis: On ridge (kd=22, k=50), δ=0.12 outperforms δ=0.10 without harming structure.\n- Minimal experiment: 2 runs per δ (seeds 0,1); total 4 EIDs.\n- Success criteria:\n  - Mean primary score(δ=0.12) − mean(δ=0.10) ≥ +0.002\n  - cLISI, Graph_conn deltas within ±0.003 of δ=0.10 (no degradation)\n- Fail/interpretation:\n  - If gain < 0.002 or cLISI/Graph_conn drop > 0.003, default δ=0.10 for this organ.\n- Verification signals: Full 10 metrics + σ_kd (median, CV, Gini); if σ_kd CV tightens ≥1% vs δ=0.10 and score increases, keep δ=0.12.\n\nH2 — Candidate pool (kq) improves mixing across baselines\n- Hypothesis: For equal‑quota graphs, larger kq improves iLISI and composite at small cost, independent of embedding (plain PCA or EtC+BRBG‑minimal).\n- Minimal experiment: kq ∈ {512, 1024, 1280} at fixed k=50, cosine; 1 seed (0) is sufficient\
    \ to detect monotonicity; confirm with seed 1 if borderline.\n- Success criteria:\n  - iLISI(1280) − iLISI(512) ≥ +0.02 and primary(1280) − primary(512) ≥ +0.005\n  - PCR(1280) − PCR(512) ≥ −0.01 (no meaningful PCR loss)\n- Fail/interpretation:\n  - If monotonicity fails or PCR cost >0.01, freeze at best kq observed and do not escalate further.\n- Verification signals: Record runtime/memory; expect ~+0.40 s and +50 MB per +256 candidates (profiling slope).\n\nH3 — Graph‑only scaling synergy without PCR loss\n- Hypothesis: Unit‑variance scaling per gene before computing graph PCs (graph path only) improves composite vs unscaled minimal (λ_r=0.64), preserving PCR≈1.000.\n- Minimal experiment: Unscaled vs graph‑only scaling at kq=1280, k=50, λ_r=0.64, cosine; seeds {0,1} if possible (else seed 0 then confirm).\n- Success criteria:\n  - primary(scaled) − primary(unscaled) ≥ +0.003\n  - PCR change ∈ [−0.005, +∞); iLISI change ≥ 0.0; Graph_conn ≥ 0.98\n- Fail/interpretation:\n  - If PCR drops\
    \ >0.005 or primary gain <0.003, freeze scaling branch for this organ (Heart showed both‑paths scaling collapsed PCR; don’t repeat).\n- Verification signals: Break out label vs mixing deltas; ensure the gain is not solely Cell_cycle noise.\n\nH4 — σ_kd‑guided δ selection rule (mechanistic prior)\n- Hypothesis: Tighter σ_kd (lower CV/Gini) favors δ↑ (0.12); wider σ_kd favors δ=0.10.\n- Minimal experiment: Compute σ_kd distributions for δ ∈ {0.10, 0.12} on ridge triage runs.\n- Decision rule:\n  - If CV(δ=0.12) ≤ CV(δ=0.10) − 1% and median(δ=0.12) ≤ median(δ=0.10) + 3%, choose δ=0.12 (provided primary improves ≥0.002).\n  - Else choose δ=0.10.\n- Verification signals: Consistency across seeds; if σ_kd deltas contradict metrics, favor metrics.\n\nH5 — Seed‑band safeguard and effect size gate\n- Hypothesis: True improvements exceed typical seed spread (Heart ≈ 0.004–0.005, driven by Cell_cycle).\n- Minimal experiment: For any “win,” run seed 1 to confirm.\n- Success criteria: Mean gain across\
    \ seeds ≥0.003 and both seeds non‑negative; ignore single‑seed wins <0.004.\n\nH6 — Symmetrization stability (keep ridge union; avoid fragile variants)\n- Hypothesis: Ridge union + soft mutual boost (μ≈1.10) remains stable; alternatives (QPS/reciprocal tie‑break) degrade.\n- Minimal experiment: None unless ridge union underperforms; treat alternatives as last‑resort probes.\n- Decision: If any alt < ridge by ≥0.005, abandon.\n\nFast go/no‑go timing\n- Run H1 and H2 first (≤4–6 EIDs total). If both pass, attempt H3 (≤2 EIDs). Publish brief results if any pass with clear deltas.\n- Stop early if any branch harms PCR (>0.01 drop) or cLISI (>0.01 drop) while giving <0.003 primary gain.\n- Always log σ_kd and note Cell_cycle variance to avoid over‑interpreting noise."
