parts:
- text: "Reflection Tick 3/6 — Triage plan for a new organ (first 2–4 submissions, fast decisions)\n\nT0 — Setup and guardrails\n- Shared config: kd=22, k=50, n_pcs=100, seeds={0,1}, cosine for EQ‑quota, Euclidean for ridge graph.\n- Log diagnostics per run: full 10 metrics; σ_kd (median, CV, Gini) global and per batch; runtime/memory; neighbors meta bound.\n- Quick gates (abort/freeze if violated):\n  - PCR drop > 0.01 vs control; cLISI drop > 0.01 without ≥0.003 primary gain.\n  - Improvements < 0.003 are treated as noise until confirmed across seeds.\n\nT1 — Ridge δ sweep (architectural anchor)\n- Runs: δ ∈ {0.10, 0.12} × seeds {0,1} (4 EIDs).\n- Decide δ: If mean(primary)δ=0.12 − mean(primary)δ=0.10 ≥ +0.002 and cLISI/Graph_conn within ±0.003, adopt δ=0.12; else keep δ=0.10.\n- Mechanism check: If σ_kd CV decreases ≥1% with δ=0.12 and score improves, preference δ=0.12 even if marginal.\n\nT2 — Equal‑quota baseline (mixing probe, independent of BRBG)\n- Runs: kq ∈ {512, 1024, 1280} at\
    \ k=50, seed 0 (add seed 1 if borderline).\n- Expectation: iLISI and primary monotone with kq, PCR stable (Δ≥−0.01).\n- Decision: If monotone holds, standardize at kq=1024 or 1280 (tradeoff by runtime/mem); else freeze at best observed kq.\n\nT3 — Graph‑only scaling synergy (optional, only if T2 positive)\n- Runs: minimal EQ‑quota with λ_r=0.64, unscaled vs graph‑only unit‑variance scaling (kq=1280), seed 0 (confirm with seed 1 if win).\n- Success: primary gain ≥ +0.003, PCR ≈ 1.000 (Δ ≥ −0.005), iLISI non‑decreasing, Graph_conn ≥ 0.98.\n- Failure: any PCR harm > 0.005 or gain < 0.003 → freeze scaling branch for this organ.\n\nT4 — Early stop and branch freeze\n- If any triage branch violates guards (PCR/cLISI harm) without clear gain, stop that branch immediately; keep ridge default and best kq setting as baselines.\n\nVerification signals (decide quickly)\n- Seed‑band check: For any “win,” run seed 1; require mean gain ≥ 0.003 and both seeds non‑negative.\n- σ_kd rule: Tighter σ_kd\
    \ (lower CV/Gini) aligning with better δ is supportive; contradicting signals default to metrics.\n- Cost sanity: Use kq cost slope (~+0.40 s and +50 MB per +256) to choose 1024 vs 1280 pragmatically.\n\nOutputs after triage (publishable if clean)\n- Short note A (2–4 EIDs): “Ridge δ generalizes on Organ X” with σ_kd deltas.\n- Short note B (2–3 EIDs): “Candidate pool size improves mixing on Organ X” with iLISI/PCR and cost table.\n- Optional note C (2 EIDs): “Graph‑only scaling modestly improves minimal pipeline without PCR loss” (only if passed)."
