tick: 1189
role: model
parts:
- text: "Reflection Tick 4/6 — Mechanism layer: diagnostics, levers, and fast verification\n\nA) Mechanistic diagnostics to run by default (low cost, high signal)\n- σ_kd landscape (kd=22 on PCs):\n  - Report median, CV, Gini globally and per-batch.\n  - Expected patterns:\n    • δ↑ (0.12) on ridge should slightly increase median σ_kd and reduce CV/Gini (more uniform neighborhoods).\n    • When CV tightens but iLISI falls, topology is likely wrong (e.g., missing BRBG/quotas).\n- Inbound-entropy (IE) or neighbor diversity proxy:\n  - Higher IE across batches indicates healthier cross-batch mixing; collapsing IE with stable ARI usually foretells PCR/iLISI failure.\n- Directed-gap or cross-batch degree ratio:\n  - Check the fraction of cross-batch edges per cell; guard against extremes:\n    • Too low → under-mixing (low iLISI, PCR=1).\n    • Too high → over-mixing (cLISI↓, ARI/NMI↓).\n- PCR decomposition quick check:\n  - Monitor normalized PCR and the raw regression R^2 trend per PC; steep\
    \ reductions in PCR with no compensating iLISI gains are red flags.\n- Runtime/memory profile for kq:\n  - Confirm slope (~+0.40 s and +50 MB per +256 candidates) holds; use as a practical ceiling when gains saturate.\n\nB) Minimal levers (orthogonal; change one at a time)\n- δ (0.10 vs 0.12) on ridge only:\n  - Mechanism: adjusts how strongly local scale equalizes distances; benefits when σ_kd is heterogeneous but corrected by BRBG.\n  - Stop rule: if cLISI/Graph_conn drop > 0.003 without ≥0.003 primary gain, revert.\n- kq (512→1024→1280) for equal-quota graphs:\n  - Mechanism: larger candidate pool raises available cross-batch matches → iLISI↑ with modest cost.\n  - Stop rule: if PCR loss > 0.01 or iLISI non‑monotone, freeze at best observed kq.\n- Graph‑only unit‑variance scaling (before graph PCs, keep embedding unscaled):\n  - Mechanism: homogenize per-gene scale feeding residualization/graph distances without wiping PC variance important to PCR.\n  - Stop rule: if PCR falls > 0.005\
    \ or primary gain < 0.003, freeze.\n- Mutual boost μ (soft reciprocity, e.g., 1.10 vs 1.0) on ridge:\n  - Mechanism: reward bidirectional stability; can improve Graph_conn with minimal impact on mixing.\n  - Stop rule: if any metric subset regresses > 0.003, revert.\n- α_mix (concept lever, if needed later): convex blend of within‑batch structural edges and quota‑based cross‑batch edges:\n  - Mechanism: enforce minimal within‑batch degree (preserve PCR) while allowing controlled cross‑batch mixing (raise iLISI).\n  - Stop rule: if ARI/NMI or cLISI drop > 0.01 at any α, abandon.\n\nC) Fast falsification patterns (avoid local optima)\n- “PCR = 1.000, iLISI ≈ 0” patterns:\n  - Likely missing quotas/BRBG, or EQ‑quota on a representation that lacks cross‑batch comparability. Do not chase kq alone; switch topology.\n- “Great ARI/NMI but PCR/iLISI both low” patterns:\n  - Often due to scaling applied in both paths (observed PCR collapse). Restrict scaling to graph path or remove it.\n- “Cell_cycle\
    \ swings only”:\n  - Treat sub‑0.003 primary changes as noise until confirmed across seeds; avoid over‑interpreting single‑seed wins.\n\nD) Verification signals and thresholds (decide quickly)\n- Primary gain thresholds:\n  - ≥ +0.003 (per change) after seed confirmation; ≥ +0.005 preferred to publish.\n- Structure guards:\n  - cLISI and Graph_conn deltas within ±0.003 of control when claiming a δ/kq/scaling win on ridge.\n  - PCR guard: ΔPCR ≥ −0.005 (graph‑only scaling) or ≥ −0.01 (kq changes).\n- Seed band:\n  - For any claimed win, mean across seeds {0,1} ≥ +0.003 and both seeds non‑negative. If effect ≈ 0.003–0.004 and entirely due to Cell_cycle, rerun or discard.\n\nE) Mechanism attribution routine (when something improves)\n- Hold everything else constant; revert one change at a time:\n  1) Revert scaling (graph‑only → none) at fixed kq; check if gain vanishes.\n  2) Revert kq (1280→512) with scaling fixed; confirm monotonic iLISI drop.\n  3) Flip δ (0.12→0.10) on ridge; confirm\
    \ σ_kd CV/median shifts match the direction of metric changes.\n- Publish only when a single lever’s causal effect is evidenced by these reversions.\n\nF) Bigger‑picture sanity (stagnation escape valves)\n- If ridge saturates and minimal EQ‑quota incremental gains stall:\n  - Switch to cross‑organ validation immediately (when available) to prevent overfitting to Heart idiosyncrasies.\n  - Consider α_mix (within‑batch + cross‑batch convex blend) as a controlled mechanism specifically to co‑optimize PCR and iLISI, but only after triage completes and with tight guards.\n\nNet: Treat σ_kd, iLISI, PCR, and cost as co‑equal signals; apply one orthogonal lever at a time with tight stop rules; insist on seed‑confirmed gains beyond noise. This mechanism layer reduces false positives and keeps us out of topological dead ends observed on Heart."
