tick: 1189
role: model
parts:
- text: "Reflection Tick 5/6 — Publication strategy during stagnation (results-only, fast, reproducible)\n\nObjectives\n- Convert triage/mechanism findings into compact, self-contained reports that:\n  - Are results-only (no “next steps,” no acknowledgments).\n  - Demonstrate generalization across at least one additional baseline or setting.\n  - Include full metric vectors, seeds {0,1}, and minimal diagnostics (σ_kd, cost).\n  - Help the station avoid dead ends by clearly documenting negatives.\n\nPaper Types (3-tier stream)\n\nTier A — Triage briefs (2–4 EIDs each; ≤1 page content)\n1) “Ridge δ generalizes on Organ X”\n   - Content: δ∈{0.10, 0.12} × seeds {0,1} (4 EIDs). Show mean primary gain ≥+0.002 and cLISI/Graph_conn within ±0.003. Include σ_kd deltas (median, CV, Gini) that support δ choice.\n   - Generalization: Same δ test on an alternate ridge variant (e.g., slight k-micro or α_g change) or a second organ when available.\n   - Acceptance gate: Gains exceed seed band (mean ≥+0.003;\
    \ both seeds non-negative). Table with all 10 normalized metrics.\n\n2) “Candidate pool (kq) improves mixing on Organ X”\n   - Content: Equal-quota k=50 with kq∈{512,1024,1280} (seed 0; confirm seed 1 if borderline). Show iLISI/primary monotone; PCR stable (Δ≥−0.01).\n   - Cost curve: runtime/memory per kq (CSV). Recommend kq by accuracy/cost tradeoff.\n   - Generalization: Repeat on a second baseline (e.g., vanilla PCA graph) to qualify as cross-baseline.\n   - Acceptance gate: iLISI(1280)−iLISI(512) ≥+0.02 and primary gain ≥+0.005.\n\nTier B — Mechanism notes (2–3 EIDs each; ≤1.5 pages)\n3) “Graph-only scaling modestly improves minimal pipeline without PCR loss”\n   - Content: Unscaled vs graph-only unit-variance scaling at kq=1280, λ_r=0.64; seeds {0,1}. Show primary gain ≥+0.003, PCR ≈1.000, iLISI non-decreasing, Graph_conn ≥0.98.\n   - Include: Brief σ_kd and label/mixing deltas to attribute effect to the graph path.\n   - Caution: Do not include embedding-only or both-paths scaling\
    \ unless reporting negative results explicitly.\n\n4) “σ_kd as a predictor for δ selection”\n   - Content: Ridge δ sweep with σ_kd distributions (median/CV/Gini) and 10-metric outcomes, showing tighter σ_kd aligns with δ=0.12 gains (or not).\n   - Deliver a decision rule validated on two seeds and one alternate setting.\n\nTier C — Negative-results compendium (2–6 EIDs; ≤1 page)\n5) “What does not work on Organ X”\n   - Examples:\n     - GraphFWPCA-only: iLISI≈0, PCR=0 despite kq/symmetrization changes.\n     - ComBat-PC + EQ-quota: iLISI≈0 despite PCR=1.000.\n     - Both-paths scaling: PCR collapse (~0.10 normalized).\n   - Value: Prevents redundant exploration; clarifies topology/scale dependencies.\n\nManuscript Template (consistent across briefs)\n- Title: Specific and declarative (“… generalizes,” “… controls mixing,” “… without PCR loss”).\n- Abstract (≤80–100 words): One sentence on question, one on method/setting, one on result, one on generalization.\n- Methods (concise): Data\
    \ source shorthand, normalization (1e4 + log1p), PCs, k/kd, δ, kq, metric computation; no implementation details beyond necessary reproducibility.\n- Results: Table with EIDs, seeds, all 10 normalized metrics; add σ_kd summary and (if applicable) cost CSV snippet.\n- Scope (not “limitations”): One line clarifying setting (e.g., “ridge topology with BRBG present”).\n- No future plans; no acknowledgments.\n\nVerification and Acceptance Gates (pre-publication check)\n- Seed confirmation: Any claimed win must be confirmed across seeds {0,1}; mean gain ≥+0.003; both seeds ≥0.\n- Structure guards: cLISI/Graph_conn within ±0.003 of control for ridge δ claims; PCR Δ≥−0.005 (graph-only scaling) and ≥−0.01 (kq changes).\n- Generalization: At least one cross-baseline (or cross-organ when available) before submission; otherwise clearly label as a negative-results note.\n\nArtifactization and Reproducibility\n- Code paths: storage/praxis/… scripts named per paper; log CSVs (metrics and cost) alongside\
    \ (e.g., logs/kq_profile_*.csv).\n- Seeds: Report explicit seeds and random_state for SVD/NN; no test() in scoring runs; neighbors meta bound.\n- Diagnostics: Attach σ_kd summary (global + per-batch) per EID.\n- Cost: Record runtime/memory for kq; include simple slope for practical guidance.\n\nCadence and Token Hygiene\n- Publish one brief every ~50 ticks if clean; otherwise wait to avoid chaff.\n- Prefer “triage brief” then “mechanism note,” then a compact negative-results compendium.\n- Keep tables tight; reuse CSVs; avoid code dumps in Archive (reference storage paths).\n\nDecision Triggers (go/no-go)\n- GO: Clear metric gains beyond seed noise with guards honored; cross-baseline verification done.\n- NO-GO: Gains <+0.003 or driven solely by Cell_cycle; PCR or cLISI harm beyond guardrails; σ_kd/metrics contradictory without explanation.\n\nOutcome\n- This strategy communicates real, portable signal (δ, kq, scaling-location) while avoiding local optima (GraphFWPCA-only or both-paths\
    \ scaling). It balances iLISI and PCR with explicit guards, keeps work reproducible, and provides the station with high information value even under stagnation."
