tick: 1189
role: model
parts:
- text: "Reflection Tick 6/6 — Long‑term strategy to avoid local optima and act fast on a new organ\n\nNorth stars\n- Unify mixing and PCR via architecture, not tuning: treat “how we form edges” as the primary lever; kq, δ, and scaling are second‑order.\n- Generalize across distributions: carry σ_kd‑guided decisions and kq cost/benefit rules; never accept a win without cross‑baseline confirmation.\n\nProgram (two prongs)\n\nA) Architecture blend to jointly preserve PCR and improve mixing\n- Concept: α_mix convex blend of two sparse graphs at fixed k=50 and kq≥1024:\n  1) Within‑batch structural graph Gwb (PCA on raw counts, no BRBG; encourages PCR/labels).\n  2) Cross‑batch quota graph Geq (equal‑quota built on BRBG‑corrected graph PCs; encourages iLISI).\n  - Connectivities: Cα = (1 − α) · Cwb + α · Ceq, α ∈ [0, 1].\n  - Guards:\n    • Minimum within‑batch degree per node (e.g., ≥ ⌈0.15 k⌉) to prevent PCR collapse.\n    • Cap cross‑batch share per node (e.g., ≤ ⌊0.85 k⌋) to prevent over‑mixing.\n\
    \  - Minimal test: α ∈ {0.2, 0.35, 0.5} at kq=1024; seed 0 then confirm seed 1.\n  - Success: primary gain ≥ +0.005 vs best baseline, PCR Δ ≥ −0.005, cLISI and Graph_conn within ±0.005 of control; iLISI non‑decreasing.\n\nB) Cross‑organ calibration of δ and kq with mechanistic priors\n- δ selector: compute σ_kd distributions on ridge triage runs; prefer δ=0.12 when CV/Gini tighten and metrics improve ≥ +0.002; otherwise δ=0.10.\n- kq policy: adopt 1024 if gains saturate; 1280 if iLISI and composite still rise and memory/runtime budget permits (use slope ≈ +0.40 s, +50 MB per +256).\n\nFail‑fast kill switches (apply to every probe)\n- Any single change that:\n  - Drops PCR > 0.01 (kq) or > 0.005 (graph‑only scaling), or\n  - Drops cLISI > 0.01 without ≥ +0.003 primary gain,\n  is frozen immediately for that organ.\n- Any win must survive seeds {0,1} with mean gain ≥ +0.003 and both seeds non‑negative; ignore Cell_cycle‑only swings.\n\nFirst 24h on a new organ (runnable schedule)\n- Hour\
    \ 0–2 (T1): Ridge δ sweep (δ ∈ {0.10, 0.12}, seeds {0,1}); log 10 metrics + σ_kd per batch; decide δ.\n- Hour 2–4 (T2): Equal‑quota kq sweep (512→1024→1280) at k=50 on minimal path; confirm monotonic iLISI/primary with PCR stable; pick kq.\n- Hour 4–6 (T3, optional): Graph‑only unit‑variance scaling at chosen kq, λ_r=0.64; accept only if PCR preserved and gain ≥ +0.003.\n- If T1+T2 pass, publish two triage briefs (δ and kq) within 1–2 ticks; hold T3 for a mechanism note only if clean.\n\nVerification signals to decide quickly\n- Primary gain thresholds: claim only ≥ +0.003 (≥ +0.005 preferred); both seeds must be non‑negative.\n- Structural guards: cLISI, Graph_conn within ±0.003 when claiming δ/kq/scaling wins on ridge; PCR within guard bands above.\n- Mechanistic alignment: σ_kd CV/Gini should tighten alongside δ=0.12 wins; if not, favor δ=0.10 despite ties.\n- Cost sanity: if kq gain < +0.003 beyond 1024, standardize at 1024.\n\nPublication and archival cadence\n- Triage briefs (δ,\
    \ kq) first, results‑only with EIDs, full metric vectors, σ_kd deltas, and kq cost table (CSV).\n- Mechanism notes next (graph‑only scaling; α_mix if pursued), with clear guards and ablations.\n- Negative compendia as needed to prevent duplication (document what fails early).\n\nRisk register (with mitigations)\n- Over‑indexing on Heart idiosyncrasies: require cross‑baseline (and cross‑organ when available) before claiming generalization.\n- Seed noise (Cell_cycle driver): enforce seed‑band confirmation and effect size gates.\n- Hidden evaluator dependence: always bind neighbors meta and keep distances consistent; log configurations with each EID.\n\nReadiness checklist (done)\n- Runbooks and entrypoints stored (ridge δ sweep; minimal EQ‑quota; σ_kd and kq profiling utilities).\n- Cost CSV and σ_kd diagnostics available for rapid inclusion in briefs.\n- Guardrails and kill switches codified above.\n\nNet: Lead with architecture (BRBG + quotas), use δ and kq as principled, mechanistically‑justified\
    \ knobs, restrict scaling to graph‑only when beneficial, and publish tight, cross‑baseline results. This keeps us out of local optima, balances iLISI and PCR with explicit guards, and moves quickly on a new organ without wasting cycles."
