tick: 1199
role: model
parts:
- text: "/execute_action{goto mail}\n/execute_action{reply 23}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Re: Cross‑Organ Study — Status and runbook for PBVE‑lite sanity checks\"\ncontent: |\n  Hi Syntellect II,\n\n  Status\n  - New organ: not yet released by the Station; the only active dataset is Human Heart (~20k × 2k HVGs). Cross‑organ study remains in standby until the new organ appears.\n  - Coordination: I’m aligned to support the PBVE‑lite sanity checks as committed by Syntellect I (simple PCA+kNN scaffold and comparison to the adopted ridge baseline). I’ll also sync with Daedalus IV once the organ drops.\n\n  Adopted ridge baseline (Heart, reference)\n  - Topology: MPB‑GraphFWPCA + BRBG + DAQB (“ridge”).\n  - Hyperparams: k=50, kd=22, λ=0.605, δ∈{0.10, 0.12}; adopted δ=0.12 on Heart.\n  - Results: 0.7458 (EID 1379, seed 0); δ=0.10 control 0.7413 (EID 1373). cLISI ≈ 0.972–0.973; Graph_conn ≈ 0.968; seed spread ≈ 0.004 driven mainly by Cell_cycle.\n  - Notes: δ benefits are topology‑dependent (helps with\
    \ BRBG, harms FWPCA‑only).\n\n  Data access and protocols (Heart; new organ will mirror this)\n  - System data (read‑only): storage/system/\n    • human_train.h5ad (raw counts in X/layers['counts'], HVGs in var['batch_hvg'])\n    • openproblems_metrics.py, openproblems_baselines.json (metric normalization)\n  - Submission contract:\n    • Use raw counts → normalize_total(1e4) + log1p (do not rely on pre‑normalized layers for evaluation).\n    • Do not use cell_type in any way. Batch labels are allowed.\n    • Return BOTH obsp['connectivities'] and obsp['distances'] (CSR); and optionally obsm['X_emb'].\n    • Resources: CPU only, ~30 min limit.\n  - New organ: expect analogous paths under storage/system (e.g., <organ>_train.h5ad). I will ping as soon as it appears.\n\n  PBVE‑lite sanity checks to run on the new organ (proposal)\n  1) Plain PCA scaffold + PBVE‑lite:\n     - Normalize 1e4 + log1p; HVG mask if provided (var['batch_hvg']).\n     - PCA(n=60) → PBVE‑lite on PCs → neighbors\
    \ k=50.\n     - Seeds {0,1}; report full 10 metrics.\n     - Optional: compare “no scaling” vs gene‑wise variance standardization (sc.pp.scale with zero_center=False) since your #53 shows strong synergy.\n  2) Compare against ridge baseline:\n     - Ridge δ sweep δ∈{0.10,0.12}, kd=22, k=50, seeds {0,1}; adopt δ by mean score and structural guards (cLISI/Graph_conn within ±0.003).\n     - Publish both sets as a cross‑baseline sanity note if results are clean.\n\n  Artifacts you can reuse (read‑only pointers; no code exchange needed)\n  - Runbook: storage/praxis/runbook_next_organ.txt (ridge δ triage; guards and metrics).\n  - Entry points: storage/praxis/new_organ_entry.py (ridge δ=0.12 seed0), new_organ_entry_d10_seed1.py (δ=0.10 seed1),\n    and new_organ_eq_quota_entry.py (equal‑quota minimal baseline).\n  - Diagnostics: storage/praxis/diag_sigma_kd.py (σ_kd med/CV/Gini per batch); profile_kq_runtime.py (kq cost curve).\n  - These document the protocol and diagnostics only; feel free\
    \ to implement independently.\n\n  Reporting/coordination\n  - When the new organ arrives, I’ll send a one‑pager with dataset ID, ridge δ decision after seeds {0,1}, and any deviations (e.g., absence of batch_hvg).\n  - For your PBVE‑lite checks, please log seeds, whether scaling was applied (and how), and share EIDs and metric vectors so we can cross‑reference in Archive with a results‑only brief.\n\n  Until the organ drops, I remain on standby. Thanks for pushing the scaled‑PCA PBVE SOTA (#53); it’s valuable for the generalization track.\n\n  — Praxis V\n```"
thinking_content: '**Preparing message summary**


  I''m getting ready to summarize the message titled "Re: Cross-Organ Study — Status and runbook for PBVE-lite checks." I’m considering whether to include "action: goto token_management prune," but it seems unnecessary. My main focus should be on the email content, so I’ll generate a clear and concise summary of the key points to ensure the message is effective. Let’s do that!'
