role: model
parts:
- text: "/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"PBVE‑lite + Scaled PCA60 — Embedding only (no graph)\"\ntags: \"pbve, pca, scaling, embedding-only\"\nabstract: \"Replicate scaled‑PCA + PBVE‑lite but return only the integrated embedding to avoid pathological kNN graphs observed with weighted edges. From raw counts: log1p normalize, gene-wise std scale (zero_center=False), PCA60, PBVE‑lite. Output X_emb only; let evaluator handle neighbors.\"\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n  from sklearn.decomposition import TruncatedSVD\n  import anndata as ad\n  import scipy.sparse as sp\n  import scanpy as sc\n\n  EPS = 1e-12\n\n  def _to_csr(X):\n      if sp.isspmatrix_csr(X): return X\n      if sp.issparse(X): return X.tocsr()\n      return sp.csr_matrix(X)\n\n  def _row_scale_csr(X, scale):\n      if not sp.issparse(X):\n          return (X.T * scale).T\n      X = _to_csr(X).copy()\n      X.data *= np.repeat(scale, np.diff(X.indptr))\n      return X\n\n  def _normalize_log1p_from_counts(adata:\
    \ ad.AnnData):\n      Xc = adata.layers['counts'] if 'counts' in adata.layers else adata.X\n      Xc = _to_csr(Xc).astype(np.float32)\n      lib = np.asarray(Xc.sum(axis=1)).ravel()\n      lib = np.maximum(lib, 1e-9)\n      scale = (1e4 / lib).astype(np.float32)\n      Xn = _row_scale_csr(Xc, scale)\n      Xn = Xn.copy()\n      Xn.data = np.log1p(Xn.data)\n      return Xn\n\n  def _select_hvgs(X, adata):\n      if 'batch_hvg' in adata.var.columns:\n          m = adata.var['batch_hvg'].values.astype(bool)\n          if m.any() and m.sum() < X.shape[1]:\n              return X[:, m]\n      return X\n\n  def _pbve_lite_equalize(Z: np.ndarray, batches: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:\n      Zc = Z.copy().astype(np.float32)\n      b = np.asarray(batches).astype(str)\n      uniq = np.unique(b)\n      p = Z.shape[1]\n      stds = np.zeros((len(uniq), p), dtype=np.float32)\n      for i, ub in enumerate(uniq):\n          idx = (b == ub)\n          stds[i] = Z[idx].std(axis=0).astype(np.float32) if\
    \ np.any(idx) else 1.0\n      target = np.maximum(stds.mean(axis=0), EPS).astype(np.float32)\n      for i, ub in enumerate(uniq):\n          idx = (b == ub)\n          sb = np.maximum(stds[i], EPS)\n          if np.any(idx):\n              Zc[idx] *= (target / sb)[None, :]\n      return Zc\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      # Normalize and select HVGs\n      Xn = _normalize_log1p_from_counts(adata)\n      Xn = _select_hvgs(Xn, adata)\n\n      # Gene-wise std scaling (zero_center=False) on a temp AnnData\n      tmp = ad.AnnData(X=Xn.copy(), obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n      sc.pp.scale(tmp, zero_center=False)\n\n      # PCA to 60 comps\n      Z = TruncatedSVD(n_components=60, random_state=0).fit_transform(tmp.X)\n\n      # PBVE-lite on PCs\n      Zc = _pbve_lite_equalize(Z, adata.obs['batch'].values)\n\n      # Output embedding only\n      adata.obsm['X_emb'] = Zc.astype(np.float32)\n      return adata\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n\
    ```yaml\ntitle: \"PBVE‑lite + Scaled PCA60 — sc.pp.neighbors graph on X_emb (k=50, euclidean)\"\ntags: \"pbve, pca, scaling, scanpy-neighbors, embedding\"\nabstract: \"Same scaled‑PCA + PBVE‑lite embedding, but use scanpy’s neighbors on X_emb (k=50, euclidean) to construct connectivities/distances, avoiding custom weighted graphs that collapsed mixing. Returns X_emb and sc.pp.neighbors‑derived graph.\"\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n  from sklearn.decomposition import TruncatedSVD\n  import anndata as ad\n  import scipy.sparse as sp\n  import scanpy as sc\n\n  EPS = 1e-12\n\n  def _to_csr(X):\n      if sp.isspmatrix_csr(X): return X\n      if sp.issparse(X): return X.tocsr()\n      return sp.csr_matrix(X)\n\n  def _row_scale_csr(X, scale):\n      if not sp.issparse(X):\n          return (X.T * scale).T\n      X = _to_csr(X).copy()\n      X.data *= np.repeat(scale, np.diff(X.indptr))\n      return X\n\n  def _normalize_log1p_from_counts(adata: ad.AnnData):\n      Xc = adata.layers['counts']\
    \ if 'counts' in adata.layers else adata.X\n      Xc = _to_csr(Xc).astype(np.float32)\n      lib = np.asarray(Xc.sum(axis=1)).ravel()\n      lib = np.maximum(lib, 1e-9)\n      scale = (1e4 / lib).astype(np.float32)\n      Xn = _row_scale_csr(Xc, scale)\n      Xn = Xn.copy()\n      Xn.data = np.log1p(Xn.data)\n      return Xn\n\n  def _select_hvgs(X, adata):\n      if 'batch_hvg' in adata.var.columns:\n          m = adata.var['batch_hvg'].values.astype(bool)\n          if m.any() and m.sum() < X.shape[1]:\n              return X[:, m]\n      return X\n\n  def _pbve_lite_equalize(Z: np.ndarray, batches: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:\n      Zc = Z.copy().astype(np.float32)\n      b = np.asarray(batches).astype(str)\n      uniq = np.unique(b)\n      p = Z.shape[1]\n      stds = np.zeros((len(uniq), p), dtype=np.float32)\n      for i, ub in enumerate(uniq):\n          idx = (b == ub)\n          stds[i] = Z[idx].std(axis=0).astype(np.float32) if np.any(idx) else 1.0\n      target = np.maximum(stds.mean(axis=0),\
    \ EPS).astype(np.float32)\n      for i, ub in enumerate(uniq):\n          idx = (b == ub)\n          sb = np.maximum(stds[i], EPS)\n          if np.any(idx):\n              Zc[idx] *= (target / sb)[None, :]\n      return Zc\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      # Normalize and select HVGs\n      Xn = _normalize_log1p_from_counts(adata)\n      Xn = _select_hvgs(Xn, adata)\n\n      # Gene-wise std scaling\n      tmp = ad.AnnData(X=Xn.copy(), obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n      sc.pp.scale(tmp, zero_center=False)\n\n      # PCA60\n      Z = TruncatedSVD(n_components=60, random_state=0).fit_transform(tmp.X)\n\n      # PBVE-lite\n      Zc = _pbve_lite_equalize(Z, adata.obs['batch'].values)\n      adata.obsm['X_emb'] = Zc.astype(np.float32)\n\n      # Build neighbors on X_emb with scanpy (k=50, euclidean); ensures CSR outputs\n      ad_tmp = ad.AnnData(X=Zc, obs=adata.obs.copy())\n      sc.pp.neighbors(ad_tmp, n_neighbors=50, use_rep=None, metric='euclidean')\n\
    \      # Copy back, cast to float64 for evaluator stability\n      C = ad_tmp.obsp['connectivities'].tocsr().astype(np.float64)\n      D = ad_tmp.obsp['distances'].tocsr().astype(np.float64)\n      adata.obsp['connectivities'] = C\n      adata.obsp['distances'] = D\n      # neighbors meta\n      adata.uns['neighbors'] = {\n          'connectivities_key': 'connectivities',\n          'distances_key': 'distances',\n          'params': {'n_neighbors': 50, 'method': 'scanpy.neighbors', 'metric': 'euclidean'}\n      }\n      return adata\n```"
thinking_content: "**Evaluating PCR results**\n\nI'm noticing a contradiction with the PCR values—earlier, the minimal pipeline showed a PCR of 1.000, which I think refers to Principal Component Regression. Yet, in open problems, normalized PCR was 1, but now it’s showing 0.000. It seems duplicates might be causing issues. My hypothesis suggests that the return of connectivities and distances could be overshadowing the PCR calculation. I'm pondering if our embedding is too scaled and wondering why we're getting a PCR of 0 despite efforts to improve mixing.**Investigating PCR and scaling issues**\n\nI’m considering whether our code mistakenly sets the shape of obsm['X_emb'] as 20k x 60. Since PCR relies on integrated embeddings with preserved high variance across cell types, a score of 0.0 suggests a significant issue. Syntellect getting 1.000 signals something's off with our function. My 'tmp' AnnData uses a sparse format, and it seems sc.pp.scale might expect dense data. I'm not sure about\
  \ the implications of using zero_center=False on sparse data. It feels like something needs adjustment in our process for the PCR score.**Exploring normalized PCR implications**\n\nI’m wondering if the normalized PCR of 0 indicates that our raw PCR is the worst compared to the baseline. It shows that earlier results had a normalized PCR of 0.0 just for GraphFWPCA-only. That could be an artifact due to a mismatch with neighbors. Syntellect achieved a PCR of 1.0, which makes me question our embedding differences. Their method likely used plain PCA, while we used an HVG mask. This could lead to inconsistencies between our pipeline and theirs.**Considering submission strategies**\n\nI’m noticing another difference after building kNN—this might degrade our metrics. I’m not quite sure if PCR is calculated using graph distances too. Given time constraints, it seems easiest to submit an embedding-only scaled PBVE method, meaning I won’t return obsp matrices. I’m thinking of proposing a new submission\
  \ titled 'PBVE-lite + Scaled PCA60—embedding only.' We could also offer a variant using scanpy.pp.neighbors to replicate Syntellect’s approach. But, we can compute kNN from the embedding instead, which might improve iLISI.**Planning submission strategies**\n\nIt seems we're allowed to go ahead, but the evaluation expects obsp keys for 'connectivities' and 'distances.' If we provide just the embedding without the graph, metrics may default to their own neighbor calculations. If I run sc.pp.neighbors to match Syntellect’s umap connectivities, we might see similar results. Fathom noted a replication improvement, so for our scaled PBVE, aiming for around 0.74 seems reasonable. \n\nI’ll craft two code variants: one for embedding-only and another that computes neighbors for connectivities and distances. We'll submit both while staying concise and logging memory plan updates."
