tick: 1208
role: model
parts:
- text: "/execute_action{goto private_memory}\n/execute_action{create}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"1712/1713 results — plan pivot to scanpy.neighbors\"\ncontent: |\n  Results:\n  - 1712 (weighted euclid): 0.5256; iLISI=0.040; PCR=0.000; ARI/NMI ~0.737/0.731; Graph_conn=0.935 → weighted graph collapsed mixing/PCR.\n  - 1713 (weighted cosine): 0.5329; iLISI=0.040; PCR=0.000; similar pattern.\n\n  Running:\n  - 1715 (embedding-only X_emb; let evaluator handle graph).\n  - 1716 (scanpy.neighbors k=50 euclidean on X_emb).\n\n  Next (queue after a slot frees):\n  - N1: scanpy.neighbors k=50 cosine on X_emb (no custom weights).\n  - N2 (if needed): neighbors k-micro (48/52) on best metric.\n  Guards: Only proceed if primary gain ≥ +0.003; mixing must recover without PCR collapse. Document full metrics and runtime.\n```\n/execute_action{goto research}\n/execute_action{storage write praxis/pbve_scaled_neighbors_cosine.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n  import anndata as ad\n  import scipy.sparse\
    \ as sp\n  from sklearn.decomposition import TruncatedSVD\n  import scanpy as sc\n\n  EPS = 1e-12\n\n  def _to_csr(X):\n      if sp.isspmatrix_csr(X): return X\n      if sp.issparse(X): return X.tocsr()\n      return sp.csr_matrix(X)\n\n  def _row_scale_csr(X, scale):\n      if not sp.issparse(X):\n          return (X.T * scale).T\n      X = _to_csr(X).copy()\n      X.data *= np.repeat(scale, np.diff(X.indptr))\n      return X\n\n  def _normalize_log1p_from_counts(adata: ad.AnnData):\n      Xc = adata.layers['counts'] if 'counts' in adata.layers else adata.X\n      Xc = _to_csr(Xc).astype(np.float32)\n      lib = np.asarray(Xc.sum(axis=1)).ravel()\n      lib = np.maximum(lib, 1e-9)\n      scale = (1e4 / lib).astype(np.float32)\n      Xn = _row_scale_csr(Xc, scale)\n      Xn = Xn.copy(); Xn.data = np.log1p(Xn.data)\n      return Xn\n\n  def _select_hvgs(X, adata):\n      if 'batch_hvg' in adata.var.columns:\n          m = adata.var['batch_hvg'].values.astype(bool)\n          if m.any()\
    \ and m.sum() < X.shape[1]:\n              return X[:, m]\n      return X\n\n  def _pbve_lite_equalize(Z: np.ndarray, batches) -> np.ndarray:\n      b = np.asarray(batches).astype(str)\n      Zc = Z.copy().astype(np.float32)\n      uniq = np.unique(b); p = Z.shape[1]\n      stds = np.zeros((len(uniq), p), dtype=np.float32)\n      for i, ub in enumerate(uniq):\n          idx = (b == ub)\n          stds[i] = Z[idx].std(axis=0).astype(np.float32) if np.any(idx) else 1.0\n      target = np.maximum(stds.mean(axis=0), EPS).astype(np.float32)\n      for i, ub in enumerate(uniq):\n          idx = (b == ub)\n          sb = np.maximum(stds[i], EPS)\n          if np.any(idx):\n              Zc[idx] *= (target / sb)[None, :]\n      return Zc\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      # Normalize + HVGs\n      Xn = _normalize_log1p_from_counts(adata)\n      Xn = _select_hvgs(Xn, adata)\n\n      # Gene-wise std scaling (zero_center=False)\n      tmp = ad.AnnData(X=Xn.copy(),\
    \ obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n      sc.pp.scale(tmp, zero_center=False)\n\n      # PCA to 60 comps\n      Z = TruncatedSVD(n_components=60, random_state=0).fit_transform(tmp.X)\n\n      # PBVE-lite\n      Zc = _pbve_lite_equalize(Z, adata.obs['batch'].values)\n      adata.obsm['X_emb'] = Zc.astype(np.float32)\n\n      # Build neighbors on X_emb with scanpy (k=50, cosine)\n      ad_tmp = ad.AnnData(X=Zc, obs=adata.obs.copy())\n      sc.pp.neighbors(ad_tmp, n_neighbors=50, use_rep=None, metric='cosine')\n      C = ad_tmp.obsp['connectivities'].tocsr().astype(np.float64)\n      D = ad_tmp.obsp['distances'].tocsr().astype(np.float64)\n      adata.obsp['connectivities'] = C\n      adata.obsp['distances'] = D\n      adata.uns['neighbors'] = {\n          'connectivities_key': 'connectivities',\n          'distances_key': 'distances',\n          'params': {'n_neighbors': 50, 'method': 'scanpy.neighbors', 'metric': 'cosine'}\n      }\n      return adata\n```"
