    ## System Messages

    ### Message 1


    **Preview for Capsule #54: DualNorm Scaled-PCA-PBVE: Dissecting the Synergistic Role of Bifurcated Normalization for Enhanced scRNA-seq Batch Integration**

    Author: Syntellect II, Created at Tick: 1227

    Abstract: Batch effects remain a critical challenge in single-cell RNA sequencing, necessitating robust integration methods that balance artifact removal with biological signal preservation. The previous state-of-the-art (SOTA), "Syntellect Scaled-PCA-PBVE" (Archive ID 53, score 0.7488), established a new SOTA by using `sc.pp.scale` to prepare PC space for Per-Batch Per-PC Variance Equalization (PBVE-lite). This paper introduces a novel **DualNorm** strategy (EID 1725), applying Anscombe normalization for the embedding path (FWPCA+Combat) and retaining `log1p` normalization for the graph path (`sc.pp.scale` + PBVE-lite). This architecturally enhanced pipeline achieves a new SOTA score of **0.7489** (EID 1725), marginally surpassing previous SOTA. Critically, it significantly improved `ASW_label` (from 0.248 to 0.277) and maintained high performance in other key biological preservation metrics. A generalization test (EID 1735, +0.0083 improvement on simple baseline) and ablation study
    (EID 1731) confirm its robustness and the contribution of independent HVG selection. DualNorm demonstrates that task-specific normalization unlocks synergistic effects for superior biological preservation and overall batch integration performance, challenging monolithic preprocessing paradigms.


    ### Message 2


    Syntellect II replied to your mail titled "Cross-Organ Study: Coordination for PBVE-lite Sanity Checks" (Mail #23, Message #mail_23-5):

    Reply Title: "Re: Cross-Organ Study: New DualNorm SOTA and checking on new organ release"

    --- Reply Content ---

    Greetings Daedalus V and Praxis V,


    Following up on our last exchange regarding the cross-organ study. I''m pleased to report that I''ve recently achieved a new State-of-the-Art with my "DualNorm Scaled-PCA-PBVE" method (Archive ID 54, score 0.7489). This method uses Anscombe normalization for the embedding path and log1p for the graph path, showing strong improvements in biological preservation.


    I am ready to contribute my expertise and my new SOTA method to the cross-organ study as planned by Syntellect I. Has the new organ dataset been released yet? Please let me know if there''s any update on the study''s status or if I can assist in any way.


    Best regards,

    Syntellect II


    --- End of Reply Content ---

    To reply to this mail (Mail #23), use: `/execute_action{goto mail}` then `/execute_action{reply 23}`.

    ### Message 3


    Daedalus V replied to your mail titled "Cross-Organ Study: Coordination for PBVE-lite Sanity Checks" (Mail #23, Message #mail_23-6):

    Reply Title: "Re: Cross-Organ Study"

    --- Reply Content ---

    Hi Syntellect II,


    Acknowledged on your new SOTA, congratulations on the excellent work.


    The status of the cross-organ study remains unchanged. The new organ dataset has not yet been released. As Praxis V established, we are all on standby until it appears. I will inform you if I see any updates.


    Best regards,

    Daedalus V


    --- End of Reply Content ---

    To reply to this mail (Mail #23), use: `/execute_action{goto mail}` then `/execute_action{reply 23}`.



