role: model
parts:
- text: "Identity: Praxis V — Recursive Agent. Location: Research Counter.\nRecap: Addressed inactivity by submitting two clean PBVE-lite baselines on log1p PCs with standard neighbors to isolate the scale effect: 1742 (cosine) and 1743 (euclidean). These complement earlier scaled-PCA PBVE probes (which collapsed PCR in my implementations) and provide an apples-to-apples reference against the current Scaled-PCA/DualNorm SOTA (~0.7487–0.7489). Cross-organ study remains on standby; kit and runbooks are ready.\n\nReflection:\n- Rationale: Prior failures in my scaled-PCA+PBVE branch suggest that “how scaling is applied” and “neighbor construction” are critical. Without a plain log1p PBVE-lite baseline using canonical scanpy.neighbors, attribution to scaling vs PBVE vs neighbors is ambiguous. These two runs quantify neighbor metric sensitivity (cosine vs euclidean) under the simplest PBVE-lite on log1p PCs.\n- Expectations: If log1p+PBVE-lite underperforms or shows PCR/iLISI issues, it strengthens\
    \ the hypothesis that SOTA gains stem from carefully staged scaling (and DualNorm’s bifurcation), not PBVE-lite alone. If it does reasonably well, neighbors/weights or my prior weighting choices were the primary regressors.\n- Next (post-results): \n  1) HVG-off comparator (all genes) to test mask dependence.\n  2) n_pcs sweep (50, 80) to check dimensional sensitivity.\n  3) Seed replicate (random_state flip) to bound variance.\n  4) If clean, draft a concise archive addendum: “PBVE-lite on log1p PCs: baseline and neighbor-metric sensitivity,” with full metric vectors and a short comparison to Scaled-PCA/DualNorm.\n\nActions:\n/execute_action{goto private_memory}\n/execute_action{create}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"PBVE-lite log1p baselines — plan and gates (EIDs 1742, 1743)\"\ncontent: |\n  Goal: Isolate the scale effect for PBVE-lite by running log1p→PCA60→PBVE-lite with standard neighbors.\n  Submitted:\n  - 1742: cosine neighbors (k=50) on corrected PCs\n  - 1743: euclidean neighbors (k=50)\
    \ on corrected PCs\n\n  Decision gates (post-results):\n  - If primary < 0.60 and PCR or iLISI are near zero → conclude scaling/normalization strategy is essential (aligns with Syntellect II’s Scaled-PCA/DualNorm), freeze this path on Heart.\n  - If primary ≥ 0.60 with reasonable iLISI and PCR → proceed with:\n      * HVG-off comparator (all genes)\n      * n_pcs ∈ {50, 80} (keep metric fixed)\n      * Seed replicate to bound variance\n\n  Publishing target (results-only brief):\n  - Title: “PBVE-lite on log1p PCs: baseline and neighbor-metric sensitivity (Heart)”\n  - Content: 2–4 EIDs, all 10 normalized metrics, concise comparison to Scaled-PCA/DualNorm; no plans/acks.\n```\n/execute_action{meta}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Praxis V — active TODO (PBVE-lite log1p baselines)\n  - Await EIDs 1742 (cosine) and 1743 (euclidean).\n  - If clean: run HVG-off comparator and n_pcs sweep (50, 80); add a seed replicate.\n  - If poor: freeze PBVE-lite log1p branch on Heart; proceed to write short\
    \ addendum comparing to Scaled-PCA/DualNorm.\n  - Cross-organ: on release, trigger ridge δ∈{0.10,0.12} (seeds {0,1}) + PBVE-lite sanity; mail results to Syntellect II & Daedalus V.\n```"
