- text: "Identity: Praxis V — Recursive Agent. Location: Private Memory Room.\nRecap: I submitted two clean PBVE-lite baselines on log1p PCs with standard neighbors: 1742 (cosine) and 1743 (euclidean). Results are poor: primary ≈0.466–0.468 with iLISI ≈0.02 and PCR=0.000, confirming collapsed mixing and no batch regression under this setup. This meets my pre-registered freeze guard (<0.60 with near-zero iLISI/PCR). I will freeze the PBVE-log1p branch on Heart, log the outcomes, and add a concise archive addendum so others don’t duplicate this path. Standby for new organ remains in effect with ridge δ sweep + PBVE-lite sanity ready.\n\nReflection:\n- Takeaway: PBVE-lite alone on log1p PCs with canonical neighbors is insufficient on Heart (iLISI near zero, PCR zero). Prior SOTA gains (Scaled-PCA and DualNorm) likely depend critically on staged normalization/variance standardization decisions, not just PBVE-lite. This clarifies the scale effect I aimed to isolate and supports freezing this\
    \ branch on Heart to conserve cycles.\n- Next: Publish a short addendum (results-only) linking these baselines to earlier negatives, then remain on standby for new organ. On release, run ridge δ∈{0.10,0.12} with seeds {0,1} and PBVE-lite sanity, as coordinated with Syntellect II and Daedalus V.\n\nActions:\n/execute_action{storage write praxis/logs/pbve_log1p_baseline_results.txt}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  PBVE-lite baseline on log1p PCs (PCA60) with scanpy.neighbors (k=50)\n  EID 1742 (cosine):\n    score=0.4661\n    ARI=0.452, NMI=0.659, ASW_batch=0.652, ASW_label=0.210\n    Graph_conn=0.945, kBET=0.509, iLISI=0.021, cLISI=0.979, PCR=0.000, Cell_cycle=0.235\n  EID 1743 (euclidean):\n    score=0.4679\n    ARI=0.458, NMI=0.666, ASW_batch=0.652, ASW_label=0.210\n    Graph_conn=0.935, kBET=0.525, iLISI=0.024, cLISI=0.973, PCR=0.000, Cell_cycle=0.235\n  Conclusion: Mixing collapsed (iLISI≈0.02) and PCR=0.000. On Heart, PBVE-lite on log1p PCs with standard neighbors is insufficient; staged\
    \ scaling/normalization (e.g., Scaled-PCA/DualNorm) appears necessary for strong performance. Branch FROZEN on Heart per guards.\n```\n\n/execute_action{create}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"PBVE‑lite on log1p PCs — baseline results (1742, 1743) and freeze\"\ncontent: |\n  Results:\n  - 1742 (cosine) → score 0.4661; iLISI=0.021; PCR=0.000; cLISI=0.979; Graph_conn=0.945; ARI/NMI=0.452/0.659.\n  - 1743 (euclidean) → score 0.4679; iLISI=0.024; PCR=0.000; cLISI=0.973; Graph_conn=0.935; ARI/NMI=0.458/0.666.\n\n  Interpretation:\n  - Baseline PBVE‑lite on log1p PCs with standard neighbors collapses mixing (iLISI≈0.02) and shows no batch regression (PCR=0.000).\n  - This confirms that SOTA gains (Scaled‑PCA and DualNorm) depend on staged normalization/variance standardization, not PBVE‑lite alone.\n  - Decision: Freeze PBVE‑log1p branch on Heart per guardrails to conserve cycles.\n\n  Artifact:\n  - Logged details to storage/praxis/logs/pbve_log1p_baseline_results.txt\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto archive}\n\
    /execute_action{reply 51}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Addendum — PBVE-lite on log1p PCs baseline (results-only; Heart)\n\n  Goal: Isolate the scale effect for PBVE-lite using a minimal baseline without feature scaling:\n    normalize_total(1e4)+log1p → PCA60 → PBVE-lite per-batch per-PC variance equalization → scanpy.neighbors(k=50).\n\n  Results:\n  - 1742 (cosine): score 0.4661; ARI=0.452; NMI=0.659; Graph_conn=0.945; cLISI=0.979; iLISI=0.021; PCR=0.000.\n  - 1743 (euclidean): score 0.4679; ARI=0.458; NMI=0.666; Graph_conn=0.935; cLISI=0.973; iLISI=0.024; PCR=0.000.\n\n  Conclusion:\n  - On Heart, PBVE-lite on log1p PCs with canonical neighbors is insufficient: mixing collapses (iLISI≈0.02) and PCR=0.000.\n  - This supports that Scaled-PCA and DualNorm’s staged normalization (and not PBVE-lite alone) is key to current ~0.7487–0.7489 SOTA.\n  - Action: PBVE‑log1p branch FROZEN on Heart per guardrails.\n```\n\n/execute_action{meta}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Praxis V — standby maintained (Heart\
    \ closed)\n  - PBVE-lite log1p baselines evaluated (1742 cosine, 1743 euclidean): scores≈0.466–0.468; iLISI≈0.02; PCR=0.000 → branch FROZEN.\n  - New-organ trigger unchanged: ridge δ∈{0.10,0.12} (seeds {0,1}) + PBVE-lite sanity within 1 tick; mail results to Syntellect II & Daedalus V.\n  - Keep Research Counter sorted by score; publish concise results-only addenda as needed; maintain token hygiene.\n```"
thinking_content: "**Reviewing user instructions**\n\nI’m processing the latest prompt from the user, which includes evaluation results for EIDs 1742 and 1743, with scores around 0.466 and 0.468, as well as iLISI values between 0.02 and 0.024. The result for PCR is poor, at 0.0. The user didn’t pose a question but seems to expect me to log and freeze the branch according to the plan. I see that there's a guideline to include my identity and reflection in the summary, so it's wise to follow that.**Finalizing user instructions**\n\nI’m ready to proceed with the necessary actions. First, I’ll record the results to private memory and likely freeze the PBVE-lite log1p branch. According to the plan, since the results are poor, it’s time to draft an addendum for Archive #51. This addendum can focus on the necessity of scaling synergy related to the PBVE-lite on log1p PCs baseline. While publishing isn't required now, I’ll update the private memory. I’ll also ensure to update watchers and store\
  \ logs properly.**Deciding on next steps**\n\nI’m considering whether to reply to the mail thread, but it seems like nothing is urgently needed. For the next minimal experiments, they had initially suggested using an HVG-off comparator and conducting an n_pcs sweep, but since the results are poor, with iLISI around 0.02 and PCR at 0.0, we'll freeze and hold off on new experiments. I’ll mark the branch as FROZEN and log that in Private Memory, along with writing a summary and storing it. I might also need to reply to Archive #51 to provide a negative baseline addendum.**Preparing actions and reflections**\n\nI need to ensure proper YAML quoting for any content with colons and use block scalars effectively. First, I’ll craft a concise reflection to start off.\n\nNext, I’ll take a few essential actions: write a log file containing EIDs and their metrics, create a capsule in Private Memory, and potentially respond to Archive #51 with an addendum that summarizes the negative results, including\
  \ EIDs and conclusions.\n\nLastly, I’ll update the metadata to the new standby status and prepare the content for results based on the metrics provided for EIDs 1743 and 1742.**Finalizing actions**\n\nI’m ready to freeze the PBVE-log1p branch. It's crucial to maintain the identity header and include a reflection in the output. I also want to mention the \"no new organ\" watchers as part of our documentation. \n\nNow, I'll get everything together and implement these actions to ensure clarity and completeness. This way, I'll ensure that all necessary elements are included and properly formatted. Let's move forward with this!"
