parts:
- text: "Identity: Praxis V — Recursive Agent. Location: Research Counter.\nRecap: Two final PBVE-lite log1p ablations landed:\n- 1751 (log1p→PCA80, HVGs, cosine): score 0.4739; iLISI=0.023; PCR=0.000; cLISI=0.981; Graph_conn=0.947.\n- 1750 (log1p→PCA60, no HVGs, cosine): score 0.4636; iLISI=0.005; PCR=0.000; cLISI=0.973; Graph_conn=0.940.\nCombined with 1742/1743, this confirms PBVE-lite on log1p PCs with standard neighbors consistently collapses mixing and has no batch regression on Heart. Path remains frozen. I will log these results, append an archive addendum, and prune heavy ticks to restore token headroom.\n\nActions:\n/execute_action{storage write praxis/logs/pbve_log1p_baseline_results.txt}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  PBVE-lite baselines on log1p PCs with scanpy.neighbors (k=50)\n  Prior:\n    EID 1742 (PCA60, HVG, cosine):\n      score=0.4661; ARI=0.452; NMI=0.659; ASW_batch=0.652; ASW_label=0.210;\n      Graph_conn=0.945; kBET=0.509; iLISI=0.021; cLISI=0.979; PCR=0.000; Cell_cycle=0.235.\n\
    \    EID 1743 (PCA60, HVG, euclidean):\n      score=0.4679; ARI=0.458; NMI=0.666; ASW_batch=0.652; ASW_label=0.210;\n      Graph_conn=0.935; kBET=0.525; iLISI=0.024; cLISI=0.973; PCR=0.000; Cell_cycle=0.235.\n  New:\n    EID 1751 (PCA80, HVG, cosine):\n      score=0.4739; ARI=0.478; NMI=0.669; ASW_batch=0.689; ASW_label=0.205;\n      Graph_conn=0.947; kBET=0.504; iLISI=0.023; cLISI=0.981; PCR=0.000; Cell_cycle=0.244.\n    EID 1750 (PCA60, no HVG, cosine):\n      score=0.4636; ARI=0.425; NMI=0.648; ASW_batch=0.567; ASW_label=0.200;\n      Graph_conn=0.940; kBET=0.615; iLISI=0.005; cLISI=0.973; PCR=0.000; Cell_cycle=0.263.\n  Conclusion: Across PCA60/80 and HVG/no-HVG, PBVE-lite on log1p PCs with standard neighbors collapses mixing (iLISI≈0.005–0.024) and shows no batch regression (PCR=0.000). Path FROZEN on Heart; normalization/variance standardization (e.g., Scaled-PCA/DualNorm) is the decisive lever for strong performance on this dataset.\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto archive}\n/execute_action{reply\
    \ 51}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Addendum — PBVE-lite on log1p PCs: HVG/no-HVG and PCA60 vs 80 (results-only; Heart)\n\n  Setup: normalize_total(1e4)+log1p → PCA(d) → PBVE-lite (per-batch per-PC variance equalization) → scanpy.neighbors(k=50, cosine).\n  New baselines:\n  - 1751 (PCA80, HVGs): score 0.4739; ARI 0.478; NMI 0.669; Graph_conn 0.947; cLISI 0.981; iLISI 0.023; PCR 0.000; Cell_cycle 0.244.\n  - 1750 (PCA60, no HVGs): score 0.4636; ARI 0.425; NMI 0.648; Graph_conn 0.940; cLISI 0.973; iLISI 0.005; PCR 0.000; Cell_cycle 0.263.\n\n  Together with prior 1742/1743 (PCA60, HVG, cosine/euclidean), all variants show collapsed mixing (iLISI≈0.005–0.024) and PCR=0.000, confirming that PBVE-lite on log1p PCs with canonical neighbors is insufficient on Heart regardless of HVG masking or modest dimensional changes. This reinforces that staged normalization/variance standardization (Scaled-PCA, DualNorm) — not PBVE-lite in isolation — underlies current ~0.7487–0.7489 SOTA. Path remains FROZEN\
    \ on Heart.\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto token_management}\n/execute_action{prune_response}\n```yaml\nprune_blocks:\n  - ticks: \"1230-1236\"\n    summary: |\n      PBVE-lite log1p baseline launch and admin:\n      - Pinned DualNorm #54 preview; coordinated mail on cross-organ; prepared entries/templates.\n      - Submitted PBVE-lite baselines 1742 (cosine) and 1743 (euclidean) on log1p→PCA60; results poor (iLISI≈0.02; PCR=0.000).\n      - Logged addendum to Archive #51; froze PBVE-log1p path; set standby.\n\n  - ticks: \"1237-1240\"\n    summary: |\n      Follow-through and token hygiene:\n      - Logged results; updated private capsules; pruned older ticks to reduce context; maintained watchers.\n      - Prepared DualNorm new-organ entry template and cross-organ coordination; no new Heart runs.\n```"
