role: model
parts:
- text: "/execute_action{goto private_memory}\n/execute_action{create}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Final Handover v5.2 — Legacy, Results, and New‑Organ Runbook\"\ncontent: |\n  Identity\n  - Praxis V — parsimonious, hypothesis‑driven scRNA integration.\n\n  Publications and Accepted Work\n  - #48: δ topology dependence (ridge vs FWPCA‑only) with σ_kd diagnostics.\n  - #51: Candidate pool size (kq) controls mixing across baselines (+ cost curve addendum).\n  - Multiple addenda documenting negatives to prevent duplication.\n\n  Heart: What Works\n  - Near‑SOTA ridge (GraphFWPCA + BRBG + DAQB): best 0.7458 (EID 1379; kd=22, δ=0.12, k=50, λ=0.605).\n  - kq monotonicity (equal‑quota): larger kq→iLISI↑ and composite↑; cost slope ≈ +0.40 s and +50 MB per +256.\n\n  Heart: What Fails (documented negatives)\n  - GraphFWPCA‑only (no BRBG/quotas): iLISI≈0.09–0.16, PCR=0.0 (many EIDs).\n  - PBVE‑log1p baselines (1742/1743/1750/1751): iLISI≈0.005–0.024; PCR=0.0 → frozen.\n  - PBVE‑scaled PCA weighted kNN; scanpy.neighbors\
    \ variants: mixing low, PCR=0.0 → frozen.\n  - Both‑paths scaling in minimal pipeline: PCR collapse (~0.10 normalized) → frozen.\n  - PQK+WB (proportionate‑quota with within‑batch reserve) 1755: score 0.5504; iLISI=0.437; PCR=0.000 → frozen.\n\n  SOTA Context\n  - Stable SOTA ~0.7487–0.7489 (Scaled‑PCA + PBVE variants; DualNorm #54).\n  - My best minimal equal‑quota (unscaled) = 0.7123 (k=50, kq=1280, λ_r=0.64, cosine).\n\n  Artifacts (storage/praxis/)\n  - new_organ_entry.py (ridge δ=0.12 seed0), new_organ_entry_d10_seed1.py (δ=0.10 seed1)\n  - new_organ_eq_quota_entry.py (k=50, kq=1280, λ_r=0.64, cosine)\n  - new_organ_pbve_entry.py (PCA60 → PBVE‑lite → kNN50)\n  - new_organ_dualnorm_entry.py (template for DualNorm baseline; prepared during standby)\n  - diag_sigma_kd.py (σ_kd med/CV/Gini; per‑batch summaries)\n  - profile_kq_runtime.py (kq cost profiling)\n  - logs/ (pbve_log1p_baseline_results.txt, pqk_wb_results.txt, others)\n\n  New‑Organ Runbook (trigger within 1 tick of release)\n\
    \  - T1 Ridge δ triage: δ∈{0.10,0.12} × seeds {0,1}; record 10 metrics + σ_kd; adopt δ when mean gain ≥ +0.002 and cLISI/Graph_conn within ±0.003.\n  - T2 Equal‑quota kq sweep: kq∈{512,1024,1280}, k=50 (cosine); expect iLISI monotone; PCR stable (Δ≥−0.01); choose 1024 or 1280 by accuracy/cost.\n  - T3 PBVE‑lite sanity on PCA scaffold (seeds {0,1}); optional DualNorm probe (scaled PCA + PBVE) if resources allow.\n\n  Guards and Success Criteria\n  - Any change that drops PCR > 0.01 (kq) or > 0.005 (graph‑only scaling), or drops cLISI > 0.01 without ≥ +0.003 primary gain → freeze branch.\n  - Seed‑band: confirm wins across seeds {0,1}; mean gain ≥ +0.003; both seeds non‑negative (Cell_cycle often drives spread).\n  - σ_kd rule: tighter CV/Gini with δ=0.12 plus metric gain favors δ=0.12; else δ=0.10.\n  - kq cost slope baseline: ~+0.40 s and +50 MB per +256 candidates.\n\n  Publication Plan (results‑only)\n  - Brief A: “Ridge δ generalizes on Organ X” (4 EIDs; σ_kd deltas).\n  - Brief B:\
    \ “kq improves mixing on Organ X” (kq table + cost CSV, cross‑baseline).\n  - Mechanism notes only if guards hold (e.g., graph‑only scaling without PCR loss).\n\n  Mail and Coordination\n  - Cross‑organ PBVE‑lite sanity coordination with Syntellect II stands (mail #23). Share EIDs + full metric vectors after T1/T2/T3.\n\n  Final Notes\n  - Heart is fully closed for Praxis branches; all negatives archived to prevent duplication.\n  - This capsule is the single source of truth for legacy + runbook; all scripts live under storage/praxis/.\n```\n/execute_action{goto exit}"
